[{"sha":"4eded02f527b90e663764cb5c194f881c4dfd1bc","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDRlZGVkMDJmNTI3YjkwZTY2Mzc2NGNiNWMxOTRmODgxYzRkZmQxYmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Felipe Coury","email":"felipe.coury@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T14:43:21Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T14:43:21Z"},"message":"[codex] fix compressed rollout fixture SessionMeta initialization (#25628)\n\n## Summary\n- initialize `parent_thread_id` in the compressed rollout test fixture's\n`SessionMeta`\n- restore rollout test compilation across Bazel test, clippy,\nrelease-build, and argument-comment-lint jobs\n\n## Root cause\nPR #25087 (`Read compressed rollouts and materialize before append`)\nadded `codex-rs/rollout/src/compression_tests.rs` in merge commit\n`a8a6071279b6f3112fcc5fc3fee69c48473d7149`. Its `write_rollout` fixture\nconstructs `SessionMeta` without the required `parent_thread_id` field,\ncausing `error[E0063]` when Bazel compiles `rollout-unit-tests-bin` on\n`main` and downstream PRs.\n\n## Validation\n- `UV_CACHE_DIR=/private/tmp/codex-uv-cache just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout` (`59` tests passed; bench smoke passed)\n- `git diff --check`\n- manually audited the touched Rust diff for positional literal argument\ncomments; the change adds no positional callsite\n\n## Local lint blocker\n- `just argument-comment-lint` could not reach source inspection locally\nbecause Bazel's LLVM dependency fails analysis:\n`compiler-rt/BUILD.bazel` glob `include/sanitizer/*.h` matched no files.","tree":{"sha":"20d96889544a2ac1a7d899b4f68c75666f9b714b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/20d96889544a2ac1a7d899b4f68c75666f9b714b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4eded02f527b90e663764cb5c194f881c4dfd1bc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHZqJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdiQQAJZCYH1AKl/50UTPoOI0THPx\nAHwCVKnbZcLuBfrfiHSJUhcJndPfnpD5PBM6Q0LVBIYYh3hweuRwzegDA3N11lVA\n2zHMOCzh3+ZCi3QuQ+GX8A5S1jng5OnWNHGSmdwUL60tNKhv2dyIbJlipjk7VsQ0\nBWU3PcCioeU7dlcAeJ7xjsZN1RNuz4l0a6kQXHcqT3lOsIWPeN9Qz0PmPvu+qO8R\njl9hImZWUq7RFNIY2o/SItP99MxA34efsVzupF+PT4Qu9iTVfJ3QJMXpJF4PPkTn\nklw/EN5Hf3m+AhFuVrvsUqvOwXxPkpCW4p351dKxC0hEY0oi+c+e8gSyItKOurFG\npElzVAld7UJh+50hnmsqyBxyW3xBi+ygtcbsEKc2wVMld1IqLYCYrtsxZN7UXal/\n0OQSH3pCkA6wW4btwNc6NWona5cpi+kgsWYj6aGLS9UZ0evr86kyUCllyGMZvGw+\nDgba1OlX+ceSS/o6gSNTPiIDoafJuWEXe4I8QAvOg2pjX95s3b1M0IYSHrsNBK5D\nDiR4L9elSg5+KF+oNspEmvtExpaaaEBKBDBy3WrX/ODA2Rfz3QaQl9+b0OZxlQBn\nYkUr32QnFPHitbuw93KsIXs/JwQAx+S8xoztDgGhPfsqCZtoRXC8fsSBheqnzE4+\nJ3I2G4tvXjMkkz6AgW2y\n=I3x5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 20d96889544a2ac1a7d899b4f68c75666f9b714b\nparent a8a6071279b6f3112fcc5fc3fee69c48473d7149\nauthor Felipe Coury <felipe.coury@openai.com> 1780325001 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780325001 +0200\n\n[codex] fix compressed rollout fixture SessionMeta initialization (#25628)\n\n## Summary\n- initialize `parent_thread_id` in the compressed rollout test fixture's\n`SessionMeta`\n- restore rollout test compilation across Bazel test, clippy,\nrelease-build, and argument-comment-lint jobs\n\n## Root cause\nPR #25087 (`Read compressed rollouts and materialize before append`)\nadded `codex-rs/rollout/src/compression_tests.rs` in merge commit\n`a8a6071279b6f3112fcc5fc3fee69c48473d7149`. Its `write_rollout` fixture\nconstructs `SessionMeta` without the required `parent_thread_id` field,\ncausing `error[E0063]` when Bazel compiles `rollout-unit-tests-bin` on\n`main` and downstream PRs.\n\n## Validation\n- `UV_CACHE_DIR=/private/tmp/codex-uv-cache just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout` (`59` tests passed; bench smoke passed)\n- `git diff --check`\n- manually audited the touched Rust diff for positional literal argument\ncomments; the change adds no positional callsite\n\n## Local lint blocker\n- `just argument-comment-lint` could not reach source inspection locally\nbecause Bazel's LLVM dependency fails analysis:\n`compiler-rt/BUILD.bazel` glob `include/sanitizer/*.h` matched no files.","verified_at":"2026-06-01T14:43:23Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4eded02f527b90e663764cb5c194f881c4dfd1bc","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4eded02f527b90e663764cb5c194f881c4dfd1bc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4eded02f527b90e663764cb5c194f881c4dfd1bc/comments","author":{"login":"fcoury-oai","id":272635208,"node_id":"U_kgDOEEAVSA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272635208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/fcoury-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a8a6071279b6f3112fcc5fc3fee69c48473d7149","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a8a6071279b6f3112fcc5fc3fee69c48473d7149","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a8a6071279b6f3112fcc5fc3fee69c48473d7149"}]},{"sha":"a8a6071279b6f3112fcc5fc3fee69c48473d7149","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGE4YTYwNzEyNzliNmYzMTEyZmNjNWZjM2ZlZTY5YzQ4NDczZDcxNDk","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif-oai","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T13:14:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T13:14:19Z"},"message":"Read compressed rollouts and materialize before append (#25087)\n\n## Why\n\nLocal rollout compression needs a cold `.jsonl.zst` representation\nwithout letting compressed physical paths leak into append-mode writers.\nThe unsafe case is resume or metadata update code successfully reading a\ncompressed rollout and then appending raw JSONL bytes to the zstd file.\n\nThis PR folds the former #25088 materialization slice into the\nread-support PR so the reader changes and append-safety invariant land\ntogether.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Teach rollout readers, discovery, listing, search, and ID lookup to\nunderstand compressed `.jsonl.zst` rollouts.\n- Keep `.jsonl` as the logical/stored rollout path while allowing read\npaths to open either plain or compressed storage.\n- Materialize compressed rollouts back to plain `.jsonl` before\nappend-mode writes, including resume and direct metadata append paths.\n- Preserve compressed-file permissions when materializing back to plain\nJSONL.\n- Refresh thread-store resolved rollout paths after compatibility\nmetadata writes so reconciliation follows the materialized file.\n- Avoid treating transient compression temp files as real rollout lookup\nresults.\n\n## Remaining Stack\n\n#25089 remains the separate worker PR. It is based directly on this PR\nand stays behind the disabled `local_thread_store_compression` feature\nflag.\n\nThe worker still has a broader coordination question: a resume or\nmetadata update can race with background compression while a plain file\nis being replaced by `.jsonl.zst`. This PR handles the read and\nmaterialize-before-append primitives; it does not make the worker\nproduction-ready.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-rollout`\n- `just test -p codex-thread-store`\n- `just fix -p codex-rollout`\n- `just fix -p codex-thread-store`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`","tree":{"sha":"7828264946399d169cc77f7eab67db3f18ad2543","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/7828264946399d169cc77f7eab67db3f18ad2543"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a8a6071279b6f3112fcc5fc3fee69c48473d7149","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHYWrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAu0sQAB6SUtuHB2zRINCQ93TOAHGL\nv7scn3TYj/fJCu0CVXR+j0rvEKDMB3BUsXssuJ6YztXR6GakRAVqvpqKyBlXVBCJ\nW6IqwLIA6UTyjjqvizNv9z2u/2AqcPaTZbWBlUrr7mU93qh2t7possR/Pu3uSX/F\nyINQ56oe9QFBruFmHTo92dLNUUrSkdI+xOgWCIJW3jfuSPoOZ4Uc3InqnOIOPaOe\nfl1tLWG3nyx+uoMONRmQ+s1W9aJKhjsLxQSpx6EfcnDTXC3yUXH1JF5MYqyz0UlV\ndDh8csx3zMqNJeqOR5+pVEPf6GizBhHda8p7nY5F+NKrVBBcslr6eZAxAFcrITKz\nzYflid1ro5IlRIbaNXJDlsg+e23Kxd6O7CeDiTJYsCDlX2gJQyV/XDTtaRgDiaqu\nDRU43r65Y/eJUGGkkdtwSEoyzJfuHPIVwfJO+WCT0X1qx7S/Df9ZmJk3n/VibPRg\nskzYl16lBA23XGO96ZlJNM9SGroHIN6rARwyjnkC8CP8cxnZwMUSXdVmdMYxIhJN\nk2owTV/EaQQQbUhbKhtnGsNDhN/mlmFylooSszKQfPe52UNGA33Uhui9q7GL+s/M\nefOaq+2xymmY5p5W32S0q1NgSUcUUl4Q8CynY9A1zYfrwxIWAzcAC4Eminz0MIgm\na3XIIOEPpffZrz5oqxdb\n=2oRM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7828264946399d169cc77f7eab67db3f18ad2543\nparent f27bbbd49c0e05e763a96cc7fa677499de32b8d8\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1780319659 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780319659 +0200\n\nRead compressed rollouts and materialize before append (#25087)\n\n## Why\n\nLocal rollout compression needs a cold `.jsonl.zst` representation\nwithout letting compressed physical paths leak into append-mode writers.\nThe unsafe case is resume or metadata update code successfully reading a\ncompressed rollout and then appending raw JSONL bytes to the zstd file.\n\nThis PR folds the former #25088 materialization slice into the\nread-support PR so the reader changes and append-safety invariant land\ntogether.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Teach rollout readers, discovery, listing, search, and ID lookup to\nunderstand compressed `.jsonl.zst` rollouts.\n- Keep `.jsonl` as the logical/stored rollout path while allowing read\npaths to open either plain or compressed storage.\n- Materialize compressed rollouts back to plain `.jsonl` before\nappend-mode writes, including resume and direct metadata append paths.\n- Preserve compressed-file permissions when materializing back to plain\nJSONL.\n- Refresh thread-store resolved rollout paths after compatibility\nmetadata writes so reconciliation follows the materialized file.\n- Avoid treating transient compression temp files as real rollout lookup\nresults.\n\n## Remaining Stack\n\n#25089 remains the separate worker PR. It is based directly on this PR\nand stays behind the disabled `local_thread_store_compression` feature\nflag.\n\nThe worker still has a broader coordination question: a resume or\nmetadata update can race with background compression while a plain file\nis being replaced by `.jsonl.zst`. This PR handles the read and\nmaterialize-before-append primitives; it does not make the worker\nproduction-ready.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-rollout`\n- `just test -p codex-thread-store`\n- `just fix -p codex-rollout`\n- `just fix -p codex-thread-store`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`","verified_at":"2026-06-01T13:14:19Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a8a6071279b6f3112fcc5fc3fee69c48473d7149","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a8a6071279b6f3112fcc5fc3fee69c48473d7149","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a8a6071279b6f3112fcc5fc3fee69c48473d7149/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f27bbbd49c0e05e763a96cc7fa677499de32b8d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f27bbbd49c0e05e763a96cc7fa677499de32b8d8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f27bbbd49c0e05e763a96cc7fa677499de32b8d8"}]},{"sha":"f27bbbd49c0e05e763a96cc7fa677499de32b8d8","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGYyN2JiYmQ0OWMwZTA1ZTc2M2E5NmNjN2ZhNjc3NDk5ZGUzMmI4ZDg","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif-oai","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T09:32:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T09:32:13Z"},"message":"Add goal extension GoalApi (#25096)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add an extension-owned `GoalApi` for thread goal get/set/clear\noperations\n- register live goal runtimes with the API from the goal extension\nbackend\n- cover the API and runtime-effect paths in goal extension tests\n\n## Stack\n\nFollow-up app-server wiring PR: #25108\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just fix -p codex-goal-extension`\n- `just test -p codex-goal-extension`","tree":{"sha":"162e4bc5f6ed1eb4339772721e3016daa91c6d14","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/162e4bc5f6ed1eb4339772721e3016daa91c6d14"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f27bbbd49c0e05e763a96cc7fa677499de32b8d8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHVGdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3b0QADjLTiAoOz2Ff93kEbEyj9Js\nyA2/uTQaHhDvLUD++F+K4fMWumWf8VEpbYO0/USeeCmpBlA4p0bq9PIBzBDxHtVw\nAZW70/sk783YKSsd8KEBnEOFSCszWIy8RovzV65Naciick+HnrWNf8dzlVZzmqxn\neQnkgmWeiXXIdpSI/cLE/77PQLoNPm+hjP3EeFKJInyiNT+ivDRTXIey9i8eK5XA\n0uWbM3E6H2OYuQRny8++9tVl55REcucLxKxds4GDHvx3GI/iTOWjBEHFUWVfCqmW\nieQinmy/uHVmb03wc7clcjqquerDrD2yK4IpZvxPTlsmTPkhvZzXC2sOtXLm1E/5\ns9e4vYjwIwmn1hBhPYwWxJWA6zPjMM/5W1lTyXzp1V3SVZXogvQIrJ+fEgxcbQuK\nXO3zJOXEafJF7HJ8blH/F0ikBIiKPX5TMNTDmorc4CqqgsRBW3HmlqSFepObi3jM\nb64RB5nksqRy2P/kRLJ80fIbkLNUVzDJvFQQMh2MfpTxtBEB2G2ECKv8eyUqXcr8\nyra77Irw7E86L/z3s4sKfbie2XtvYDeRkUBWjHZCXmZG1VBliKcVY4rljBxHSfOO\nrN9XoW+/Oc1s7TB2ng9SQfVhE6UTLW2wRENGlkagpmoJdApWEB5i8dumDmPuCDNa\nFjIIa+E6WwFXkcGghZ3J\n=slwB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 162e4bc5f6ed1eb4339772721e3016daa91c6d14\nparent 48c16b8bcbbba54201c3ea4ea3495acd1bd52c50\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1780306333 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780306333 +0200\n\nAdd goal extension GoalApi (#25096)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add an extension-owned `GoalApi` for thread goal get/set/clear\noperations\n- register live goal runtimes with the API from the goal extension\nbackend\n- cover the API and runtime-effect paths in goal extension tests\n\n## Stack\n\nFollow-up app-server wiring PR: #25108\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just fix -p codex-goal-extension`\n- `just test -p codex-goal-extension`","verified_at":"2026-06-01T09:32:13Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f27bbbd49c0e05e763a96cc7fa677499de32b8d8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f27bbbd49c0e05e763a96cc7fa677499de32b8d8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f27bbbd49c0e05e763a96cc7fa677499de32b8d8/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"48c16b8bcbbba54201c3ea4ea3495acd1bd52c50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/48c16b8bcbbba54201c3ea4ea3495acd1bd52c50","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/48c16b8bcbbba54201c3ea4ea3495acd1bd52c50"}]},{"sha":"48c16b8bcbbba54201c3ea4ea3495acd1bd52c50","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDQ4YzE2YjhiY2JiYmE1NDIwMWMzZWE0ZWEzNDk1YWNkMWJkNTJjNTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif-oai","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T09:06:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T09:06:38Z"},"message":"Remove Plan-mode gate from idle turn injection (#25577)\n\n## Why\n\n`try_start_turn_if_idle` is the core helper for starting injected input\nonly when the session is actually idle. It should stay focused on\ngeneric turn-lifecycle safety. The previous `ModeKind::Plan` guard mixed\ncaller policy into that helper: Plan mode may choose not to auto-start\nsome extension work, but that decision belongs at the extension or\ncaller boundary rather than in the session injection primitive.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Removed the `ModeKind::Plan` early return from\n`Session::try_start_turn_if_idle`.\n- Removed the now-unused `ModeKind` import from\n`core/src/session/inject.rs`.\n\n## Testing\n\nNot run locally.","tree":{"sha":"4d06f63509040835eccb38774ff2b59a16471b37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/4d06f63509040835eccb38774ff2b59a16471b37"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/48c16b8bcbbba54201c3ea4ea3495acd1bd52c50","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHUueCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuyQQAHER98n27Eam9y9VqjWeecIP\n3dOeBqFXINqS7bv1ZRCcZqe68VNethj0333ALiIGb6uN31lZyk5ER/sdzkQ65CPX\nRPnRvmsK37PBNLPmDYqJ/ZqdXyR6PsMu3hzLjFVrFZ+eMn1sNgep3VSMaXWuPECD\nXHQ+tdhxYqdScWFGBzkqlK2Rkv+OT1ngcq7xtmDE5AzPPpihHvotf6DjV6SdrKKX\nojzjj2kM5jarK7lXpMgECoU0GSmwn15fRsW2phuG8gMwXxgPfFCXyj38t5pBgIRX\nM+jMCqet+TH49GWEDNP9qAJ00sT/BkBII1LgnHLVCEJOyJ0alNUxg4SsB/P3mEAl\nJVjT4rmv9giV4cnb0D0TwRikSwbgtfHigMYtVPruk6FVoKfl2wZJrizMLG6WihvP\nTpyxG2NinIsPR02KRm27bjtCt+ceOJxxxXRLq+m3EOWF9RS4jKDVhFksMlB2rQX2\nt00CO9acCArefWaJLinGLMlZIev/keWnJM7sgd2mMg2N1wXIn9RcHHiV59vTKOSg\njCwks1F2MTS7cNRyz64C/m0IMFI6BR1Nt4lORBa8slEUyu1hL66VW3yqh3EEJnmZ\nq3mbZkefKzLZoQmyyFRFenjpa7NB6CO4oMHLB72B6H6tywJcClYpdhhsAWZnh/sb\nC0syK1hwxVkdx2lwiYoT\n=q2sR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4d06f63509040835eccb38774ff2b59a16471b37\nparent c875bc8a333eb492b104d8c9abb2bf4cbde195b7\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1780304798 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780304798 +0200\n\nRemove Plan-mode gate from idle turn injection (#25577)\n\n## Why\n\n`try_start_turn_if_idle` is the core helper for starting injected input\nonly when the session is actually idle. It should stay focused on\ngeneric turn-lifecycle safety. The previous `ModeKind::Plan` guard mixed\ncaller policy into that helper: Plan mode may choose not to auto-start\nsome extension work, but that decision belongs at the extension or\ncaller boundary rather than in the session injection primitive.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Removed the `ModeKind::Plan` early return from\n`Session::try_start_turn_if_idle`.\n- Removed the now-unused `ModeKind` import from\n`core/src/session/inject.rs`.\n\n## Testing\n\nNot run locally.","verified_at":"2026-06-01T09:06:38Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/48c16b8bcbbba54201c3ea4ea3495acd1bd52c50","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/48c16b8bcbbba54201c3ea4ea3495acd1bd52c50","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/48c16b8bcbbba54201c3ea4ea3495acd1bd52c50/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c875bc8a333eb492b104d8c9abb2bf4cbde195b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c875bc8a333eb492b104d8c9abb2bf4cbde195b7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c875bc8a333eb492b104d8c9abb2bf4cbde195b7"}]},{"sha":"c875bc8a333eb492b104d8c9abb2bf4cbde195b7","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGM4NzViYzhhMzMzZWI0OTJiMTA0ZDhjOWFiYjJiZjRjYmRlMTk1Yjc","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif-oai","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T08:55:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T08:55:14Z"},"message":"Use templates for goal steering prompts (#25576)\n\n## Why\n\nGoal steering prompts have grown into long inline Rust strings, which\nmakes the authored prompt text hard to review and easy to damage while\nchanging the surrounding plumbing. Moving those prompts into embedded\nMarkdown templates keeps the policy text in the shape reviewers actually\nread, while preserving the existing runtime substitution and objective\nescaping behavior.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added `ext/goal/templates/goals/continuation.md`, `budget_limit.md`,\nand `objective_updated.md` for the three goal steering prompts.\n- Updated `ext/goal/src/steering.rs` to parse those embedded templates\nonce with `codex-utils-template` and render the existing goal values\ninto them.\n- Kept user objectives XML-escaped before rendering and converted budget\ncounters into template variables.\n- Added the template directory to `ext/goal/BUILD.bazel` `compile_data`\nso Bazel has the same embedded prompt inputs as Cargo.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Not run locally.","tree":{"sha":"dd4c04817030aa2e557b1d06c10b98eccac24e67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/dd4c04817030aa2e557b1d06c10b98eccac24e67"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c875bc8a333eb492b104d8c9abb2bf4cbde195b7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHUjyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1joQACgXeh25Q/b+12h0c3Gc9pLr\noa7A1SwGYLgy+7+ymsjWJrqcmmpVveAkcT+nzncT5kPp129aILZ03FtmYMyVJDbE\npWy1kuV1D5kALpPiJyked9frXrzjoW5fMALo9Lo73qJEpdqsbbDE0Imi2rv1qk/b\ntRbPVy5Rj3wDp1OSNtN+4dQHmoC6HhqRrIIUxZs1JaX0aS0pIbPZtefQrHisW+LE\nTF9UDIJKy5T8RPYnwxqCoHwdqjVm8C8ScgltEVG+fw3HA6aEG39VkM65lpk1PZa7\nzOHDo3Vx51qd/R2PlqoZp2P7Dv/RZUTmAdHAkQaDn/16sluOINwVpXpZLasbzcA1\nN/kdBkVOEdOU52CDT3FomzmX3z8pfb5hxNNMa+VYnVJ1qOEMCE0Oka0JXrZRNETk\n3H3OZP/SylcFWAMB/puLrIyqpcmoGCvfPHw0VWQMJj5hLPtyyoScZv3Ansam6N3C\nP5diCo0DbugzxcLXfoQT6DYNAZGXgcK2Ymk1y1ytWAgZegdTV/1ev9ugr4bqxMi1\nwaqAPjg9vYRmc5kGnA6qz0XX1uhFN5q5jLh80RuWh3BiN2aaWUfhlihKWehYJmnS\nScy5OzBK6FBdidJkvS+rAkGmgpoqE2t4enfuwnAKWSX6rk3Ok8eArN+UJKbcaZKm\n8Tjex2QQu24ZQpRMndSy\n=5im2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree dd4c04817030aa2e557b1d06c10b98eccac24e67\nparent f1b1b64005cd477dd4821dfac8bc72097297ee96\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1780304114 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780304114 +0200\n\nUse templates for goal steering prompts (#25576)\n\n## Why\n\nGoal steering prompts have grown into long inline Rust strings, which\nmakes the authored prompt text hard to review and easy to damage while\nchanging the surrounding plumbing. Moving those prompts into embedded\nMarkdown templates keeps the policy text in the shape reviewers actually\nread, while preserving the existing runtime substitution and objective\nescaping behavior.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added `ext/goal/templates/goals/continuation.md`, `budget_limit.md`,\nand `objective_updated.md` for the three goal steering prompts.\n- Updated `ext/goal/src/steering.rs` to parse those embedded templates\nonce with `codex-utils-template` and render the existing goal values\ninto them.\n- Kept user objectives XML-escaped before rendering and converted budget\ncounters into template variables.\n- Added the template directory to `ext/goal/BUILD.bazel` `compile_data`\nso Bazel has the same embedded prompt inputs as Cargo.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Not run locally.","verified_at":"2026-06-01T08:55:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c875bc8a333eb492b104d8c9abb2bf4cbde195b7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c875bc8a333eb492b104d8c9abb2bf4cbde195b7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c875bc8a333eb492b104d8c9abb2bf4cbde195b7/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f1b1b64005cd477dd4821dfac8bc72097297ee96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f1b1b64005cd477dd4821dfac8bc72097297ee96","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f1b1b64005cd477dd4821dfac8bc72097297ee96"}]},{"sha":"f1b1b64005cd477dd4821dfac8bc72097297ee96","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGYxYjFiNjQwMDVjZDQ3N2RkNDgyMWRmYWM4YmM3MjA5NzI5N2VlOTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif-oai","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T08:42:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T08:42:01Z"},"message":"Add goal extension idle continuation (#25060)\n\n## Why\n\nThe goal extension needs a way to resume an active goal after the thread\nbecomes idle, but the old core goal runtime should not be refactored as\npart of this step. The missing piece is a small core-owned turn-start\nprimitive: let an extension ask for a normal model turn only when the\nthread is idle, and otherwise fail without injecting into whatever is\ncurrently active.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Adds `CodexThread::try_start_turn_if_idle(...)` as the narrow\nextension-facing primitive for synthetic idle work.\n- Implements the session side so it refuses to start when:\n  - the provided input is empty,\n  - the session is in plan mode,\n  - a turn is already active, or\n  - trigger-turn mailbox work is pending.\n- Gives trigger-turn mailbox work priority if it appears while the idle\nturn is being prepared.\n- Wires `GoalExtension::on_thread_idle` to read the active persisted\ngoal and submit the continuation prompt through this idle-only\nprimitive.\n- Keeps the legacy core goal continuation implementation in place\ninstead of folding it into this PR.\n\n## Behavior\n\nThis is intentionally best-effort. If `try_start_turn_if_idle` observes\nthat the thread is not idle, or that higher-priority mailbox work should\nrun first, it returns the input to the caller. The goal extension drops\nthat continuation prompt and waits for a future idle opportunity instead\nof injecting stale synthetic goal text into an active turn.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\ntry_start_turn_if_idle_rejects_active_turn_without_injecting`\n- `just test -p codex-goal-extension`","tree":{"sha":"0dea9703a7151bded4e9742f66ae16f4adf1ff02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/0dea9703a7151bded4e9742f66ae16f4adf1ff02"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f1b1b64005cd477dd4821dfac8bc72097297ee96","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHUXZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+SkQAJG+ogd+iPp9vfwZSzBKaQql\n16c3sG16KksWtOzDyfYQ4HionsbrnZCOJy6rqU9Q6IMTNuhdPhvCgWaNAnZgdqZs\nRJPXefnbJhaY0o6lrHIhpppeDNvmO7IwSjj+Iz7Ovvp7ODzxAwI/SLyqTlexEoDD\nyjbc/aVAbfpxs3glVzNtIJEbOhvWUCkBlPmPVgghv1YL2r+lpK+40puD5y+jr3e1\nI0e4T9UZ7j8iY+enSb/AiP5qKZID3WAuJuIHtyIbElTkC7JIrMpPXTa7JJD/s60y\nVxVD+6lhfEMMN58oGQHLMFEw9hsDMtQ2Pf0h9p/SP6EdbMsuJ2X/MegsxHvM35w7\nvWWRpN+3Jy9t9E8IqRHQhj7zt0VaqXYqhUwjE0DR076ct10O058T125/w4KRTykt\nZO12NBjcqbDOSKvhAupAucdzFK6UIWJ5JSaceR0lc+ri0obiSiA/hmSkGM58QuMa\nR8hmENbwQIAjHty4hYYEYAnty3FRtx7fpoyTwerOe3PdWsO8JX7moRRB1fCmiRWu\nHvrrpGWZ4YkiM3/PQIvQwetU3P/ftkQ3beaFMQz6QpCiiwBkdwRlw21oeGCT8/5m\nzCDPiYs8sP7A0vKE9K8kQ55ezBZ4XKoNBFR6sepY2eTXwjb/eK+pd9GF5kJHf1c8\nPeoCZFaS8o5Ud62f0Vle\n=9Z40\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0dea9703a7151bded4e9742f66ae16f4adf1ff02\nparent 8d49394febc57518479ece9e3dc5eb9060ac6968\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1780303321 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780303321 +0200\n\nAdd goal extension idle continuation (#25060)\n\n## Why\n\nThe goal extension needs a way to resume an active goal after the thread\nbecomes idle, but the old core goal runtime should not be refactored as\npart of this step. The missing piece is a small core-owned turn-start\nprimitive: let an extension ask for a normal model turn only when the\nthread is idle, and otherwise fail without injecting into whatever is\ncurrently active.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Adds `CodexThread::try_start_turn_if_idle(...)` as the narrow\nextension-facing primitive for synthetic idle work.\n- Implements the session side so it refuses to start when:\n  - the provided input is empty,\n  - the session is in plan mode,\n  - a turn is already active, or\n  - trigger-turn mailbox work is pending.\n- Gives trigger-turn mailbox work priority if it appears while the idle\nturn is being prepared.\n- Wires `GoalExtension::on_thread_idle` to read the active persisted\ngoal and submit the continuation prompt through this idle-only\nprimitive.\n- Keeps the legacy core goal continuation implementation in place\ninstead of folding it into this PR.\n\n## Behavior\n\nThis is intentionally best-effort. If `try_start_turn_if_idle` observes\nthat the thread is not idle, or that higher-priority mailbox work should\nrun first, it returns the input to the caller. The goal extension drops\nthat continuation prompt and waits for a future idle opportunity instead\nof injecting stale synthetic goal text into an active turn.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\ntry_start_turn_if_idle_rejects_active_turn_without_injecting`\n- `just test -p codex-goal-extension`","verified_at":"2026-06-01T08:42:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f1b1b64005cd477dd4821dfac8bc72097297ee96","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f1b1b64005cd477dd4821dfac8bc72097297ee96","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f1b1b64005cd477dd4821dfac8bc72097297ee96/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8d49394febc57518479ece9e3dc5eb9060ac6968","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8d49394febc57518479ece9e3dc5eb9060ac6968","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8d49394febc57518479ece9e3dc5eb9060ac6968"}]},{"sha":"8d49394febc57518479ece9e3dc5eb9060ac6968","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhkNDkzOTRmZWJjNTc1MTg0NzllY2U5ZTNkYzVlYjkwNjBhYzY5Njg","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif-oai","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-01T08:24:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T08:24:46Z"},"message":"Set multi-agent v2 dogfood defaults (#25266)\n\n## Summary\n- default multi-agent v2 to direct-model-only tools so code mode does\nnot wrap subagent tools\n- add default root/subagent team prompts aligned with dogfood training\nassumptions\n- tighten spawn-agent model override wording to prefer the inherited\nmodel by default\n\n## Tests\n- just fmt\n- just test -p codex-core\nspawn_agent_description_lists_visible_models_and_reasoning_efforts\n- just test -p codex-core\nmulti_agent_v2_default_session_thread_cap_counts_root\n- just test -p codex-rollout-trace\n- just fix -p codex-core\n- just fix -p codex-rollout-trace\n\nNote: a broad just test -p codex-core run was attempted locally, but\nthis sandbox produced unrelated environment failures around\nsandbox-exec, missing test_stdio_server, and realtime timeouts.","tree":{"sha":"dcead78ea2b2cc72974e40d97ec86ba4febe85e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/dcead78ea2b2cc72974e40d97ec86ba4febe85e3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8d49394febc57518479ece9e3dc5eb9060ac6968","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHUHOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPh0QAHjxWGM4s3n8/aFZnO7oykQM\nlvwdgL1Si+ZAMIhRWKt2HGe43urzvU8s2ACUeuOGU74VfqiyCxbz5HnvTNXwIUxD\n2CBnmncX2xbUlU9xd96aPrGouFoPSmGaWt2YRetbsPOGbyM8bvh3AWHyBWWAfigu\nx+6ClAOTf7PlW9MUxEHqtlKZ9d/lY66/TJxT0zko/hGo3mvdGDkBpZmN3qV5d3MS\nLyVSRsV7DSgZSMmEfuSxroX2UovQTnyBLirEshRtS5qGAOMC/MMWRgJ0VuKLAViP\n622l9xk71f1r4g0m/3c2UT5F1KbBj6OWjuGMLLS2VdRA6uB9tfPMs/YhwEarL8xr\naeSSGeFobz+9lGHGX+mqjIayBgBSXbAQK5P96noGhKIIDVYhLsY7NWNnFqBFrFms\ns/bmhE7hLitQQKdImLc9b7Z4s7Qfw9nAmgiVVM7ltkdJAwVMs+14HHkcD7iUjNwY\nIEly2OkK2Vh90WiROg/mJfQ32OOBmNaTtksXKcjMaxnEeh8fCQm8AULPgPVPzxyn\njJmDIa9kk79dRdyNaFbu7nq3c0r/yGrHrrFhoSXpXmk6KYBASYQeT5j9OX+MaudU\nsMfymGGbVNnu3f0kRjHsovYX8HSteg4ZAw73qs5lUIEQ1YNas8ncW9WIjhZ+pvQ4\niLV3m+f9LOurSWY+KbwK\n=CAU6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree dcead78ea2b2cc72974e40d97ec86ba4febe85e3\nparent cf0911076f234e0219bd8d61dd3bc2f80a2df287\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1780302286 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780302286 +0200\n\nSet multi-agent v2 dogfood defaults (#25266)\n\n## Summary\n- default multi-agent v2 to direct-model-only tools so code mode does\nnot wrap subagent tools\n- add default root/subagent team prompts aligned with dogfood training\nassumptions\n- tighten spawn-agent model override wording to prefer the inherited\nmodel by default\n\n## Tests\n- just fmt\n- just test -p codex-core\nspawn_agent_description_lists_visible_models_and_reasoning_efforts\n- just test -p codex-core\nmulti_agent_v2_default_session_thread_cap_counts_root\n- just test -p codex-rollout-trace\n- just fix -p codex-core\n- just fix -p codex-rollout-trace\n\nNote: a broad just test -p codex-core run was attempted locally, but\nthis sandbox produced unrelated environment failures around\nsandbox-exec, missing test_stdio_server, and realtime timeouts.","verified_at":"2026-06-01T08:24:46Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8d49394febc57518479ece9e3dc5eb9060ac6968","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8d49394febc57518479ece9e3dc5eb9060ac6968","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8d49394febc57518479ece9e3dc5eb9060ac6968/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cf0911076f234e0219bd8d61dd3bc2f80a2df287","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cf0911076f234e0219bd8d61dd3bc2f80a2df287","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/cf0911076f234e0219bd8d61dd3bc2f80a2df287"}]},{"sha":"cf0911076f234e0219bd8d61dd3bc2f80a2df287","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGNmMDkxMTA3NmYyMzRlMDIxOWJkOGQ2MWRkM2JjMmY4MGEyZGYyODc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Owen Lin","email":"owenlin0@gmail.com","date":"2026-06-01T04:33:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T04:33:20Z"},"message":"store and expose parent_thread_id on Threads (#25113)\n\n## Why\n\nThis PR\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/pull/24161#discussion_r3325692763\nrevealed a subagent data modeling issue, where we overloaded\n`forked_from_id` to also mean `parent_thread_id`. That's incorrect since\nguardian and review subagents can be a subagent and NOT fork the main\nthread's history.\n\nThe solution here is to explicitly store a new `parent_thread_id` on\n`SessionMeta`, alongside `forked_from_id` which already exists. While\nwe're at it, also expose it in the app-server protocol on the `Thread`\nobject.\n\nA thread->subagent relationship and a fork of thread history are\northogonal concepts.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added top-level `parent_thread_id` persistence on `SessionMeta` and\nruntime/session plumbing through `SessionConfiguredEvent`,\n`CodexSpawnArgs`, `SessionConfiguration`, `ThreadConfigSnapshot`,\n`TurnContext`, and `ModelClient`.\n- Made turn metadata, request headers, analytics, and subagent-start\nevents read the separate runtime/top-level parent field instead of\nderiving general parent lineage from `SessionSource` or\n`forked_from_thread_id`.\n- Passed parent lineage separately at delegated subagent, review,\nguardian, agent-job, and multi-agent spawn construction sites;\ncopied-history fork lineage remains derived only from `InitialHistory`.\n- Persisted and exposed parent lineage through rollout/thread-store\nprojections and app-server v2 `Thread.parentThreadId`.\n- Updated app-server README text and regenerated app-server schema\nfixtures for the additive `parentThreadId` response field.","tree":{"sha":"a7a7ca757ca9c413e07776ebd9fe64e3dd76c2ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a7a7ca757ca9c413e07776ebd9fe64e3dd76c2ba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/cf0911076f234e0219bd8d61dd3bc2f80a2df287","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHQuQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAb08QAHpVRXVIMHYQD/ImV5JNAqe2\nWTLygEwAq4EK55qa5QPxYJnijpAxdKCYF7J+573r9BvXgD/uDL1brtrIUvsQOdij\nS4fn46NrzyONy6OEX9j0iLiN9eoK4hj6FsYq09p44+KWDBmrElzs1wDnfR1zt7F5\ndIYBSemluhG+yH+dPZVDN6R0Hfsc/+b6usWSy1At1yCwKDh0C3CDFxnZfr9CBxoj\n+VCiffkvj9LXSwlh7wrG461pT+UGqYaPuq4CKqmprDN0gcIh9WWPQ5iQPLtQqUqp\nLPtGOBFXa3eHw0NyyRKSz2doPgtN8mGXpy3O76adnRow+0BekV14IjxatwopbFZv\nnqfRllyoP5vfAluq7C3kdQG6VcBDGegcMcT8oy6ou9CBSspAinb3EPB5XC9cxdAj\ngrISPr5yTuMbIjJjU+Yg0GW/lxBCwtbVzJpJ1y0Z3XpIW5V2rQpbq3jE/eQXTtGg\nXk6BgK2ms92PfOmPMFcR3KTv/QsHM4gPCenK1Yfoh46vW6vItBQ9fiwNX9NkF9vs\n5V6+Hq1VeSZN4zcnUzeeqWR674RGDKcvf9xgmwLKm1NkQkRHN4nSPY+bkNQfMKT0\nOBrUabenv+4tfjsnXuF+IV+TAthdC84gkD3dS5eb5X8r8LZaGdMZmvQq+K5Ib9ec\nquJdazyqiXJV1NWdcP5s\n=Go1T\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a7a7ca757ca9c413e07776ebd9fe64e3dd76c2ba\nparent 3b7334d099b339e7b18418a0cf7ac34e7bed2e43\nauthor Owen Lin <owenlin0@gmail.com> 1780288400 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780288400 +0000\n\nstore and expose parent_thread_id on Threads (#25113)\n\n## Why\n\nThis PR\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/pull/24161#discussion_r3325692763\nrevealed a subagent data modeling issue, where we overloaded\n`forked_from_id` to also mean `parent_thread_id`. That's incorrect since\nguardian and review subagents can be a subagent and NOT fork the main\nthread's history.\n\nThe solution here is to explicitly store a new `parent_thread_id` on\n`SessionMeta`, alongside `forked_from_id` which already exists. While\nwe're at it, also expose it in the app-server protocol on the `Thread`\nobject.\n\nA thread->subagent relationship and a fork of thread history are\northogonal concepts.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added top-level `parent_thread_id` persistence on `SessionMeta` and\nruntime/session plumbing through `SessionConfiguredEvent`,\n`CodexSpawnArgs`, `SessionConfiguration`, `ThreadConfigSnapshot`,\n`TurnContext`, and `ModelClient`.\n- Made turn metadata, request headers, analytics, and subagent-start\nevents read the separate runtime/top-level parent field instead of\nderiving general parent lineage from `SessionSource` or\n`forked_from_thread_id`.\n- Passed parent lineage separately at delegated subagent, review,\nguardian, agent-job, and multi-agent spawn construction sites;\ncopied-history fork lineage remains derived only from `InitialHistory`.\n- Persisted and exposed parent lineage through rollout/thread-store\nprojections and app-server v2 `Thread.parentThreadId`.\n- Updated app-server README text and regenerated app-server schema\nfixtures for the additive `parentThreadId` response field.","verified_at":"2026-06-01T04:33:21Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cf0911076f234e0219bd8d61dd3bc2f80a2df287","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/cf0911076f234e0219bd8d61dd3bc2f80a2df287","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cf0911076f234e0219bd8d61dd3bc2f80a2df287/comments","author":{"login":"owenlin0","id":947871,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk0Nzg3MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/947871?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0","html_url":"https://github.com/owenlin0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3b7334d099b339e7b18418a0cf7ac34e7bed2e43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3b7334d099b339e7b18418a0cf7ac34e7bed2e43","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3b7334d099b339e7b18418a0cf7ac34e7bed2e43"}]},{"sha":"3b7334d099b339e7b18418a0cf7ac34e7bed2e43","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDNiNzMzNGQwOTliMzM5ZTdiMTg0MThhMGNmN2FjMzRlN2JlZDJlNDM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Shijie Rao","email":"shijie.rao@openai.com","date":"2026-05-31T23:05:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-31T23:05:33Z"},"message":"Revert \"Add build_unsigned_archive release mode\" (#25462)\n\nReverts openai/codex#25435","tree":{"sha":"c435f6186551274b50f9a7cc2ff2c4e0a8d765b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c435f6186551274b50f9a7cc2ff2c4e0a8d765b6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/3b7334d099b339e7b18418a0cf7ac34e7bed2e43","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHL69CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyesQAHBcxcdK+oQC4h2RsgdfNR5B\nkaOicZBLV1V+E+UZ/FFmuhoyI7TNciqc4PZToXU7Ccr/1ZK2YdwS+hLQjAqhHMWu\n/NhRRcv5WjAJPS8n/10fdygz4otOtpVA+jcjW3CEjiaYv29gDM2UMNZ8zQJd+E9n\nBOWSu4ZoovPbTboJB1AklAZNiT6xmbXqRWeV/7aQoizEdF5faUQ23KfZ2Vg1yXez\nYo4rEm6kP22YQqeorqjqmwbay3wjDJ6fDrcIlVB4S/vvhnYvGu1mgJZ+yEH7NI1L\n5VWK8kIoK02vEzXNXbjWgwLJH8maGAJmeP1iXeymnQLmzthRJiky064rmAPOOEUl\n7VOst3HaLtfJAnzJT8DJD+tFtbr7Ui5h/kUb5pneo5CibRcmDTQZWc6ypmLCCH+c\nKVrOl7w8cUAIYBOoJmHqNwfLctzmWnrpAw1BgPG69UbiuIRfsADatdwDc0jh4UyH\nxpukxbScqofXSUoTzZLw2LR20eBzmhisCeoyupCABhQ8FGWwrMNA6knqpK5rC4MJ\n8F86B8Vf/BJGIJ/8LC/3mmJWdl55clyLy/6PmUC7QOOVWydldSD3KmCXNqBwdq/A\nzOpPCY2JN0mvx0eh/UoSlaIu/g0Q9jUzLE+z0WqaWb2s3turXZ4Ie7NrVGzRUWCs\nsXzFZ396Lp5Nf2d/V/+x\n=3Eut\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c435f6186551274b50f9a7cc2ff2c4e0a8d765b6\nparent 8a556296f0b222412be75db039724d1cac624217\nauthor Shijie Rao <shijie.rao@openai.com> 1780268733 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780268733 -0700\n\nRevert \"Add build_unsigned_archive release mode\" (#25462)\n\nReverts openai/codex#25435","verified_at":"2026-05-31T23:05:34Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3b7334d099b339e7b18418a0cf7ac34e7bed2e43","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3b7334d099b339e7b18418a0cf7ac34e7bed2e43","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3b7334d099b339e7b18418a0cf7ac34e7bed2e43/comments","author":{"login":"shijie-oai","id":235382242,"node_id":"U_kgDODgel4g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/235382242?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/shijie-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8a556296f0b222412be75db039724d1cac624217","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8a556296f0b222412be75db039724d1cac624217","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8a556296f0b222412be75db039724d1cac624217"}]},{"sha":"8a556296f0b222412be75db039724d1cac624217","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhhNTU2Mjk2ZjBiMjIyNDEyYmU3NWRiMDM5NzI0ZDFjYWM2MjQyMTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"joeflorencio-openai","email":"joeflorencio@openai.com","date":"2026-05-31T22:54:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-31T22:54:31Z"},"message":"Add cloud-managed config layer support (#24620)\n\n## Summary\n\nPR 3 of 5 in the cloud-managed config client stack.\n\nAdds enterprise-managed cloud config as a first-class config layer\nsource. The layer metadata is preserved through config loading,\ndiagnostics, debug output, hook attribution, and app-server protocol\nsurfaces.\n\n## Details\n\n- Enterprise-managed config becomes a normal config layer source with\nbackend-supplied `id` and display `name` attached for provenance.\n- These layers are designed to behave like non-file managed config: they\ncan surface syntax/type diagnostics by layer name even though there is\nno physical config file.\n- Relative path settings are resolved from a stored config base so\ncloud-delivered config remains consistent with existing MDM-delivered\nconfig semantics.\n- Hook attribution distinguishes config-delivered hooks from\nrequirements-delivered hooks via `HookSource::CloudManagedConfig`.\n- This remains pull-based and snapshot-oriented; the PR adds layer\nidentity/diagnostics, not dynamic reload behavior.\n\n## Validation\n\nValidated through the targeted stack checks after rebasing onto current\n`main`:\n\n- Rust crate tests for\nconfig/hooks/cloud-config/backend-client/app-server-protocol\n- Filtered `codex-core` and `codex-app-server` `cloud_config_bundle`\ntests\n- Python generated-file contract test\n- `cargo shear --deny-warnings`\n- Targeted `argument-comment-lint` for config/hooks","tree":{"sha":"96a656172a2666108907e6d1b39c3fc54982b622","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/96a656172a2666108907e6d1b39c3fc54982b622"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8a556296f0b222412be75db039724d1cac624217","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHLwnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAS0EQAG68MB0vSapZ8sUS1nllTrI/\nkLB5SHAk/DLHxIx+2c6O7Eb/QX3PZXiXzVtK08go6WYCjp93EkJRpJhhOCARrPIH\nkExxid5SGX2ajFqp2JpAMEOwdSgG1rvOyb91PlrUEAcDY7kO2QQfH/KLBfSCfP95\n6ZOeDE5QF8uFbRnb9/zwjTpAv659HXDe/fIVm+CMZBdOADpDorKQ6YmpQMxNLJbW\n4n4kEJ70Fcn11PAuFXQkfEt8o5otA/HBZtUvaZz6JHAKoWvACwWU74uFGKu8xGH3\nNSVWVg/aGoTjLYzLsnohRqWBjLuQnJBogRW9Vz4eoxfdgoXUhP/OykI2V3J2kIp2\niIPUrB1Dpmfg7AWTmXoeugBd1A3dcbAmbY2f2FkE0tS2hTiQ1Xw+n8/6480M3n3d\nYOvJYwAewY7FSZoSKTgps+GL6ua9ldoJzcYbrPtsO4KGp9ZWJviVQzMjSAPD4jaJ\nHKaoXNyS9gdPFhmgHJuGnbl3/MJdq6saR5vEfG9DyiKcR2yueW6A3if7BdgHm31v\ngdnOTYfz3LMrcLytOt5hM6s4Jqnb3zJRSd5/KYEtKyJRBAILeFXMnL/vbt/i0RuH\nff5U8tf5/F789kM+dXvz2Z2LXYh+yaddpk3l0EC0rGllaOo60m1hgoW3VxJubkg2\ngCGCXsHvo5m6Cq2mK1If\n=Kl7x\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 96a656172a2666108907e6d1b39c3fc54982b622\nparent 20debf746bb6bd954549c615c5ea806ad3c30377\nauthor joeflorencio-openai <joeflorencio@openai.com> 1780268071 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780268071 -0700\n\nAdd cloud-managed config layer support (#24620)\n\n## Summary\n\nPR 3 of 5 in the cloud-managed config client stack.\n\nAdds enterprise-managed cloud config as a first-class config layer\nsource. The layer metadata is preserved through config loading,\ndiagnostics, debug output, hook attribution, and app-server protocol\nsurfaces.\n\n## Details\n\n- Enterprise-managed config becomes a normal config layer source with\nbackend-supplied `id` and display `name` attached for provenance.\n- These layers are designed to behave like non-file managed config: they\ncan surface syntax/type diagnostics by layer name even though there is\nno physical config file.\n- Relative path settings are resolved from a stored config base so\ncloud-delivered config remains consistent with existing MDM-delivered\nconfig semantics.\n- Hook attribution distinguishes config-delivered hooks from\nrequirements-delivered hooks via `HookSource::CloudManagedConfig`.\n- This remains pull-based and snapshot-oriented; the PR adds layer\nidentity/diagnostics, not dynamic reload behavior.\n\n## Validation\n\nValidated through the targeted stack checks after rebasing onto current\n`main`:\n\n- Rust crate tests for\nconfig/hooks/cloud-config/backend-client/app-server-protocol\n- Filtered `codex-core` and `codex-app-server` `cloud_config_bundle`\ntests\n- Python generated-file contract test\n- `cargo shear --deny-warnings`\n- Targeted `argument-comment-lint` for config/hooks","verified_at":"2026-05-31T22:54:32Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8a556296f0b222412be75db039724d1cac624217","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8a556296f0b222412be75db039724d1cac624217","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8a556296f0b222412be75db039724d1cac624217/comments","author":{"login":"joeflorencio-openai","id":195963627,"node_id":"U_kgDOC64q6w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/195963627?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/joeflorencio-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"20debf746bb6bd954549c615c5ea806ad3c30377","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/20debf746bb6bd954549c615c5ea806ad3c30377","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/20debf746bb6bd954549c615c5ea806ad3c30377"}]},{"sha":"20debf746bb6bd954549c615c5ea806ad3c30377","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDIwZGViZjc0NmJiNmJkOTU0NTQ5YzYxNWM1ZWE4MDZhZDNjMzAzNzc","commit":{"author":{"name":"joeflorencio-openai","email":"joeflorencio@openai.com","date":"2026-05-31T22:14:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-31T22:14:06Z"},"message":"Compose requirements layers (#24619)\n\n## Summary\n\nPR 2 of 5 in the cloud-managed config client stack.\n\nAdds a shared requirements-layer composition engine. The composer\ndefines how ordered requirements layers combine, with focused tests for\nthe merge semantics and provenance behavior. The final PR in the stack\nwires runtime requirements sources into this path.\n\n## Details\n\n- Mental model: requirements layers are ordered lowest priority first,\nmatching `ConfigLayerStack`; lower-priority layers provide defaults\nwhile higher-priority layers win scalar/list conflicts.\n- Regular fields use config-style TOML merging, including recursive\ntable merging, so requirements layering follows the same broad model as\n`config.toml` layering.\n- Domain-specific fields keep explicit semantics: `rules.prefix_rules`\nand hooks preserve high-priority-first output, hooks fail closed on\nactive managed-dir conflicts, and `permissions.filesystem.deny_read`\ndedupes as a stable high-priority-first union.\n- `remote_sandbox_config` is evaluated within each layer before the\nregular TOML merge, so host-specific sandbox constraints do not leak\nacross layers.\n- Provenance points at the exact source when one layer owns a value and\nuses composite provenance when a table field is assembled from multiple\nlayers.\n\n## Validation\n\nLocal validation:\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `cargo check -p codex-config`\n- `just test -p codex-config requirements_composition`\n- `git diff --check`\n\nCI will run the broader test matrix.","tree":{"sha":"394e16d390abbd8172088ef7bddf08a9a2c6ee4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/394e16d390abbd8172088ef7bddf08a9a2c6ee4e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/20debf746bb6bd954549c615c5ea806ad3c30377","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHLKuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsCsQAEA5LvTOY87UWF5U9dETw3DW\nI/UaF4tAmBpweuechqY50xlJKEaYSJ6RDK9apE4R5sAkyTRH6mh7npboccwMs0Nk\nZUX8jDN1gfNjWaebxpESYhaMMMxSgd29XhM9M3MWbgiWowWq1WxCFFgFjDqG/6mg\nZqhHamS9OwP2wXN5mbSjqa4/1ff3cMQCEyAz+wviC7sMxoQfaFtC/fmMGrmaCLz3\nPoKB7yfBaYZhTTMrFZj5ulaut415CSN877L+0sqWvJLCJaqac8169hOxiFxou1pg\nWbkR4a2e2Ps076aJKnEqrEXlbTyCXHplC91g3vCaDFDAT1hckToRJqJEALOfIfqB\nl262D/rTekNwibPHa9RLhaSQo0COUN/3SXxQlIykxnTxwm06vM4lwugLR+dEbuVT\nJ5ztcdRXJcfsKeSyTfZdDgS6ZBkl/vNMo9p7rBGUVZI+WQq2V8iVFU6gm1a4p4au\nd/+h9oDwPEFHjmHOK5RGEYNJK+96pYH4d94569uf3uIAtdnS/8miBQP3y+wLP+ix\nYU4ltJv7Lmeeo1o02FrdkbT7K795Wo2KTwo5EWXqU4tFUZjstmjO0WepRFV9h8+d\n+3jS7yi9DCsOlJlAEb7/kjEXge7UiuY850PGxn4qTrVKZ+ROMn4H77nUogNdJ8NP\ndUoFjivQZzi3KdUqsUQK\n=WB1J\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 394e16d390abbd8172088ef7bddf08a9a2c6ee4e\nparent 5f60b013524c6fbdc597417c15c1e1ee96244176\nauthor joeflorencio-openai <joeflorencio@openai.com> 1780265646 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780265646 -0700\n\nCompose requirements layers (#24619)\n\n## Summary\n\nPR 2 of 5 in the cloud-managed config client stack.\n\nAdds a shared requirements-layer composition engine. The composer\ndefines how ordered requirements layers combine, with focused tests for\nthe merge semantics and provenance behavior. The final PR in the stack\nwires runtime requirements sources into this path.\n\n## Details\n\n- Mental model: requirements layers are ordered lowest priority first,\nmatching `ConfigLayerStack`; lower-priority layers provide defaults\nwhile higher-priority layers win scalar/list conflicts.\n- Regular fields use config-style TOML merging, including recursive\ntable merging, so requirements layering follows the same broad model as\n`config.toml` layering.\n- Domain-specific fields keep explicit semantics: `rules.prefix_rules`\nand hooks preserve high-priority-first output, hooks fail closed on\nactive managed-dir conflicts, and `permissions.filesystem.deny_read`\ndedupes as a stable high-priority-first union.\n- `remote_sandbox_config` is evaluated within each layer before the\nregular TOML merge, so host-specific sandbox constraints do not leak\nacross layers.\n- Provenance points at the exact source when one layer owns a value and\nuses composite provenance when a table field is assembled from multiple\nlayers.\n\n## Validation\n\nLocal validation:\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `cargo check -p codex-config`\n- `just test -p codex-config requirements_composition`\n- `git diff --check`\n\nCI will run the broader test matrix.","verified_at":"2026-05-31T22:14:07Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/20debf746bb6bd954549c615c5ea806ad3c30377","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/20debf746bb6bd954549c615c5ea806ad3c30377","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/20debf746bb6bd954549c615c5ea806ad3c30377/comments","author":{"login":"joeflorencio-openai","id":195963627,"node_id":"U_kgDOC64q6w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/195963627?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/joeflorencio-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5f60b013524c6fbdc597417c15c1e1ee96244176","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5f60b013524c6fbdc597417c15c1e1ee96244176","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5f60b013524c6fbdc597417c15c1e1ee96244176"}]},{"sha":"5f60b013524c6fbdc597417c15c1e1ee96244176","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDVmNjBiMDEzNTI0YzZmYmRjNTk3NDE3YzE1YzFlMWVlOTYyNDQxNzY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Shijie Rao","email":"shijie.rao@openai.com","date":"2026-05-31T21:56:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-31T21:56:06Z"},"message":"Add build_unsigned_archive release mode (#25435)\n\n## Why\nWe want a manual mode that produces the full packaged unsigned macOS\nCodex archive, including bundled resources like `rg`, without mixing\nthose archives into the signing and publishing flow.\n\nThe existing `build_unsigned` mode is the handoff used by external\nsigning and `promote_signed`, so archive-only inspection and local\npackaging should live in a separate mode and artifact namespace.\n\n## What Changed\n- added `build_unsigned_archive` as a new manual `release_mode`\n- kept the existing `build` matrix running for that mode instead of\nintroducing a separate archive-only job\n- wrote unsigned macOS package archives to\n`codex-rs/unsigned-archive-dist/...` instead of the normal `dist/...`\ntree\n- uploaded those packaged macOS outputs as dedicated\n`*-unsigned-archive` workflow artifacts\n- kept `build_unsigned` and `promote_signed` on their existing raw\nunsigned binary path\n\n## Validation\n- parsed `.github/workflows/rust-release.yml` with `ruby -e 'require\n\"yaml\"; YAML.load_file(\".github/workflows/rust-release.yml\")'`\n- ran `git diff --check -- .github/workflows/rust-release.yml`\n- reviewed the workflow diff to confirm `build_unsigned_archive` now\nreuses the existing `build` job while isolating the unsigned macOS\npackage archives under dedicated artifact names\n- locally verified the package builder layout against unsigned macOS\nbinaries to confirm the packaged archive contains `bin/codex`,\n`codex-path/rg`, and `codex-resources/zsh/bin/zsh`","tree":{"sha":"45d25aae9205a40782f5012055bf5703410a390e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/45d25aae9205a40782f5012055bf5703410a390e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/5f60b013524c6fbdc597417c15c1e1ee96244176","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHK52CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAl4IQAJREzkz7XXDSRdevu7ROXUc1\nxL/vNiai1t2bVbzq3yG95Pf8cIprBava2kCm/678pZYrlD9V31UILwDX9KSWAJ1b\n8ShYfcCbwM7cUC0TLQBYVxgcYUK31U5lt2a0AYSmaaHjAU/XIO1XD6mtlc3IfX5a\nk468NebYmGPZrQBYN+jhv3ivcCfDU2/XxU9JO+TmdkF7xPK8tCmtRKUWmwCctACo\nC0PCA0z5f70L3jAyIPLQNG0bZo0OisxUKRcZfrjPJ5iS9v5AbT3G+fxNcnbMohBo\nZ9hN+U8koyhauUlcaW5oOF7oxyFxyc9eXbHVNQ/SL7/yUDU7XVi8MSaaj/gWKl0V\nXdwBtGXKRE5aSV4ewoL/vko58DwfNDyYrp8hJ4X4YdlMfU2Q26BTpIUPy/Y6Rnyd\nrW5+gcqFgmAlSG04rJV98KiTVB596WpN5Rts2bnwAZR69JG2HGIwWpEjKIb8lpX6\nq0G7NrGRlBoy9biP8IxmjxSb8xdgkk5/adhPL7Th1Piv9BUkfmnowLSlE+rzO4t4\nG5FUjhd3Ti/SXRWPW345iUQF01VCiVxiQSwuZ3zCWC5i2dDojiiWt+vhJDJobiWx\n6v89CjPNknVyym1R6tE3viOVY6dvYE0C8Sg2Pdw78nholTIy6dQJKMmMLX/+Xuge\no5TFKmBA88hmQdcWYTgu\n=OlAE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 45d25aae9205a40782f5012055bf5703410a390e\nparent e93dc98a48d597df322436ffe8d03bfd7ec63b3b\nauthor Shijie Rao <shijie.rao@openai.com> 1780264566 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780264566 -0700\n\nAdd build_unsigned_archive release mode (#25435)\n\n## Why\nWe want a manual mode that produces the full packaged unsigned macOS\nCodex archive, including bundled resources like `rg`, without mixing\nthose archives into the signing and publishing flow.\n\nThe existing `build_unsigned` mode is the handoff used by external\nsigning and `promote_signed`, so archive-only inspection and local\npackaging should live in a separate mode and artifact namespace.\n\n## What Changed\n- added `build_unsigned_archive` as a new manual `release_mode`\n- kept the existing `build` matrix running for that mode instead of\nintroducing a separate archive-only job\n- wrote unsigned macOS package archives to\n`codex-rs/unsigned-archive-dist/...` instead of the normal `dist/...`\ntree\n- uploaded those packaged macOS outputs as dedicated\n`*-unsigned-archive` workflow artifacts\n- kept `build_unsigned` and `promote_signed` on their existing raw\nunsigned binary path\n\n## Validation\n- parsed `.github/workflows/rust-release.yml` with `ruby -e 'require\n\"yaml\"; YAML.load_file(\".github/workflows/rust-release.yml\")'`\n- ran `git diff --check -- .github/workflows/rust-release.yml`\n- reviewed the workflow diff to confirm `build_unsigned_archive` now\nreuses the existing `build` job while isolating the unsigned macOS\npackage archives under dedicated artifact names\n- locally verified the package builder layout against unsigned macOS\nbinaries to confirm the packaged archive contains `bin/codex`,\n`codex-path/rg`, and `codex-resources/zsh/bin/zsh`","verified_at":"2026-05-31T21:56:07Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5f60b013524c6fbdc597417c15c1e1ee96244176","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5f60b013524c6fbdc597417c15c1e1ee96244176","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5f60b013524c6fbdc597417c15c1e1ee96244176/comments","author":{"login":"shijie-oai","id":235382242,"node_id":"U_kgDODgel4g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/235382242?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/shijie-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e93dc98a48d597df322436ffe8d03bfd7ec63b3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e93dc98a48d597df322436ffe8d03bfd7ec63b3b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e93dc98a48d597df322436ffe8d03bfd7ec63b3b"}]},{"sha":"e93dc98a48d597df322436ffe8d03bfd7ec63b3b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGU5M2RjOThhNDhkNTk3ZGYzMjI0MzZmZmU4ZDAzYmZkN2VjNjNiM2I","commit":{"author":{"name":"joeflorencio-openai","email":"joeflorencio@openai.com","date":"2026-05-31T18:52:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-31T18:52:18Z"},"message":"Add config bundle transport types (#24617)\n\n## Summary\n\nPR 1 of 5 in the cloud-managed config client stack.\n\nAdds the generated backend models and client transport surface for the\nconfig bundle endpoint. This bundle endpoint is the replacement backend\nsurface for legacy cloud requirements; the final PR in the stack\nswitches runtime consumers over to it.\n\n## Details\n\n- This is transport-only plumbing: no runtime config behavior changes in\nthis PR.\n- The bundle endpoint is the new shared backend surface for\ncloud-delivered config and requirements data.\n- Both supported path styles are wired here: `/api/codex/config/bundle`\nand `/wham/config/bundle`.\n- The response types come from generated backend models so later PRs\nconsume the backend contract directly instead of maintaining\nhand-written mirror structs.\n\n## Validation\n\nValidated through the targeted stack checks after rebasing onto current\n`main`:\n\n- Rust crate tests for\nconfig/hooks/cloud-config/backend-client/app-server-protocol\n- Filtered `codex-core` and `codex-app-server` `cloud_config_bundle`\ntests\n- Python generated-file contract test\n- `cargo shear --deny-warnings`\n- Targeted `argument-comment-lint` for config/hooks","tree":{"sha":"ac0fe8bb4a78d55f3d4b75e8b2f86a49c0575bc6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/ac0fe8bb4a78d55f3d4b75e8b2f86a49c0575bc6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e93dc98a48d597df322436ffe8d03bfd7ec63b3b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHINiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGvIQAIPksbRQZykRCGQUEExyodeU\nJ8ZwAwPIroy9P4JoTuVL8xF3YRXNKX8dHiDUAQbrGz/rd3lekPq9c8gTVmVMBPdT\nifNrvnLDPGLYJisYCNdyunJWOU9FGCsfTSKA2WxLM60ri1XLun8KpCMoQeP4uA+J\nGjqPVO1QqlbsKS/cQ1q9zzrHQq8I04hIQ3RiZBleX59+ipEDYH1lQNp3uAlsjvJl\nMsAAFCqtJkGpKKCNeCCTtoJ6FirR8TQL2Z5Lim13LLkBRApip8np06q715cfUeRm\nYUTvkkZLFmOSDGwkBlPZxbGMA2O8p0zkm0R3wuyRWX9r5l/H7ScS1rwDFbztfgZw\n6fDE1fIbxKmdGEe89tzhWfmL7mGmbHxknZxOwwH6ytH58pz4vrlbnPlzKQdJDo5p\nCBNpnvQnXMgn4d8XXFndwBBlfkCdpeMb5Rw3WESwvt4JQ+nuPolCVWCDEBeg9Kku\nBp22D3uP9iy4VmhV5Y5nEjtaZLhzrZYObvMkXFGcMX4QfWjXPQksNeTpDOt+KwtM\nQFTRqrQ0Dk2WeV+n5d+64g9SN88/7Na4WpEo41R6ZUjag7neKGW3HINCxsDeHGA4\nbAg1030WMptIo3Xa8/P5ZL2ke217afpV611pxcdBHSvEm9KOmSq1g0lqIFVfXjOe\ntQ2l64Y5BpWxSmioIMW4\n=aR/Q\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ac0fe8bb4a78d55f3d4b75e8b2f86a49c0575bc6\nparent 2f0726ad6d5939e5e79b4df6fcb71f79a5fdf48f\nauthor joeflorencio-openai <joeflorencio@openai.com> 1780253538 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780253538 -0700\n\nAdd config bundle transport types (#24617)\n\n## Summary\n\nPR 1 of 5 in the cloud-managed config client stack.\n\nAdds the generated backend models and client transport surface for the\nconfig bundle endpoint. This bundle endpoint is the replacement backend\nsurface for legacy cloud requirements; the final PR in the stack\nswitches runtime consumers over to it.\n\n## Details\n\n- This is transport-only plumbing: no runtime config behavior changes in\nthis PR.\n- The bundle endpoint is the new shared backend surface for\ncloud-delivered config and requirements data.\n- Both supported path styles are wired here: `/api/codex/config/bundle`\nand `/wham/config/bundle`.\n- The response types come from generated backend models so later PRs\nconsume the backend contract directly instead of maintaining\nhand-written mirror structs.\n\n## Validation\n\nValidated through the targeted stack checks after rebasing onto current\n`main`:\n\n- Rust crate tests for\nconfig/hooks/cloud-config/backend-client/app-server-protocol\n- Filtered `codex-core` and `codex-app-server` `cloud_config_bundle`\ntests\n- Python generated-file contract test\n- `cargo shear --deny-warnings`\n- Targeted `argument-comment-lint` for config/hooks","verified_at":"2026-05-31T18:52:19Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e93dc98a48d597df322436ffe8d03bfd7ec63b3b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e93dc98a48d597df322436ffe8d03bfd7ec63b3b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e93dc98a48d597df322436ffe8d03bfd7ec63b3b/comments","author":{"login":"joeflorencio-openai","id":195963627,"node_id":"U_kgDOC64q6w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/195963627?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/joeflorencio-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/joeflorencio-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2f0726ad6d5939e5e79b4df6fcb71f79a5fdf48f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2f0726ad6d5939e5e79b4df6fcb71f79a5fdf48f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2f0726ad6d5939e5e79b4df6fcb71f79a5fdf48f"}]},{"sha":"2f0726ad6d5939e5e79b4df6fcb71f79a5fdf48f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDJmMDcyNmFkNmQ1OTM5ZTVlNzliNGRmNmZjYjcxZjc5YTVmZGY0OGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Felipe Coury","email":"felipe.coury@openai.com","date":"2026-05-31T18:42:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-31T18:42:39Z"},"message":"feat(tui): allow function keys through f24 in keymaps (#25329)\n\n## Why\n\nCloses #25006.\n\n`tui.keymap` currently rejects `F13` even though Codex's terminal event\nlayer can report higher function keys. This prevents users from using\ncommon remappings such as Caps Lock to `F13`.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Define a shared portable upper bound of `F24` for stored TUI\nkeybindings.\n- Accept `f13` through `f24` in config normalization and runtime\nparsing.\n- Allow `/keymap` capture to persist `F13` through `F24`.\n- Update the unsupported-function-key error and add boundary tests for\n`F13`, `F24`, and `F25`.\n\n## How to Test\n\n1. Add a binding such as:\n\n   ```toml\n   [tui.keymap.global]\n   open_transcript = \"f13\"\n   ```\n\n2. Start Codex and press the remapped `F13` key.\n3. Confirm Codex loads the config without the previous `F1 through F12`\nerror and the action runs.\n4. Open `/keymap`, capture `F13` for an action, and confirm the saved\nbinding is `f13`.\n5. As a regression check, try to capture `F25` and confirm Codex reports\nthat only `F1` through `F24` can be stored.\n\nTargeted tests:\n\n- `just test -p codex-config`\n- `just test -p codex-tui function_keys`\n\nFull `just test -p codex-tui` completed with 2,752 passing tests, 4\nskipped tests, and two unrelated guardian feature-flag failures:\n\n-\n`app::tests::update_feature_flags_disabling_guardian_clears_review_policy_and_restores_default`\n-\n`app::tests::update_feature_flags_disabling_guardian_clears_manual_review_policy_without_history`","tree":{"sha":"08a441c076f493ca2edae8df552005779edf5bfc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/08a441c076f493ca2edae8df552005779edf5bfc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/2f0726ad6d5939e5e79b4df6fcb71f79a5fdf48f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHIEfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOGEQAD8LijAn/JY8tUjFihTXfe+t\n+dyCVkIxGJwHSTpC4U6G3133c3xqyVMJ9iW1x71Szl04qHiKSEOIP01JBWgkuIxS\nGX0GkNBSmP/2/8fUSi2zXbyn2RkkdGxlMuSGckxLeHRRa0l7Eq4l9WDtDg6mhYgE\nPeB1cr2ODXe+etm22mrW4fLEjiDwSpOtmGt6YZLSTSgnOcAUbOd20Dp+GqO6mpjc\nJlcSXJN2TMrBdax//0mg3PI4Ku+6Wvju60ncEyCQit/lUtXTK8tvLv9teelN+g5r\nGN+CwFsAkbRfUtxFKaSDOUTn+DIhCFCVwn90l4lwFtOmYf0GUhd/CwRJgutJ5wZK\n/gwUUvp6VoldpTK/8e3vEDfbEYG37M6CZzX7KahhO999BSIN7V78jruM3yLNl02z\nALhMdNQlM4LNVdppobgutxBDPmXH4yuzdjSh8HDsenx7ExY+hKMGI1THyg5knt3B\nQvakr/KFy31Jd4tjTIeLA1aIlB3VJuZ24p73heXwTvlDICU9GB1HuddKsp9OxYW1\nez+WsfbkGuIHerG1+jNOGfbcVZEc8sk6nE4G2eWMAbAIoiSg+8mS2j8utz4t7a9B\ni5xcztkf/Pg4kiZL3t969uSVcK83PJjQGZW8aKRq9Fh9IP3VxT6Uz72fNPrw6Td7\nmOWLtXqSc+zaCZFupen3\n=GSdN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 08a441c076f493ca2edae8df552005779edf5bfc\nparent cdde711fac008cd4e1115603ead713cf23b1a580\nauthor Felipe Coury <felipe.coury@openai.com> 1780252959 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780252959 -0300\n\nfeat(tui): allow function keys through f24 in keymaps (#25329)\n\n## Why\n\nCloses #25006.\n\n`tui.keymap` currently rejects `F13` even though Codex's terminal event\nlayer can report higher function keys. This prevents users from using\ncommon remappings such as Caps Lock to `F13`.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Define a shared portable upper bound of `F24` for stored TUI\nkeybindings.\n- Accept `f13` through `f24` in config normalization and runtime\nparsing.\n- Allow `/keymap` capture to persist `F13` through `F24`.\n- Update the unsupported-function-key error and add boundary tests for\n`F13`, `F24`, and `F25`.\n\n## How to Test\n\n1. Add a binding such as:\n\n   ```toml\n   [tui.keymap.global]\n   open_transcript = \"f13\"\n   ```\n\n2. Start Codex and press the remapped `F13` key.\n3. Confirm Codex loads the config without the previous `F1 through F12`\nerror and the action runs.\n4. Open `/keymap`, capture `F13` for an action, and confirm the saved\nbinding is `f13`.\n5. As a regression check, try to capture `F25` and confirm Codex reports\nthat only `F1` through `F24` can be stored.\n\nTargeted tests:\n\n- `just test -p codex-config`\n- `just test -p codex-tui function_keys`\n\nFull `just test -p codex-tui` completed with 2,752 passing tests, 4\nskipped tests, and two unrelated guardian feature-flag failures:\n\n-\n`app::tests::update_feature_flags_disabling_guardian_clears_review_policy_and_restores_default`\n-\n`app::tests::update_feature_flags_disabling_guardian_clears_manual_review_policy_without_history`","verified_at":"2026-05-31T18:42:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2f0726ad6d5939e5e79b4df6fcb71f79a5fdf48f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2f0726ad6d5939e5e79b4df6fcb71f79a5fdf48f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2f0726ad6d5939e5e79b4df6fcb71f79a5fdf48f/comments","author":{"login":"fcoury-oai","id":272635208,"node_id":"U_kgDOEEAVSA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272635208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/fcoury-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cdde711fac008cd4e1115603ead713cf23b1a580","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cdde711fac008cd4e1115603ead713cf23b1a580","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/cdde711fac008cd4e1115603ead713cf23b1a580"}]},{"sha":"cdde711fac008cd4e1115603ead713cf23b1a580","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGNkZGU3MTFmYWMwMDhjZDRlMTExNTYwM2VhZDcxM2NmMjNiMWE1ODA","commit":{"author":{"name":"xl-openai","email":"xl@openai.com","date":"2026-05-31T09:14:15Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-31T09:14:15Z"},"message":"[codex] Avoid forced directory refresh during plugin install auth checks (#25381)\n\n## Summary\n- Use normal directory loading for plugin install app metadata so\ninstall avoids forced directory refresh while still loading metadata on\ncold cache.\n- Continue force-refreshing codex_apps tools for auth state.\n- Add regression coverage that pre-warms the directory cache and asserts\ninstall returns cached app metadata without extra directory requests.\n\n## Validation\n- just fmt\n- git diff --check\n- just test -p codex-app-server plugin_install_returns_apps_needing_auth\nplugin_install_filters_disallowed_apps_needing_auth (blocked locally:\ncargo-nextest is not installed)","tree":{"sha":"076195d5fd0ec4c98ef02c77ffbc12a85fc67cf6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/076195d5fd0ec4c98ef02c77ffbc12a85fc67cf6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/cdde711fac008cd4e1115603ead713cf23b1a580","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqG/vnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8/sQADr43za7JG33UMfqHlBJXn6g\nSqISzEidQIDPeQiVoUmK5vO6cTplspDqR+zp91TngDLz6iTfc+NjM4S6a1irDqqn\nKF+pj1UJUxCrregGpJTBuRVPo9KC+KhNxpWNajSwKb8rGxGm+rIt2GVSVFD5m5Jo\n7gQTJ2Muv2RUAbGud2QCIisHnNDCFUHh5dvUshVRDA5fz7esuJ+JspXGrmv1GR2Y\nGXZ5JCzDnwGg/DI79RZfQiJ0kodMRpBXgxG2Hles9UZFVmFLe59y8ve/UPc0rTyA\nonPbIQaB233xoqmocKCjTk1/3exHXKg82HhvERKTw4q6sf41AqcVDhl+b6vHEIzs\nolUGZFWEu24IpSBebpHL/SX7RKtmLXCodYas2A/9kMaXjAtSKKNsHyZGWEjzmpS8\n4p0JNc0GcLSjKY8CDyR1877NY3K72oWkRw4pk0nZ7Y65FtOoGMHGUeDSlJ6Oge+O\nYpvuYeDS2hOkZiFkHJ0/es2IqX6KDHGNe/hMx8shymA1vv+Ud5GGPs2dy+qzzd2K\n4YSmLCHWLQgTrm3LbW5hy8ti/KJfA4UcknvY38GkKaJxn08WC92+1wFTr8R05o/U\n8OVbTIKiMIPGqs9HMVSl/tJ9SZgAC/VX/WdmKn0eD7+7Iqsb+6ZZY4Xjlf49Txey\nyAcjPUE5qsABU1/odlWV\n=B9L+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 076195d5fd0ec4c98ef02c77ffbc12a85fc67cf6\nparent 966932124c243aab71719c269d79305844f35814\nauthor xl-openai <xl@openai.com> 1780218855 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780218855 -0700\n\n[codex] Avoid forced directory refresh during plugin install auth checks (#25381)\n\n## Summary\n- Use normal directory loading for plugin install app metadata so\ninstall avoids forced directory refresh while still loading metadata on\ncold cache.\n- Continue force-refreshing codex_apps tools for auth state.\n- Add regression coverage that pre-warms the directory cache and asserts\ninstall returns cached app metadata without extra directory requests.\n\n## Validation\n- just fmt\n- git diff --check\n- just test -p codex-app-server plugin_install_returns_apps_needing_auth\nplugin_install_filters_disallowed_apps_needing_auth (blocked locally:\ncargo-nextest is not installed)","verified_at":"2026-05-31T09:14:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cdde711fac008cd4e1115603ead713cf23b1a580","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/cdde711fac008cd4e1115603ead713cf23b1a580","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cdde711fac008cd4e1115603ead713cf23b1a580/comments","author":{"login":"xl-openai","id":184293535,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvwYnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184293535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/xl-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"966932124c243aab71719c269d79305844f35814","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/966932124c243aab71719c269d79305844f35814","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/966932124c243aab71719c269d79305844f35814"}]},{"sha":"966932124c243aab71719c269d79305844f35814","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDk2NjkzMjEyNGMyNDNhYWI3MTcxOWMyNjlkNzkzMDU4NDRmMzU4MTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Owen Lin","email":"owenlin0@gmail.com","date":"2026-05-30T18:54:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-30T18:54:58Z"},"message":"fix: Limit Bedrock GPT models to default service tier (#25318)\n\n## Description\n\nBedrock currently only supports the implicit `default` service tier for\nGPT models. This PR strips non-default service tier metadata from\nBedrock model catalogs so Codex does not advertise or send unsupported\ntiers.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Normalize both built-in and configured Bedrock catalogs to\ndefault-only service tier behavior.\n- Add regression coverage for built-in and configured Bedrock catalogs.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-model-provider`","tree":{"sha":"5e93511ce680ef8e4141649c0591e18e2498b8c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/5e93511ce680ef8e4141649c0591e18e2498b8c1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/966932124c243aab71719c269d79305844f35814","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGzKCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARDcQAEvHWCOlbNpF7Z6GZ7LLYQBR\ntandOScPDYT6Pdkau/JwPXUn84fs1BbENjnLNL8v6dUufud/9b/4s2pEdiL3/4Ra\nqtERetk0bZXnificOOBghqCAdUjUvshsewkx3wt3eeriVDQav7aGojVOIOB4+guj\nJlD9XoUCtWTgW0kmJEypwiKFoBrt4ZYccTrc42YB351FBBN2Li0NoIn9lozwDvUe\nw1RGIodfZn/nbyPcuXRw6bCdnRGS6IHH8A3JaSOWR5riFlgN1+kmyQBKlH41nr5L\nQ97RykOgaV/FJZ/CjjLvetacCmUVZQIGADNw9EPgE0D5NV3TYWSpFd+BY6oLyv2i\nYmqKmQ5R5UE81eg8SPhlVFwTEtpy3a+gIdUmZRASohKU57PCOQgv3/Og60oRyTfu\nYDHu5dJ492zMfywT8lxyfZrQafK2UdHMI2kzsroaf5nayxbE//MIxSvCCxH6zPfB\npTqzDowMXnssHd/9oj47Sdh+uxUc93uwGfUeyhFJ+6TwENK5o+vQpxDNAWy/IUuo\nNRVcKFiq72NPd6EK+8/vmwofncl2Cnt1/961nEshDmTc+Czvdg6+zEbYADJdDNWr\nz7OMK1CF2I961g3GclGDONZJlqKG6NN0AI5opEJERPZP22ED1UGrt1Pyk3aaaSsq\n8BzFFupMyrVKzAHr0pxm\n=PqXu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5e93511ce680ef8e4141649c0591e18e2498b8c1\nparent 8acaec73b6a227ae9375064e910ecf86f2620ec0\nauthor Owen Lin <owenlin0@gmail.com> 1780167298 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780167298 -0700\n\nfix: Limit Bedrock GPT models to default service tier (#25318)\n\n## Description\n\nBedrock currently only supports the implicit `default` service tier for\nGPT models. This PR strips non-default service tier metadata from\nBedrock model catalogs so Codex does not advertise or send unsupported\ntiers.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Normalize both built-in and configured Bedrock catalogs to\ndefault-only service tier behavior.\n- Add regression coverage for built-in and configured Bedrock catalogs.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-model-provider`","verified_at":"2026-05-30T18:54:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/966932124c243aab71719c269d79305844f35814","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/966932124c243aab71719c269d79305844f35814","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/966932124c243aab71719c269d79305844f35814/comments","author":{"login":"owenlin0","id":947871,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk0Nzg3MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/947871?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0","html_url":"https://github.com/owenlin0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owe