(#25267)\n\n## Summary\n- rename the multi-agent v2 follow-up task tool surface to assign_task\n- update core tests and spec-plan expectations\n- keep rollout-trace classification backward-compatible with legacy\nfollowup_task\n\n## Tests\n- just fmt\n- just test -p codex-core\nmulti_agents_spec::tests::assign_task_tool_requires_message_and_has_no_output_schema\n- just test -p codex-rollout-trace\n- just fix -p codex-core\n- just fix -p codex-rollout-trace\n\nNote: a broad just test -p codex-core run was attempted locally, but\nthis sandbox produced unrelated environment failures around\nsandbox-exec, missing test_stdio_server, and realtime timeouts.","tree":{"sha":"2a3968a30f43f4df980a0026f8e3bb9af5677c39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2a3968a30f43f4df980a0026f8e3bb9af5677c39"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8acaec73b6a227ae9375064e910ecf86f2620ec0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGtRRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoUkQABYl2APpR0VjIkN690eqrXdg\n16/COFJhZ3QVcS2WpxG+2KqUpwOy9tLcDbPSXXKYqrOGty6V3baUhrEuk+XzoJSp\nyaFdKvxclPjpHjG9+BzjE9h5bUmzLTwTfvfZRMgBn2Oj6aAPfhegmhIWgxuZkP4N\ncSBZFSqJ1Kz0e0V5eAoUCSTmMqHskbg9f53hMSrap7vJKy0j17RrhOpWuVTqb5Kl\neCpGRNUlcTYfAv+5M7BjZ1iLjWYCZmeg2suo6aH0lDuKa6R0z/RpTJTiD02HAa4Q\nm0TMmFEIW74s2xRUTyxqQnKlLMoz3jf2cQMd9ala1VSV/QAohBxS81GKUrD52oXU\nNIcm1+lElce1xG0sboYDgxQCXT9yVHmobaJE7MpZlgrCWnPS68W597vB4I+HWgmD\ndLaDPBDmU5RP1uzV6kE0jqKtYW4i8LiKnWBmeWMWps7rW1MtzYmEQZxrk4C8r70Q\nL+HKGW5Avou+9zRuv5UAeNr2J4vWeTGYZicI2jKx9IwAXlIA4v8CFAXkkoSfJowr\nzVfw8YHASOCmplT3VMcCJaQ11tYMpiKXNyMgLGAqrRviUQySKZ17PXlZBzc28kkJ\nrpP5JX6vlTHn6DRkBJe9kH6bRmt755diGElvWEc9Tg6IGNG+6l/JvJt8eHOfZn1j\nJtghdTvZoIHuk9EGzoey\n=Fz8I\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2a3968a30f43f4df980a0026f8e3bb9af5677c39\nparent 3e7baa00e43419967d90d6ad9cef40f58d5ac89f\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1780143185 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780143185 +0200\n\nRename multi-agent v2 assignment tool (#25267)\n\n## Summary\n- rename the multi-agent v2 follow-up task tool surface to assign_task\n- update core tests and spec-plan expectations\n- keep rollout-trace classification backward-compatible with legacy\nfollowup_task\n\n## Tests\n- just fmt\n- just test -p codex-core\nmulti_agents_spec::tests::assign_task_tool_requires_message_and_has_no_output_schema\n- just test -p codex-rollout-trace\n- just fix -p codex-core\n- just fix -p codex-rollout-trace\n\nNote: a broad just test -p codex-core run was attempted locally, but\nthis sandbox produced unrelated environment failures around\nsandbox-exec, missing test_stdio_server, and realtime timeouts.","verified_at":"2026-05-30T12:13:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8acaec73b6a227ae9375064e910ecf86f2620ec0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8acaec73b6a227ae9375064e910ecf86f2620ec0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8acaec73b6a227ae9375064e910ecf86f2620ec0/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3e7baa00e43419967d90d6ad9cef40f58d5ac89f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3e7baa00e43419967d90d6ad9cef40f58d5ac89f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3e7baa00e43419967d90d6ad9cef40f58d5ac89f"}]},{"sha":"3e7baa00e43419967d90d6ad9cef40f58d5ac89f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDNlN2JhYTAwZTQzNDE5OTY3ZDkwZDZhZDljZWY0MGY1OGQ1YWM4OWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-05-30T06:37:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-30T06:37:26Z"},"message":"Add thread archive CLI commands (#25021)\n\n## Problem\n\nSaved threads can already be archived through app-server RPCs, but the\ncommand line did not expose direct archive or unarchive commands.\n\n## Solution\n\nAdd `codex archive <thread>` and `codex unarchive <thread>`, resolving\nUUIDs or exact thread names before calling the existing `thread/archive`\nand `thread/unarchive` RPCs. The commands support scoped remote flags so\ncallers can target remote app-server endpoints when archiving or\nunarchiving threads.\n\nThis also fixes a long-standing bug in `codex resume <thread id>` and\n`codex fork <thread id>` that I found when testing the new commands.\nThese operations shouldn't be allowed on archived sessions. They now\nfail with an error that tells the user to run `codex unarchive <thread\nid>` first.\n\n## Verification\n\nAdded app-server coverage for rejecting archived thread resume by id and\nchecking that the error includes the matching `codex unarchive <thread\nid>` command.","tree":{"sha":"cda3e31a80aee96c2fbc7e9ffe037ab0d6ae7d09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/cda3e31a80aee96c2fbc7e9ffe037ab0d6ae7d09"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/3e7baa00e43419967d90d6ad9cef40f58d5ac89f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGoWmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVe4QAA4GWAmgfKIfeWOslUSNZYVe\nUHmxsjWfr0JJ16H4VX5BTcRAs+NXJNNWJQNLWU/NO/jO7IRy+b1qh2lCBVYzL5DI\nOCR2G3DUZNgRc6/ic6Dz5XFgPeHv/QNSnDI/sXC8KDgGXvjlpeEPVaEWh7bu6cAG\nUJ+vuNgOZ5K7axhF5Fdgr37DA7PPs8OFhOueVLuU484GWGxWpNxOCose9y80mxIY\n9WxdjsNhEBLo/DNEpb0da1N+PWKj02AThvEYAjycyuqsq9E05pNC+LHOmloT5gGO\nj42QncBlJAUBOfEc972OtCR9ygItcAefmBjEcPlYSvos2DR4rDtrzTZdFKKaijHO\n+US9J0RHSIi47yCmQF901a5eQzga0/1j5oxyfXcu36me0/MD0Vd9WqEMOhxolNps\nPFNqnipyOXlJfj/a+NyEoeIK2/Z8Z77zGmfKqkOeWwa1zp5GJ4Zpyee9ivvfHDHL\nkUfTQEVEN/5majEQuQVi2qmseLPo18eX9atuZKQnx4DTilDkgfjiusD+2TSm8hhK\nNUjfw4Woa6LRJxLVNl6vzFPHNhpN7g5Lb7jNl80gWK2jNz7zriqDfSfC7PHbWGpT\nuiSIjtR/e0zHNMaZX69la3ea9bHkd0P0ZGI13fWqkh13rpjzZgxib1GyB5HIjtJg\nS8DM/AwZUxudQcn98ePG\n=GI1R\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree cda3e31a80aee96c2fbc7e9ffe037ab0d6ae7d09\nparent e0435afb72d37fc92e7e646f51f8a1eb26664dd7\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1780123046 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780123046 -0700\n\nAdd thread archive CLI commands (#25021)\n\n## Problem\n\nSaved threads can already be archived through app-server RPCs, but the\ncommand line did not expose direct archive or unarchive commands.\n\n## Solution\n\nAdd `codex archive <thread>` and `codex unarchive <thread>`, resolving\nUUIDs or exact thread names before calling the existing `thread/archive`\nand `thread/unarchive` RPCs. The commands support scoped remote flags so\ncallers can target remote app-server endpoints when archiving or\nunarchiving threads.\n\nThis also fixes a long-standing bug in `codex resume <thread id>` and\n`codex fork <thread id>` that I found when testing the new commands.\nThese operations shouldn't be allowed on archived sessions. They now\nfail with an error that tells the user to run `codex unarchive <thread\nid>` first.\n\n## Verification\n\nAdded app-server coverage for rejecting archived thread resume by id and\nchecking that the error includes the matching `codex unarchive <thread\nid>` command.","verified_at":"2026-05-30T06:37:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3e7baa00e43419967d90d6ad9cef40f58d5ac89f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3e7baa00e43419967d90d6ad9cef40f58d5ac89f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3e7baa00e43419967d90d6ad9cef40f58d5ac89f/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e0435afb72d37fc92e7e646f51f8a1eb26664dd7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e0435afb72d37fc92e7e646f51f8a1eb26664dd7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e0435afb72d37fc92e7e646f51f8a1eb26664dd7"}]},{"sha":"e0435afb72d37fc92e7e646f51f8a1eb26664dd7","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGUwNDM1YWZiNzJkMzdmYzkyZTdlNjQ2ZjUxZjhhMWViMjY2NjRkZDc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Dylan Hurd","email":"dylan.hurd@openai.com","date":"2026-05-30T04:35:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-30T04:35:53Z"},"message":"feat(config) experimental_request_user_input toggle (#24541)\n\n## Summary\nExperimental flag to allow toggling `request_user_input`:\n\n```\ntools.experimental_request_user_input = false\n```\n\n## Testing\n- [x] Added unit tests","tree":{"sha":"62450fd690dec064bd1754b4c4328e3460b91708","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/62450fd690dec064bd1754b4c4328e3460b91708"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e0435afb72d37fc92e7e646f51f8a1eb26664dd7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGmkpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdbwQAEa8ZmVQZ3WH+uvUb2+fOvn6\nn1avEYr0hJE7gNKj3B7zbV/jynf94CTSQHpDWJB8dSbzuz34XNp7K3uaBL+bj+Qa\nApFVTzp+N3FmnzjCLEXR5G2/nERPqOCl12u/lzLDavZMGXwARPBTX458glZmjugZ\n8Upcih9BNYJW2EqZH9xVTcMXB6WeAaGtAFPcYZFJZDkJNvzjE5DrMRY1wvr0nNp+\neEShjLrVcAH8fbxQDgmTFbGL3QHAzfkU3REmohK+myzezFh3YQSVyB9oi52c1km7\nnE4uQRKjYxvl0dj79Un1IBFxxxPAXiQ90djRLu/F6V1ENW1o/8Ww7XczTGh1Obaq\ndfntlMA819DpXMisX0fpiD4qvgpr23wzSMqms43ypuDLAIERQv5wjDvLoE+KkY1b\nFOv60X6YGV2Z52OQr4h+1k25Zf2/D4He1zobtVHMG/nLv1vgH+2z8+JOL2DvAO7X\nIWkD6RkDl88C2QrtiWEo7iAzGgxJWYo+DuGpf16MnYl1JILFc5FIf5lWMFbAV6mF\nftkOjernmyY/45EifhbSFVPpF9H2Ss57sbCumyVV2rBhTfLJDWFc7bUeFGwNruiB\n92IzwimW2KNook8XS9CT3kEF7AwRFPasrE4eZT1nYbKgcJKEzaN6dFPhE3NwsFFX\nU3e0MyJoeafodsC+DYys\n=JIjK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 62450fd690dec064bd1754b4c4328e3460b91708\nparent 00ca857d3ff6883b7334292d887601344e1bd029\nauthor Dylan Hurd <dylan.hurd@openai.com> 1780115753 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780115753 -0700\n\nfeat(config) experimental_request_user_input toggle (#24541)\n\n## Summary\nExperimental flag to allow toggling `request_user_input`:\n\n```\ntools.experimental_request_user_input = false\n```\n\n## Testing\n- [x] Added unit tests","verified_at":"2026-05-30T04:35:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e0435afb72d37fc92e7e646f51f8a1eb26664dd7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e0435afb72d37fc92e7e646f51f8a1eb26664dd7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e0435afb72d37fc92e7e646f51f8a1eb26664dd7/comments","author":{"login":"dylan-hurd-oai","id":220976066,"node_id":"U_kgDODSvTwg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/220976066?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/dylan-hurd-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dylan-hurd-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"00ca857d3ff6883b7334292d887601344e1bd029","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/00ca857d3ff6883b7334292d887601344e1bd029","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/00ca857d3ff6883b7334292d887601344e1bd029"}]},{"sha":"00ca857d3ff6883b7334292d887601344e1bd029","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDAwY2E4NTdkM2ZmNjg4M2I3MzM0MjkyZDg4NzYwMTM0NGUxYmQwMjk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Celia Chen","email":"celia@openai.com","date":"2026-05-30T01:17:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-30T01:17:38Z"},"message":"fix: Bedrock API key region fallback (#25171)\n\n## Why\n\nUsers following the Amazon Bedrock API-key setup can export\n`AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK` and `AWS_REGION`, but Codex's bearer-token\nauth path only accepted `model_providers.amazon-bedrock.aws.region`.\nThat made the documented env-based setup fail with a missing-region\nerror even though the standard AWS region environment variable was\npresent.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Updates Bedrock bearer-token region resolution to use\n`model_providers.amazon-bedrock.aws.region` first, then fall back to\n`AWS_REGION`, then `AWS_DEFAULT_REGION`.\n- Updates the missing-region error to list all supported region sources.\n- Adds focused coverage for config precedence, `AWS_REGION`,\n`AWS_DEFAULT_REGION`, and the missing-region failure.","tree":{"sha":"c3c357a02ab9f38fa8bf8431ae160f489b2bef27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c3c357a02ab9f38fa8bf8431ae160f489b2bef27"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/00ca857d3ff6883b7334292d887601344e1bd029","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGjqyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFAAQABJgKh7PgVvRrjYdWBpGDCfq\nUY6u/8YGDbY17KSj4VvXJuyZwX6BijT6DD61raA0kCnCK3LQdZ7h6+OSKlOu5jma\nDrLOKWYHWITsTliy8hxMU5vULqVOMvlPIMKHUznOrvOmx+xRBYlxOzxrtgaph2Wz\n9wyuHOHi9KMph/JmXkougG4Zih1u4WRdQnWV+FOtEQH9+xjBRA+vgncCgbdsxm2P\n1PwzfVtjMvlPGuXjtgMRXbva4jLMSYiPIFw2t8lYDTXYdMgf4k+lKzYi3o81Xpns\nD2+A2n2XvkILM6ei8OYW1ZuOnldyOwFKfeMPFHEU4DBOFNicaigFyj6K+ahUvPer\nYmNNQKqkyzKGj1x49xKlEN3pFPkZh6MiE67U6Lh4GM0cPbyOUc1GAknjEfzXUg8M\ng2LDo8bjhi3JQjO+rMUlh+uEgMEFpu6XXHPfKDNfPR5GRT+qVbmCTDLxdJeMvvud\nOvjzq4di+P6OgiB7QGzEuYL87QCblx/0J1yG2ujw3tVWq8EQMNMS1EKOYlYhN4ln\nX0XIdibSppXIWUyWUGlnqMedNZ/OdbSQu98JK7DjGdyqWRItwjovqGtlsFSrj4c5\nluaxYH4Oqxi9fy6Ob8KLU91Lh4u0CisfbX+qIcZmf4Ijpi8BAJT/yVGc0WsDjYBy\n05I4I41zUw2glserYdzw\n=tPU4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c3c357a02ab9f38fa8bf8431ae160f489b2bef27\nparent e929bb5c88545c80ec92b4a2d78dd079eb16756d\nauthor Celia Chen <celia@openai.com> 1780103858 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780103858 +0000\n\nfix: Bedrock API key region fallback (#25171)\n\n## Why\n\nUsers following the Amazon Bedrock API-key setup can export\n`AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK` and `AWS_REGION`, but Codex's bearer-token\nauth path only accepted `model_providers.amazon-bedrock.aws.region`.\nThat made the documented env-based setup fail with a missing-region\nerror even though the standard AWS region environment variable was\npresent.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Updates Bedrock bearer-token region resolution to use\n`model_providers.amazon-bedrock.aws.region` first, then fall back to\n`AWS_REGION`, then `AWS_DEFAULT_REGION`.\n- Updates the missing-region error to list all supported region sources.\n- Adds focused coverage for config precedence, `AWS_REGION`,\n`AWS_DEFAULT_REGION`, and the missing-region failure.","verified_at":"2026-05-30T01:17:38Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/00ca857d3ff6883b7334292d887601344e1bd029","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/00ca857d3ff6883b7334292d887601344e1bd029","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/00ca857d3ff6883b7334292d887601344e1bd029/comments","author":{"login":"celia-oai","id":209693228,"node_id":"U_kgDODH-qLA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/209693228?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/celia-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e929bb5c88545c80ec92b4a2d78dd079eb16756d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e929bb5c88545c80ec92b4a2d78dd079eb16756d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e929bb5c88545c80ec92b4a2d78dd079eb16756d"}]},{"sha":"e929bb5c88545c80ec92b4a2d78dd079eb16756d","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGU5MjliYjVjODg1NDVjODBlYzkyYjRhMmQ3OGRkMDc5ZWIxNjc1NmQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Ning","email":"ericning@openai.com","date":"2026-05-30T00:57:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-30T00:57:34Z"},"message":"[codex] Update remote connector suggestions (#25172)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Use the session-loaded plugin app IDs as the source of connector\nsuggestion candidates.\n- Remove the redundant plugin reload from\n`tool_suggest_connector_ids()`.\n- Add regression coverage for connectors declared by a loaded remote\nplugin, using the Databricks app case.\n\n## Context\n\nLoaded remote plugins can declare app connector IDs in `.app.json`. The\nsession-owned `PluginsManager` already loads those plugins and exposes\ntheir effective app IDs.\n\nThe connector suggestion path was creating a separate `PluginsManager`\nand recomputing plugin app IDs. That new manager does not share the\nsession manager’s remote installed plugin cache, so app IDs from loaded\nremote plugins were missing from connector suggestions.\n\n## Fix\n\nPass the already-loaded effective app IDs into connector suggestion\ngeneration and use them directly as the plugin-derived connector\ncandidate set.\n\nConnector candidates are now built from:\n\n- App IDs declared by loaded plugins\n- Explicitly configured connector discoverables\n- Existing disabled-suggestion filtering\n\nThis avoids a second plugin-manager lookup and keeps connector\nsuggestions aligned with the plugins actually loaded for the turn.\n\n## Behavior\n\nFor example, when a plugin is loaded and its `.app.json` declares data\napps, `list_available_plugins_to_install` can now return those data\nconnectors.\n\nThis does not create plugin suggestions from the plugin itself. Plugin\nsuggestions still come from eligible uninstalled entries in the\nmarketplace catalog and require existing matching/filtering rules.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- Added regression coverage for a loaded-plugin connector ID appearing\nin discoverable tools\n- Attempted `just test -p codex-core`; the command exited unsuccessfully\nin the local test environment without useful failure detail captured in\nthe run output","tree":{"sha":"7740c172e4edea153dd395f4cb4ef4173bd3fad5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/7740c172e4edea153dd395f4cb4ef4173bd3fad5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e929bb5c88545c80ec92b4a2d78dd079eb16756d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGjX+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzgcQAKIxbV4yPhmXsJer6p15p6IZ\nsF8Krer96/NZp9mJ7LRbNlIwgzOxu29eEdznqdmL3tV/ILv5ggDjDDnwy1+8mmH6\nllRBeeLM7/DZMrhko3vBB8V8v9bNu1946xLStm1qWCQ0eus52m5WSR+PaB2SMSfN\nsJi7wgakEC+GqfFVmAlGM1NLs6TXjca0JwaJOnvnmHBY8EP7AhdsRJ13WPVYxwhU\n5Bw1MXC6ROc+7m+rMHbZl2drvDcXaKPJuw3V30l0QlSfGaSVSn1RkGPA5YVRJK3n\nlOi8uSBymZRIEDgX6/Fzoohlhb8sauxq8lUo5MjMKtmlyCkO9UkIRvmGgvsABMQc\nf7tY2fSSA8yR3x79Xe65Rj3kEeeTyF1fWI759NKNtiaArfIMSnyFTCDTnZXEzbPW\njvsA5Ow9n2/0kDSrb2DBI1SNf8O0fiStvf3tGeZF6MEB0MZILWBo+EbowZIA8Pwi\nnJCeXXC1Yz3qTmwGtzKvO1RIENEg3ZKaLSiOTuysY+lM+AyuFevOPl8Fz8oGFedn\n60H/I2lbZh6wkgjpRC7/UDtvk6nCzRxvNRV0WeGSeTNehTZuMquW6MZt4DeeZpAG\nnee2Kw8GERtxNBR8T5xvwb0fAw6v7H4faxHNbufjymOBwq3AWryR6jupybIccsI6\nW8K7XhOoAWeqnGUs5/Jm\n=sOO6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7740c172e4edea153dd395f4cb4ef4173bd3fad5\nparent a5a94ee5a7447d2c0a846dbc97c2a469c115a598\nauthor Eric Ning <ericning@openai.com> 1780102654 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780102654 -0700\n\n[codex] Update remote connector suggestions (#25172)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Use the session-loaded plugin app IDs as the source of connector\nsuggestion candidates.\n- Remove the redundant plugin reload from\n`tool_suggest_connector_ids()`.\n- Add regression coverage for connectors declared by a loaded remote\nplugin, using the Databricks app case.\n\n## Context\n\nLoaded remote plugins can declare app connector IDs in `.app.json`. The\nsession-owned `PluginsManager` already loads those plugins and exposes\ntheir effective app IDs.\n\nThe connector suggestion path was creating a separate `PluginsManager`\nand recomputing plugin app IDs. That new manager does not share the\nsession manager’s remote installed plugin cache, so app IDs from loaded\nremote plugins were missing from connector suggestions.\n\n## Fix\n\nPass the already-loaded effective app IDs into connector suggestion\ngeneration and use them directly as the plugin-derived connector\ncandidate set.\n\nConnector candidates are now built from:\n\n- App IDs declared by loaded plugins\n- Explicitly configured connector discoverables\n- Existing disabled-suggestion filtering\n\nThis avoids a second plugin-manager lookup and keeps connector\nsuggestions aligned with the plugins actually loaded for the turn.\n\n## Behavior\n\nFor example, when a plugin is loaded and its `.app.json` declares data\napps, `list_available_plugins_to_install` can now return those data\nconnectors.\n\nThis does not create plugin suggestions from the plugin itself. Plugin\nsuggestions still come from eligible uninstalled entries in the\nmarketplace catalog and require existing matching/filtering rules.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- Added regression coverage for a loaded-plugin connector ID appearing\nin discoverable tools\n- Attempted `just test -p codex-core`; the command exited unsuccessfully\nin the local test environment without useful failure detail captured in\nthe run output","verified_at":"2026-05-30T00:57:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e929bb5c88545c80ec92b4a2d78dd079eb16756d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e929bb5c88545c80ec92b4a2d78dd079eb16756d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e929bb5c88545c80ec92b4a2d78dd079eb16756d/comments","author":{"login":"ericning-o","id":182030612,"node_id":"U_kgDOCtmRFA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/182030612?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o","html_url":"https://github.com/ericning-o","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a5a94ee5a7447d2c0a846dbc97c2a469c115a598","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a5a94ee5a7447d2c0a846dbc97c2a469c115a598","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a5a94ee5a7447d2c0a846dbc97c2a469c115a598"}]},{"sha":"a5a94ee5a7447d2c0a846dbc97c2a469c115a598","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGE1YTk0ZWU1YTc0NDdkMmMwYTg0NmRiYzk3YzJhNDY5YzExNWE1OTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Abhinav","email":"abhinav@openai.com","date":"2026-05-29T23:31:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T23:31:33Z"},"message":"Constrain Windows sandbox requirements (#23766)\n\n# Why\n\nManaged requirements can already constrain sandbox policy choices, but\nWindows sandbox implementation selection was still resolved\nindependently from those requirements. That left the TUI able to\ncontinue through the unelevated fallback even when an organization wants\nto require the elevated Windows sandbox implementation.\n\n# What\n\n- Add `[windows].allowed_sandbox_implementations` requirements support\nfor the Windows `elevated` and `unelevated` implementations.\n- Apply that allowlist during core config resolution so disallowed\nconfigured or feature-selected Windows sandbox implementations fall back\nto an allowed implementation with the existing requirements warning\npath.\n- Reuse the existing TUI Windows setup prompts to block disallowed\nunelevated continuation, keep required elevated setup in front of the\nuser, and refuse to persist a TUI-selected Windows sandbox mode that\nrequirements disallow.\n\n# Semantics\n\n| Allowed | Selected | Effective |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `[\"elevated\"]` | `unelevated` / unset | `elevated` |\n| `[\"unelevated\"]` | `elevated` / unset | `unelevated` |\n| `[\"elevated\", \"unelevated\"]` | `elevated` | `elevated` |\n| `[\"elevated\", \"unelevated\"]` | `unelevated` | `unelevated` |\n| `[\"elevated\", \"unelevated\"]` | unset | `elevated` |\n\nAvailability is handled by interactive setup surfaces after allowlist\nresolution. If the effective elevated implementation is not ready,\nelevated-only requirements block on setup. When unelevated is also\nallowed, the UI may offer the existing unelevated fallback.\n\n## TUI Screens\n\nIf elevated setup is not already complete:\n```\n  Your organization requires the default Codex agent sandbox to continue. Set it up to protect your files and control\n  network access.\n  Learn more <https://developers.openai.com/codex/windows>\n\n› 1. Set up default sandbox (requires Administrator permissions)\n  2. Quit\n```\n\nIf admin setup fails under `[\"elevated\"]`:\n```\n  Couldn't set up your sandbox with Administrator permissions\n\n  Your organization requires the default sandbox before Codex can continue.\n  Learn more <https://developers.openai.com/codex/windows>\n\n› 1. Try setting up admin sandbox again\n  2. Quit\n```\n\n# Next Steps\n\n\n- extend the requirements/readout surface, such as\n`configRequirements/read`, so clients can inspect the loaded\n`[windows].allowed_sandbox_implementations` requirement instead of\ninferring it from Windows setup state\n- consider extending `windowsSandbox/readiness` as well\n- update the App startup guide, setup flow, and banner surfaces so an\nelevated-only requirement omits any continue-unelevated escape hatch and\nblocks startup until a permitted implementation is ready;\n- preserve the existing unelevated fallback path when requirements allow\nit, including the `[\"unelevated\"]` case where elevated is disallowed","tree":{"sha":"af533357d3e0b394e5f1c704f710dd6f1e239279","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/af533357d3e0b394e5f1c704f710dd6f1e239279"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a5a94ee5a7447d2c0a846dbc97c2a469c115a598","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGiHVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAS1EQAENepWJMf0JRgIiRhe2f721y\nRwcQ0r00tSdtIUpHFJxtZaoJ/VwTvLBVhBBkBI2EfSK5+DbBmGaW2F6Ju+iB+DpV\nx0RKEOmIemxS3tp2bdVse+laWjF1Mblo4ZIkcuGDmUVDcWuF0OOBTESf6DDSOMcv\ndHjiQgnWFJE6EQAhQrZ7lwRrvKIhQMFaNyqEGlB73mQmy0+5vqT/DZwMuaDcxxLS\nzRFRoXmwJ9/GBpNyuyRg9PeoCUmzX+doKYKuNzTEgjd/lPLOOukOaNRDZKUkXbf7\n7ZnxSBR8XZ/dF5PXhxwUTdAFqadE0doRs3R/4IZMnt58JGUxhs8ydElKyhsCRnWD\nUcQqwMT3ejd8it34I5kxdhjVzhAmRzKCZK1xwi92loRG0NB1uMP4nh6UDAojgRQH\nmQ2w93N3X72FlbNilEgEMSSXaw0cXA56YWCmmb9lrtWkUbXFjZMUBXe82fygwrbu\nJJeZn+AgovmihVKvMdnDpN3ntx+sLyP46nbz6LhvB1/zYgmoihzum2EFzh8sl+lv\nK11FhzgfoirGBz2rxsUtDBBJ8rk8eY32f1kecF3T1QnTPQu7g53W0Fu0YQ0DFADP\nx5vfZhB11aFlrq6b7k9DPTaDdMCOLS8vlkmdnUkpSdGx28G/AXPWPKsD3lUByRcU\nl5dDjwp2DKqe/qd7Vk7a\n=VBXD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree af533357d3e0b394e5f1c704f710dd6f1e239279\nparent 8e5f5616976d98c5e035b7f67fe0632e3a4337bf\nauthor Abhinav <abhinav@openai.com> 1780097493 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780097493 -0700\n\nConstrain Windows sandbox requirements (#23766)\n\n# Why\n\nManaged requirements can already constrain sandbox policy choices, but\nWindows sandbox implementation selection was still resolved\nindependently from those requirements. That left the TUI able to\ncontinue through the unelevated fallback even when an organization wants\nto require the elevated Windows sandbox implementation.\n\n# What\n\n- Add `[windows].allowed_sandbox_implementations` requirements support\nfor the Windows `elevated` and `unelevated` implementations.\n- Apply that allowlist during core config resolution so disallowed\nconfigured or feature-selected Windows sandbox implementations fall back\nto an allowed implementation with the existing requirements warning\npath.\n- Reuse the existing TUI Windows setup prompts to block disallowed\nunelevated continuation, keep required elevated setup in front of the\nuser, and refuse to persist a TUI-selected Windows sandbox mode that\nrequirements disallow.\n\n# Semantics\n\n| Allowed | Selected | Effective |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `[\"elevated\"]` | `unelevated` / unset | `elevated` |\n| `[\"unelevated\"]` | `elevated` / unset | `unelevated` |\n| `[\"elevated\", \"unelevated\"]` | `elevated` | `elevated` |\n| `[\"elevated\", \"unelevated\"]` | `unelevated` | `unelevated` |\n| `[\"elevated\", \"unelevated\"]` | unset | `elevated` |\n\nAvailability is handled by interactive setup surfaces after allowlist\nresolution. If the effective elevated implementation is not ready,\nelevated-only requirements block on setup. When unelevated is also\nallowed, the UI may offer the existing unelevated fallback.\n\n## TUI Screens\n\nIf elevated setup is not already complete:\n```\n  Your organization requires the default Codex agent sandbox to continue. Set it up to protect your files and control\n  network access.\n  Learn more <https://developers.openai.com/codex/windows>\n\n› 1. Set up default sandbox (requires Administrator permissions)\n  2. Quit\n```\n\nIf admin setup fails under `[\"elevated\"]`:\n```\n  Couldn't set up your sandbox with Administrator permissions\n\n  Your organization requires the default sandbox before Codex can continue.\n  Learn more <https://developers.openai.com/codex/windows>\n\n› 1. Try setting up admin sandbox again\n  2. Quit\n```\n\n# Next Steps\n\n\n- extend the requirements/readout surface, such as\n`configRequirements/read`, so clients can inspect the loaded\n`[windows].allowed_sandbox_implementations` requirement instead of\ninferring it from Windows setup state\n- consider extending `windowsSandbox/readiness` as well\n- update the App startup guide, setup flow, and banner surfaces so an\nelevated-only requirement omits any continue-unelevated escape hatch and\nblocks startup until a permitted implementation is ready;\n- preserve the existing unelevated fallback path when requirements allow\nit, including the `[\"unelevated\"]` case where elevated is disallowed","verified_at":"2026-05-29T23:31:34Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a5a94ee5a7447d2c0a846dbc97c2a469c115a598","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a5a94ee5a7447d2c0a846dbc97c2a469c115a598","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a5a94ee5a7447d2c0a846dbc97c2a469c115a598/comments","author":{"login":"abhinav-oai","id":274334565,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFoDZQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274334565?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/abhinav-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8e5f5616976d98c5e035b7f67fe0632e3a4337bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8e5f5616976d98c5e035b7f67fe0632e3a4337bf","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8e5f5616976d98c5e035b7f67fe0632e3a4337bf"}]},{"sha":"8e5f5616976d98c5e035b7f67fe0632e3a4337bf","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhlNWY1NjE2OTc2ZDk4YzVlMDM1YjdmNjdmZTA2MzJlM2E0MzM3YmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Noah MacCallum","email":"171723556+nm-openai@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-05-29T22:32:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T22:32:04Z"},"message":"Filter plugin install suggestions by installed apps (#24996)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Keep the original `TOOL_SUGGEST_DISCOVERABLE_PLUGIN_ALLOWLIST` as a\nfallback seed list, so users with no installed plugins still get initial\ninstall suggestions.\n- Allow additional install suggestions from trusted marketplaces:\n`openai-curated` and `openai-bundled`.\n- Require non-fallback, non-configured marketplace candidates to share\n`.app.json` connector IDs with already installed plugins.\n- Preserve explicit configured plugin discoverables as an override,\nwhile still omitting installed, disabled, and `NOT_AVAILABLE` plugins.\n\n## Context\n\n`list_available_plugins_to_install` controls which plugins the model can\ntrigger via `request_plugin_install`. We want a small starter set for\nempty/new users, but we also want installed workflow plugins to unlock\nrelevant source plugins without maintaining every source plugin ID by\nhand.\n\nThis keeps the legacy plugin ID allowlist only as the starter fallback.\nFor everything else, the trusted marketplace is the candidate boundary,\nand installed app connector overlap is the relevance filter. For\nexample, an installed Sales plugin can make HubSpot and Granola\nsuggestible when those source plugins are in `openai-curated` and share\nSales app connector IDs, while an unrelated test-source plugin with an\napp connector not declared by Sales stays hidden.\n\n## Test Coverage\n\n- Empty/no-installed-plugin case: returns the fallback seed plugins from\nthe original allowlist.\n- Installed-app expansion: returns non-fallback marketplace plugins only\nwhen their app connector IDs overlap with an installed plugin.\n- Sales workflow case: installed Sales declares HubSpot and Granola\napps, so `hubspot@openai-curated` and `granola@openai-curated` are\nreturned.\n- Sales negative case: `test-source@openai-curated` has an app connector\nnot declared by Sales, so it is not returned.\n- Existing guardrails: installed plugins, disabled suggestions, and\n`NOT_AVAILABLE` plugins remain omitted; explicit configured\ndiscoverables still work as an override.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core plugins::discoverable::tests`\n- `just test -p codex-core` was attempted earlier, but current `main` /\nlocal env failed with unrelated existing failures around missing\n`test_stdio_server`, CLI/code-mode MCP tool setup, and\nunified_exec/shell snapshot flakes/timeouts. The touched discoverable\ntests pass.","tree":{"sha":"980d2e59587b9ad0b7ce06f190c67c9a5b1ac938","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/980d2e59587b9ad0b7ce06f190c67c9a5b1ac938"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8e5f5616976d98c5e035b7f67fe0632e3a4337bf","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGhPkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAd7EQAGCcwIk12QZiFpB5yim+/rON\nnDljlq8LeuzbomrxVlvokeL572J6yMPcze/2cAQjLCvOx0X4PlGnX8jCVAEFkgXb\nkcJI2+4TV3N4fjh+I28QCQFYwgEuTWsr1+iu5scV6lMQGZ/NU3oblyMU+PHM+zNV\nEKwbRtNWlxGObZbZtRClmyvB3ebwS6GGfECkOHxVy32Dh75a0MhBgXr3PCa5z73K\nPsGrXa9eCPP28WQbJ0zScNQQzbp/L/yg1HU5a6eiRLmjivJRPrXLctJUpNmhF4dL\nlrcKH5Y3az8Y0QhrIOLnQS3jj3KeepmCy414I1DCvc55dxJI1ZDFgjeiLZh0hEQp\nSeBEVhty2lgx42Uya67P7YdLt+ZxXb0fN5G/OS4Nz3tKgiHLyFwrYqn3sSY7/Pjl\nnR06nsBFF77E3XfiNC53tiUXpw/kcANEyQ+q36dMpg22EkJon/KlViWmHwI2ePYG\nldGvBsRV0QMCDgouX1fXmdD5ZXD5QO5PrbOfaxMZZXT8fNUY79/OGSlc8Ye4TX/B\ntIhGbb4qHPSKP6+BQ32yWVeQpvxGGCrdLw0bLcmlL1ykekNSbWnYIQfbNA1ZMKUN\nIgbQTEjYth1e10ILitXzdtU5CJrqHrx+VA6bM76GIE8J0JYjzEwWuAtik6pp2cFZ\nXmz3Rju+w+ImLyN+245B\n=lGeS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 980d2e59587b9ad0b7ce06f190c67c9a5b1ac938\nparent a076b21730c7f0c8445c3f7b09580e7608ce1166\nauthor Noah MacCallum <171723556+nm-openai@users.noreply.github.com> 1780093924 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780093924 -0700\n\nFilter plugin install suggestions by installed apps (#24996)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Keep the original `TOOL_SUGGEST_DISCOVERABLE_PLUGIN_ALLOWLIST` as a\nfallback seed list, so users with no installed plugins still get initial\ninstall suggestions.\n- Allow additional install suggestions from trusted marketplaces:\n`openai-curated` and `openai-bundled`.\n- Require non-fallback, non-configured marketplace candidates to share\n`.app.json` connector IDs with already installed plugins.\n- Preserve explicit configured plugin discoverables as an override,\nwhile still omitting installed, disabled, and `NOT_AVAILABLE` plugins.\n\n## Context\n\n`list_available_plugins_to_install` controls which plugins the model can\ntrigger via `request_plugin_install`. We want a small starter set for\nempty/new users, but we also want installed workflow plugins to unlock\nrelevant source plugins without maintaining every source plugin ID by\nhand.\n\nThis keeps the legacy plugin ID allowlist only as the starter fallback.\nFor everything else, the trusted marketplace is the candidate boundary,\nand installed app connector overlap is the relevance filter. For\nexample, an installed Sales plugin can make HubSpot and Granola\nsuggestible when those source plugins are in `openai-curated` and share\nSales app connector IDs, while an unrelated test-source plugin with an\napp connector not declared by Sales stays hidden.\n\n## Test Coverage\n\n- Empty/no-installed-plugin case: returns the fallback seed plugins from\nthe original allowlist.\n- Installed-app expansion: returns non-fallback marketplace plugins only\nwhen their app connector IDs overlap with an installed plugin.\n- Sales workflow case: installed Sales declares HubSpot and Granola\napps, so `hubspot@openai-curated` and `granola@openai-curated` are\nreturned.\n- Sales negative case: `test-source@openai-curated` has an app connector\nnot declared by Sales, so it is not returned.\n- Existing guardrails: installed plugins, disabled suggestions, and\n`NOT_AVAILABLE` plugins remain omitted; explicit configured\ndiscoverables still work as an override.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core plugins::discoverable::tests`\n- `just test -p codex-core` was attempted earlier, but current `main` /\nlocal env failed with unrelated existing failures around missing\n`test_stdio_server`, CLI/code-mode MCP tool setup, and\nunified_exec/shell snapshot flakes/timeouts. The touched discoverable\ntests pass.","verified_at":"2026-05-29T22:32:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8e5f5616976d98c5e035b7f67fe0632e3a4337bf","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8e5f5616976d98c5e035b7f67fe0632e3a4337bf","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8e5f5616976d98c5e035b7f67fe0632e3a4337bf/comments","author":{"login":"nm-openai","id":171723556,"node_id":"U_kgDOCjxLJA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/171723556?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nm-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/nm-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nm-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nm-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nm-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nm-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nm-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.git