e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/eb1c649cd2cd8f107478f4c558b1f041ec5729ee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a076b21730c7f0c8445c3f7b09580e7608ce1166","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGhIpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAXgQAD6s2etWjZd1HSRGWgXYGrDx\nxUJvJaB8Wqs4w8Z2rAmhE8fUEv6keKB0rz0pzKXI0cWXlDc2nEBkmBharmO9/N4W\nNjpn7bJ3nH441pVPs4lDAkljxyC2HcYvBNGQPCvBjoswMTI0WQIPjyklf5L19M9a\nEhAq8h3l02mZ3pXDeD8OqGmj/k5NJPCqkwpoVicNPzXET5cROLkZxk2usGhcJtks\nYDEdvoyolXfKOE2IKZARA4rakpsAZ1gKr81OO7hGDyx+vNz69dKaDtzHUwh4lG+j\nBbxKi5fkhIm1LT1HLgvSkZ6T8lqSy87XbIwUZPR2p3Att4pD8Rh764tyV9mk9DXY\ntc/lo/eHivNr7sTNexqNSxwvMl62fx1jruac0QBR7BVyk3k2pYv+0w4TK5slhWJK\nAJ+DrMwAQyYG9EptOGCjqXccbDo7gIvjO3ZKdYWTqMbkSibzMusvBMVc5C5kUbpT\ndIHd+aVuqLDd1oQC2/1fuQ5hRGe4cFwl4DB3Crtt1BkcPPGFfW/ScGwUqr1POsY7\nId7CQFyDTFhLU8Foptn76AXFl89o8t4sPb6siX2doNSUT9QYBSOYePXod37KfGkx\n3lKC6Jt410utgLG/I57/xahpzf52HD+AaRoHBvGljqc525m0SCyOsUms15ZjZj3K\ntxDcDPdbH8OTdhVwrXQD\n=l30U\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree eb1c649cd2cd8f107478f4c558b1f041ec5729ee\nparent f2e7b462a932c654f8c9810387a73c12bd4e198f\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1780093481 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780093481 -0700\n\nRecommend Bazel VSCode extension. (#25161)\n\nProvides starlark syntax highlighting and editor formatting.","verified_at":"2026-05-29T22:24:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a076b21730c7f0c8445c3f7b09580e7608ce1166","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a076b21730c7f0c8445c3f7b09580e7608ce1166","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a076b21730c7f0c8445c3f7b09580e7608ce1166/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f2e7b462a932c654f8c9810387a73c12bd4e198f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f2e7b462a932c654f8c9810387a73c12bd4e198f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f2e7b462a932c654f8c9810387a73c12bd4e198f"}]},{"sha":"f2e7b462a932c654f8c9810387a73c12bd4e198f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGYyZTdiNDYyYTkzMmM2NTRmOGM5ODEwMzg3YTczYzEyYmQ0ZTE5OGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jinghan Xu","email":"jinghanx@openai.com","date":"2026-05-29T21:01:27Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T21:01:27Z"},"message":"[codex] Fix Vim normal mode editing (#25022)\n\n## Summary\n- add Vim normal-mode `s` support to substitute the character under the\ncursor and enter insert mode\n- fix Vim normal-mode `o` so opening below the final line moves the\ncursor onto the new blank line\n- update keymap config/schema and keymap picker snapshots for the new\naction\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `just write-config-schema`\n- `just test -p codex-config`\n- focused `just test -p codex-tui` coverage for the Vim `s` and `o`\nbehavior, keymap conflict handling, and keymap picker snapshots\n- `cargo insta pending-snapshots --manifest-path tui/Cargo.toml`\n- `git diff --check`\n\n## Notes\nA full `just test -p codex-tui` run still has two unrelated Guardian\nfeature-flag failures in this checkout:\n-\n`app::tests::update_feature_flags_disabling_guardian_clears_review_policy_and_restores_default`\n-\n`app::tests::update_feature_flags_disabling_guardian_clears_manual_review_policy_without_history`","tree":{"sha":"ae888642fcdc04c11b0737e0f1b6d59417a76343","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/ae888642fcdc04c11b0737e0f1b6d59417a76343"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f2e7b462a932c654f8c9810387a73c12bd4e198f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGf6nCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/9gQAFyn1DMwzCGCbxWTeqXRoS2v\noIXQmCet/hN9iosrSq0DA564hceVAW+SISngP92ZbeooqMZM2sumjiHjQ90hrZrh\nE4tUEfLLeANsizNIJ+gASjQiinIgLgeM1Z6Ov2/vASNZa6orSej+iqp1aDeDDFOv\nqe4vsILnbS1kHj74E+eH4sbuhiQ8O2r7KI8BWItsEm1kiq0vlooMPyrn0+CmmgWL\nu7+GoKBHGXRQCDMq2T6xjvCyZGnzMW6P++8hntczzy4tSFb6fqaso2YoWFX8QbwH\nKdrzZO0otlmQCfj8WVC4VTzwQ9F8+IzfavvNt+ZjE18zMMS3ZbZNElr8QU4o0dGX\np3C1AnXLAT03BTtBhkCsJXJJ3Mf8DURmbguNbEeaLN8Nvb0zQu1zpsHvMEfFasIB\nFZzqON8ofYw+gYDorLwd5Y+5eO1IUBE4xVqKCDT/YUNGwbQ2iX60yR2d8W4ewIxE\n97xs8NSVrKEIzim/0DAonnWVOaTQclrgDvnSESz3i5i59ULZ+hjuWP9O3FHEraso\nzdxFbc2gTyGREIvePNkg1XCMJBvAkos7BhmksVfPgGpC6VQEy3s8nMdgNBLlEAvP\nS0ENd0D4117xifuGQ8oKChYZL1z145FZTtReYNOe8DHVPUBbchuwQXKWELALdj+j\nHvZcjmVriGZ+J03S00De\n=B0ya\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ae888642fcdc04c11b0737e0f1b6d59417a76343\nparent a717e4ef31f64feab49b6d857f1b5b1e027ff254\nauthor Jinghan Xu <jinghanx@openai.com> 1780088487 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780088487 -0700\n\n[codex] Fix Vim normal mode editing (#25022)\n\n## Summary\n- add Vim normal-mode `s` support to substitute the character under the\ncursor and enter insert mode\n- fix Vim normal-mode `o` so opening below the final line moves the\ncursor onto the new blank line\n- update keymap config/schema and keymap picker snapshots for the new\naction\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `just write-config-schema`\n- `just test -p codex-config`\n- focused `just test -p codex-tui` coverage for the Vim `s` and `o`\nbehavior, keymap conflict handling, and keymap picker snapshots\n- `cargo insta pending-snapshots --manifest-path tui/Cargo.toml`\n- `git diff --check`\n\n## Notes\nA full `just test -p codex-tui` run still has two unrelated Guardian\nfeature-flag failures in this checkout:\n-\n`app::tests::update_feature_flags_disabling_guardian_clears_review_policy_and_restores_default`\n-\n`app::tests::update_feature_flags_disabling_guardian_clears_manual_review_policy_without_history`","verified_at":"2026-05-29T21:01:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f2e7b462a932c654f8c9810387a73c12bd4e198f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f2e7b462a932c654f8c9810387a73c12bd4e198f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f2e7b462a932c654f8c9810387a73c12bd4e198f/comments","author":{"login":"jinghanx88","id":284132297,"node_id":"U_kgDOEO-DyQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/284132297?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinghanx88","html_url":"https://github.com/jinghanx88","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinghanx88/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinghanx88/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinghanx88/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinghanx88/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinghanx88/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinghanx88/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinghanx88/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinghanx88/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jinghanx88/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a717e4ef31f64feab49b6d857f1b5b1e027ff254","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a717e4ef31f64feab49b6d857f1b5b1e027ff254","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a717e4ef31f64feab49b6d857f1b5b1e027ff254"}]},{"sha":"a717e4ef31f64feab49b6d857f1b5b1e027ff254","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGE3MTdlNGVmMzFmNjRmZWFiNDliNmQ4NTdmMWI1YjFlMDI3ZmYyNTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"starr-openai","email":"starr@openai.com","date":"2026-05-29T19:20:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T19:20:17Z"},"message":"exec-server: preserve fs helper CoreFoundation env (#25118)\n\n## Summary\n- preserve macOS `__CF_USER_TEXT_ENCODING` when launching the sandboxed\nfs helper\n- keep the fs-helper env narrow; this adds only the CoreFoundation\nstartup var instead of copying the broader MCP stdio baseline\n- add focused coverage that the helper keeps that var without admitting\n`HOME`\n\n## Diagnosis\nThe sandboxed fs helper is not launched like a normal child process.\nExec-server rebuilds its environment from an allowlist, then calls\n`env_clear()` before re-execing Codex with `--codex-run-as-fs-helper`.\nThat helper dispatches before the normal Codex startup path and only\nneeds to boot a small Tokio runtime, read one JSON request from stdin,\nperform the direct filesystem operation, and write one JSON response.\n\nThe reported macOS hang sampled the helper before Rust main, in\nCoreFoundation initialization while resolving the default text encoding:\n`_CFStringGetUserDefaultEncoding -> getpwuid_r -> notify_register_check\n-> bootstrap_look_up3 -> mach_msg2_trap`. The fs-helper allowlist kept\n`PATH` and temp vars for runtime needs, but it dropped macOS\n`__CF_USER_TEXT_ENCODING`. Other Codex subprocess launchers that\nintentionally build a minimal Unix baseline, such as MCP stdio, already\npreserve that variable.\n\nMy read is that stripping `__CF_USER_TEXT_ENCODING` forced this internal\nhelper down CoreFoundation's fallback user-lookup path, and that lookup\nintermittently wedged on the affected machine before the helper could\nread stdin or touch the target file. Preserving only this macOS startup\nvariable avoids that fallback without broadening the fs-helper\nenvironment to shell-like vars such as `HOME`, `USER`, locale settings,\nterminal settings, or proxy credentials.\n\nInternal Slack thread omitted from the public PR body.\n\n## Validation\n- `cd codex-rs && just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`","tree":{"sha":"6175208ad3aa0ab64d65a8d17d0f71b387f56df1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6175208ad3aa0ab64d65a8d17d0f71b387f56df1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a717e4ef31f64feab49b6d857f1b5b1e027ff254","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGebxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqRMQAH+cGc4ycSoehW9c5zh5P0hG\nXyyFDvVDkImhPzatYTuXqlUlt6nqwlrn/UZ/0ywA0/5OpUKqr76eCG57jSOfCrnt\nbSYPUCMPCf+FS4iLC+Oc5F/rg3xloJX5HJU/PKZXwOT/zRfQuedCsMnx2QTn+hhl\ny+vxVMUy9BNpcVDi3C+LFkKErLU9cp0nkcKUy9mF4bVGnHudwvD8HgsOaThD6/4W\n0gMTi1hJv7cPdPlSvh+AxyW4jbvE5i336mbDOGCWNdUp/rGl8YyxKwcLRzJ/e8rv\n0iFm20AugCBv5IFuWDcJ/gZStGOlImKjyhvK9d54Ccij+m/FlUJBq0/fDGQ9FlZn\nVuxtXZhd/+Q2fayXKUlu/z5dSIkULoTMGNKJFqiMUUNpsiba3tAxwxN+CwmVJSv3\nCcT6DzUaCf2OeS8dNNLwuRKpb+rx0DO54+0aPfDRGx0tl0ZWjR7Q/Y+5tecsu/Q4\nu8v7L+VlHkqSC95qR/Q+e9fvFpvAFJExWHo5fKAVN50YqVUyiaVVlEtGQoTIDF4/\nFrXeAHnp3v6CZpMlXafCJHOhDIC4yBUMRqwmj2Vi/UR1qfofgSwL0y7/DWaw0DHH\nzOwNfvUgOg23oWOrhY5O6/ts7pFr5TODFTiwp/mia3wYd3jDCss2kNW9iJVsAoLa\nozplJ3iAE4Dl3u4pRK89\n=KoDu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6175208ad3aa0ab64d65a8d17d0f71b387f56df1\nparent 20da4c37c5a56f168118b4b1573b8bf749d3bece\nauthor starr-openai <starr@openai.com> 1780082417 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780082417 -0700\n\nexec-server: preserve fs helper CoreFoundation env (#25118)\n\n## Summary\n- preserve macOS `__CF_USER_TEXT_ENCODING` when launching the sandboxed\nfs helper\n- keep the fs-helper env narrow; this adds only the CoreFoundation\nstartup var instead of copying the broader MCP stdio baseline\n- add focused coverage that the helper keeps that var without admitting\n`HOME`\n\n## Diagnosis\nThe sandboxed fs helper is not launched like a normal child process.\nExec-server rebuilds its environment from an allowlist, then calls\n`env_clear()` before re-execing Codex with `--codex-run-as-fs-helper`.\nThat helper dispatches before the normal Codex startup path and only\nneeds to boot a small Tokio runtime, read one JSON request from stdin,\nperform the direct filesystem operation, and write one JSON response.\n\nThe reported macOS hang sampled the helper before Rust main, in\nCoreFoundation initialization while resolving the default text encoding:\n`_CFStringGetUserDefaultEncoding -> getpwuid_r -> notify_register_check\n-> bootstrap_look_up3 -> mach_msg2_trap`. The fs-helper allowlist kept\n`PATH` and temp vars for runtime needs, but it dropped macOS\n`__CF_USER_TEXT_ENCODING`. Other Codex subprocess launchers that\nintentionally build a minimal Unix baseline, such as MCP stdio, already\npreserve that variable.\n\nMy read is that stripping `__CF_USER_TEXT_ENCODING` forced this internal\nhelper down CoreFoundation's fallback user-lookup path, and that lookup\nintermittently wedged on the affected machine before the helper could\nread stdin or touch the target file. Preserving only this macOS startup\nvariable avoids that fallback without broadening the fs-helper\nenvironment to shell-like vars such as `HOME`, `USER`, locale settings,\nterminal settings, or proxy credentials.\n\nInternal Slack thread omitted from the public PR body.\n\n## Validation\n- `cd codex-rs && just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`","verified_at":"2026-05-29T19:20:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a717e4ef31f64feab49b6d857f1b5b1e027ff254","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a717e4ef31f64feab49b6d857f1b5b1e027ff254","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a717e4ef31f64feab49b6d857f1b5b1e027ff254/comments","author":{"login":"starr-openai","id":176426273,"node_id":"U_kgDOCoQNIQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176426273?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/starr-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/starr-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"20da4c37c5a56f168118b4b1573b8bf749d3bece","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/20da4c37c5a56f168118b4b1573b8bf749d3bece","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/20da4c37c5a56f168118b4b1573b8bf749d3bece"}]},{"sha":"20da4c37c5a56f168118b4b1573b8bf749d3bece","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDIwZGE0YzM3YzVhNTZmMTY4MTE4YjRiMTU3M2I4YmY3NDlkM2JlY2U","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-05-29T19:06:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T19:06:55Z"},"message":"ci: use issue triage environment for issue workflows (#25134)\n\n## Summary\n\nThis adds `environment: issue-triage` to the Codex-calling issue\nworkflow jobs so they can read the GitHub Environment Secret while\nstaying on GitHub-hosted runners for public issue-triggered workflows.","tree":{"sha":"0ff96f39abf5a4ed7769727dc2314e1719f999a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/0ff96f39abf5a4ed7769727dc2314e1719f999a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/20da4c37c5a56f168118b4b1573b8bf749d3bece","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGePPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXv0QADlwemWrRLSAz4k58eVrL8Hl\nSNNVp/GL/mOTZUcPXEoQce3/a26y7DLDDA4RaUyogFCtwXWBoTEo2UTKF9N5BTUJ\n+/Y6qChnkariOrt/5qgZ8YlbJlISgxQPV+vJwBJ7Gk4sPkNVvuTX0GqCveA8VFlc\nwqHpdP3bzAlBqKPUS+/oOgMXnFZV94CgHo2sv2NDAlGFTo7KNF6BzXAQyK3EZm6O\nhG7Jkqz5iy7u/JTwFZy4bI0c5PPCkfuZv3/lSGXodJ3vhxG7MXq5t5djvAzMqEuY\nJAfofAkQDkOMURjrPKpT6+TLe4I50t8jSg4PgXFuFnvzIaZp31JCYPlfCbsz8sf7\nR6zlyTg/tzpqvwiJa8Ev98OddZWTdW+WX+IkqiLP9+0IKj3cEDib5RN+mk969OKG\nDqCCwFjtUc6V9YLloAczfnbLMeR7NmVkDtctYK36MJf9qo+oQKKEWNtlVLlPoSqM\nEY3oMW5tazBxo+yxZdeyH0qdpyqObJWpZSXn4/685lxsBfOB4Uz1qEe+lZLZKP2u\nJ6kJ2kM9IiCJnvNQnq/alGQ+uBb7i1Li2AGRbQ1DKoV3O8oWsRTxZowf7rFKvy6I\nGrEyZl7p49eEasoSEQ3gfw+vSJczeTCi4Ef6zZ71f4PgdpLRhoZoY9bcevHc3ICC\nQpbyFMeGciQ/SEvIKKdQ\n=Blm7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0ff96f39abf5a4ed7769727dc2314e1719f999a6\nparent 1f93706e994d3f39a9155dff5d41c4141dc67c4c\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1780081615 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780081615 -0700\n\nci: use issue triage environment for issue workflows (#25134)\n\n## Summary\n\nThis adds `environment: issue-triage` to the Codex-calling issue\nworkflow jobs so they can read the GitHub Environment Secret while\nstaying on GitHub-hosted runners for public issue-triggered workflows.","verified_at":"2026-05-29T19:06:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/20da4c37c5a56f168118b4b1573b8bf749d3bece","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/20da4c37c5a56f168118b4b1573b8bf749d3bece","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/20da4c37c5a56f168118b4b1573b8bf749d3bece/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1f93706e994d3f39a9155dff5d41c4141dc67c4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1f93706e994d3f39a9155dff5d41c4141dc67c4c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1f93706e994d3f39a9155dff5d41c4141dc67c4c"}]},{"sha":"1f93706e994d3f39a9155dff5d41c4141dc67c4c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDFmOTM3MDZlOTk0ZDNmMzlhOTE1NWRmZjVkNDFjNDE0MWRjNjdjNGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"sayan-oai","email":"sayan@openai.com","date":"2026-05-29T19:03:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T19:03:04Z"},"message":"[codex] Require model for standalone web search (#25131)\n\n## Why\n\nThe standalone `/v1/alpha/search` request now requires a `model`, but\nthe `web.run` extension currently omits it.\n\nAdds `model` to extension `ToolCall` invocation.\n\nFollow-up to #23823.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Make `SearchRequest.model` required.\n- Expose the effective per-turn model on extension tool calls and pass\nit in standalone web-search requests.\n- Assert the model is forwarded in the app-server round-trip test.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-api -p codex-tools -p codex-web-search-extension\n-p codex-memories-extension -p codex-goal-extension`\n- `just test -p codex-core -E\n'test(passes_turn_fields_and_scoped_turn_item_emitter_to_extension_call)'`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server -E\n'test(standalone_web_search_round_trips_encrypted_output)'`","tree":{"sha":"ca7d152479aa111f44af40fc004a051493cb973b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/ca7d152479aa111f44af40fc004a051493cb973b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/1f93706e994d3f39a9155dff5d41c4141dc67c4c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGeLoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0rIQACqJCtaY/MFM5R22ZLHMA93i\nYTMpo4kJddueMINAmqfTo8MTp4EJcH6/b8rapR3UxIXoQRSZyyFQm6CX/tzHnme/\nL56x0p+E7XHCGxGjgQh/RQXnVrsLe9MxQEOJBQFXoT0gmRBkXDino3FkS/QWJuwX\nKtY2Bdyn4Fo2ZX5pW7JOowvInFRvBsPzHcPybdI/bB0q3aBu9UtkXJacHd0FdOZ1\nwHMepdZ6Fdne8Ud5imrHv0AOF47o8VRFEpWgai+Vs8+wj5+NotEuP+dtDPJ74vOE\n+uojcGeUUTrFIA6SWweJBRVKXIZrPSeXLkDjOI0jzO9klhkm0KVxPsFFxxgF7wCW\nBXT5QxgpzrxV7ehHvEMjCJ9TRQo0Dr2A3GLglfewFqEFuQaVpeMnWHtiCmHjSZOS\ncJFvseodhHxbWW5PrPMFlOIO4m03NOCpKPpiiAJiPr9XPYJLiyX0H/nAxcYUGDh0\nqpGyatX+GoqpMGRuhRdmGMZtFI1XyC6LHrKUGDRCwqmZDepZXaRI2PqJtmo+vgG2\nYN9N1Lp/65AlMh9rAjt15qsBdttluLDF2TpCP0mlqaEwN/PmPRf3BNy/hHLLMrpy\ncFl0+xhsfC0i9BEcoDZziQoA4/6uXeyyneXbuZ58DzHMstPYoSGk+BP2jQUUuTR0\ntf7YMHORi5gufecoL7VO\n=Ewmf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ca7d152479aa111f44af40fc004a051493cb973b\nparent a1ecf0cf1c25985b2c0e01103b7ddf8cf9fcc051\nauthor sayan-oai <sayan@openai.com> 1780081384 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780081384 -0700\n\n[codex] Require model for standalone web search (#25131)\n\n## Why\n\nThe standalone `/v1/alpha/search` request now requires a `model`, but\nthe `web.run` extension currently omits it.\n\nAdds `model` to extension `ToolCall` invocation.\n\nFollow-up to #23823.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Make `SearchRequest.model` required.\n- Expose the effective per-turn model on extension tool calls and pass\nit in standalone web-search requests.\n- Assert the model is forwarded in the app-server round-trip test.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-api -p codex-tools -p codex-web-search-extension\n-p codex-memories-extension -p codex-goal-extension`\n- `just test -p codex-core -E\n'test(passes_turn_fields_and_scoped_turn_item_emitter_to_extension_call)'`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server -E\n'test(standalone_web_search_round_trips_encrypted_output)'`","verified_at":"2026-05-29T19:03:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1f93706e994d3f39a9155dff5d41c4141dc67c4c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1f93706e994d3f39a9155dff5d41c4141dc67c4c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1f93706e994d3f39a9155dff5d41c4141dc67c4c/comments","author":{"login":"sayan-oai","id":244841968,"node_id":"U_kgDODpf98A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244841968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/sayan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a1ecf0cf1c25985b2c0e01103b7ddf8cf9fcc051","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a1ecf0cf1c25985b2c0e01103b7ddf8cf9fcc051","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a1ecf0cf1c25985b2c0e01103b7ddf8cf9fcc051"}]},{"sha":"a1ecf0cf1c25985b2c0e01103b7ddf8cf9fcc051","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGExZWNmMGNmMWMyNTk4NWIyYzBlMDExMDNiN2RkZjhjZjlmY2MwNTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-05-29T18:55:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T18:55:31Z"},"message":"thread-store: store permission profiles (#23165)\n\n## Why\n\n`SandboxPolicy` is the legacy compatibility shape, but\n`codex-thread-store` still exposed it through `StoredThread`,\n`ThreadMetadataPatch`, and live metadata sync. That kept thread-store\nconsumers tied to the legacy representation and meant richer permission\nprofile data could not round-trip through thread metadata or cold\nrollout reconciliation.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Replaced thread-store `sandbox_policy` API fields with canonical\n`PermissionProfile` fields.\n- Persist new permission-profile metadata as canonical JSON in the\nexisting SQLite metadata slot while continuing to read older legacy\nsandbox policy values.\n- Updated local, in-memory, live metadata sync, and rollout extraction\npaths to propagate `TurnContextItem::permission_profile()`.\n- Re-materialize legacy permission metadata against the final rollout\ncwd when rollout-derived metadata replaces stale SQLite summaries.\n- Updated affected app-server and core test constructors to build\n`PermissionProfile` values directly.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- `cargo test -p codex-state`\n- `cargo test -p codex-thread-store`\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server\nsummary_from_stored_thread_preserves_millisecond_precision --lib`\n- `cargo test -p codex-core realtime_context --lib`","tree":{"sha":"2e04249f9ae27aeb5d588e1f5e3edeb4afbac11a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2e04249f9ae27aeb5d588e1f5e3edeb4afbac11a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a1ecf0cf1c25985b2c0e01103b7ddf8cf9fcc051","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGeEjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjxMQAGD6XpVnl6Ek6UpHShycRsYV\nTjo+4CMK2e8YHL0mhBHlf+PxsmOGbhd7NHBZyFnDt1wt/4ugVT+BiXcnrB3i4s6l\nb5ycCPxoj50JPH7kB6eEo8Jb4jhb0sGxfH38DfludIzWz6Qi0pZ3ZMPxF+kpQN8t\nyu+RXORle9rjyt0I+KopOi9SER44JzEpka18bWjo+E9SnENUYUD9DdLEpmJbjPZg\nnWkbHevJe21FDg6N9ZFhwOCgetqBRlLfnuB2v7aLTHFkkV0EyAXQ2YRvvzivmonS\nET3hiq472VoDfw9xJcUL708/vX3jslP6Ni1Qn3xrrfN5Cj/a5DT23Zz2iHBVJbDA\nbem0F5cutowaeOFx/ZN6xGT48cGghqY5KCga5x/qCGI4N4+AumOeAzUMoW/I9pop\nY87JTDGEsNL1kiJCSQFulb7lbnr8k9L9w/WDyNM48kG9VZ+/KrQbKHTb94Fk6iaH\nZrUEylwxve+/CjLHlpqCaWaJm79r0m3oBIlRC4CFtDxbtm3Gyz54JjDBda3bmjZP\nJkdY6Rqfmc3QBB6FPiN4wTS/p91fRDOqgLEunVyZp2zJRzF0SXZZYQY5YlK2UaDP\nrkl0/kMOGNMwvMFw2ujvhqpCKHbVEYLh1T51lV4GqRzi4BFJmdIXOcp12sfFW5J7\nk/ZEL4VXsspEcu0mncEV\n=1cEg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2e04249f9ae27aeb5d588e1f5e3edeb4afbac11a\nparent c9dc0f6338450c2bc8b70b96852f7ac422d75bbf\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1780080931 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780080931 -0700\n\nthread-store: store permission profiles (#23165)\n\n## Why\n\n`SandboxPolicy` is the legacy compatibility shape, but\n`codex-thread-store` still exposed it through `StoredThread`,\n`ThreadMetadataPatch`, and live metadata sync. That kept thread-store\nconsumers tied to the legacy representation and meant richer permission\nprofile data could not round-trip through thread metadata or cold\nrollout reconciliation.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Replaced thread-store `sandbox_policy` API fields with canonical\n`PermissionProfile` fields.\n- Persist new permission-profile metadata as canonical JSON in the\nexisting SQLite metadata slot while continuing to read older legacy\nsandbox policy values.\n- Updated local, in-memory, live metadata sync, and rollout extraction\npaths to propagate `TurnContextItem::permission_profile()`.\n- Re-materialize legacy permission metadata against the final rollout\ncwd when rollout-derived metadata replaces stale SQLite summaries.\n- Updated affected app-server and core test constructors to build\n`PermissionProfile` values directly.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- `cargo test -p codex-state`\n- `cargo test -p codex-thread-store`\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server\nsummary_from_stored_thread_preserves_millisecond_precision --lib`\n- `cargo test -p codex-core realtime_context --lib`","verified_at":"2026-05-29T18:55:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a1ecf0cf1c25985b2c0e01103b7ddf8cf9fcc051","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a1ecf0cf1c25985b2c0e01103b7ddf8cf9fcc051","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a1ecf0cf1c25985b2c0e01103b7ddf8cf9fcc051/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c9dc0f6338450c2bc8b70b96852f7ac422d75bbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c9dc0f6338450c2bc8b70b96852f7ac422d75bbf","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c9dc0f6338450c2bc8b70b96852f7ac422d75bbf"}]},{"sha":"c9dc0f6338450c2bc8b70b96852f7ac422d75bbf","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGM5ZGMwZjYzMzg0NTBjMmJjOGI3MGI5Njg1MmY3YWM0MjJkNzViYmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Channing Conger","email":"cconger@openai.com","date":"2026-05-29T18:42:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T18:42:52Z"},"message":"code-mode: introduce durable session interface (#24180)\n\n## Summary\n\nIntroduce a `CodeModeSession` interface for executing and managing\ncode-mode cells.\n\nThis moves cell lifecycle, callback delegation, termination, and\nshutdown behind a session abstraction, while continuing to use the\nexisting in-process implementation, and the ability to implement an\nexternal process one behind this interface.\n\nA Codex session owns one `CodeModeSession`, which in turn owns its\nrunning cells and stored code-mode state. Each cell is represented to\nthe caller as a `StartedCell`, exposing its cell ID and initial\nresponse.\n\nIt also introduces a `CodeModeSessionDelegate` callback interface. A\nsession uses the delegate to invoke nested host tools and emit\nnotifications while a cell is running, allowing the runtime to\ncommunicate with its owning Codex session without depending directly on\ncore turn handling.\n\n<img width=\"2121\" height=\"1001\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c349a819-2a59-485c-bda4-2caf68ac4c31\"\n/>","tree":{"sha":"b818009b0822c712acfa4968293176f636fa2693","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/b818009b0822c712acfa4968293176f636fa2693"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c9dc0f6338450c2bc8b70b96852f7ac422d75bbf","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGd4sCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqMcQAC9pN0X/Uij4gJdrO7ZTnuQH\nuZW6Fi4wTS9keH/XJoQM76i6OKSIwMeHDJ22uJK4v0a44vKW6IGXwkmajUmr85pX\nGIM/EZUY8+jL9Ur759KCaFcSz0CJqxKC4e9RASZmsUrvzuGS9BlLVFQNuQbnnnbn\nzIXzAniT4uWpoC+deaeoojkVADgCC0qTHqnJKtZnTBO6bDM3r77TpRLyAiP8SEO5\nZFKxpICCs7Ls2FPKtwNqLXEdYYx1x7py2EfWOAIZKENDuV1dZnzpSB2F5l0DKXtr\nXdlkjXn4JxnYjq9rzaGyCm85+6YzkLgKgWxjpMxh6Z6WDNEPjT/2O5FNSRgQsfX/\nqlp5b1PSDVnSvgY47Yh8ZigvZEl7IbFtzmVqEupIAdg6bCTO/a0nM8fR+EQZy1wB\nc8v8CSXfRHE85mtV48rGffpq0fCqUj3ZTv+pq5q3iawBV+3t9TaA4bSgMA9uAl4M\n+c6zkX9TkbNs05KCUS8D9dlmZ6E1uixoGoYRTRSYGIhjD9a0vkZnm934VYSe/yHj\nIasmiLtfV6Vlp213MBKgRB/FkBOHfWqfvVppSJYv7Th5AroABzYyUb2+KpFVlJw5\nC4gnvnjL9Pe7rvFL8cbRLjopJv8PTKuXGyuZ2igerlKvw5jiFodbxIoa8BSrtYAx\nERqt34cKHDfHSNjPEs2z\n=nDqa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b818009b0822c712acfa4968293176f636fa2693\nparent 451b38644283345cab51739eef8d683fe1a4219c\nauthor Channing Conger <cconger@openai.com> 1780080172 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780080172 -0700\n\ncode-mode: introduce durable session interface (#24180)\n\n## Summary\n\nIntroduce a `CodeModeSession` interface for executing and managing\ncode-mode cells.\n\nThis moves cell lifecycle, callback delegation, termination, and\nshutdown behind a session abstraction, while continuing to use the\nexisting in-process implementation, and the ability to implement an\nexternal process one behind this interface.\n\nA Codex session owns one `CodeModeSession`, which in turn owns its\nrunning cells and stored code-mode state. Each cell is represented to\nthe caller as a `StartedCell`, exposing its cell ID and initial\nresponse.\n\nIt also introduces a `CodeModeSessionDelegate` callback interface. A\nsession uses the delegate to invoke nested host tools and emit\nnotifications while a cell is running, allowing the runtime to\ncommunicate with its owning Codex session without depending directly on\ncore turn handling.\n\n<img width=\"2121\" height=\"1001\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c349a819-2a59-485c-bda4-2caf68ac4c31\"\n/>","verified_at":"2026-05-29T18:42:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c9dc0f6338450c2bc8b70b96852f7ac422d75bbf","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c9dc0f6338450c2bc8b70b96852f7ac422d75bbf","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c9dc0f6338450c2bc8b70b96852f7ac422d75bbf/comments","author":{"login":"cconger","id":200563,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDU2Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger","html_url":"https://github.com/cconger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"451b38644283345cab51739eef8d683fe1a4219c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/451b38644283345cab51739eef8d683fe1a4219c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/451b38644283345cab51739eef8d683fe1a4219c"}]},{"sha":"451b38644283345cab51739eef8d683fe1a4219c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDQ1MWIzODY0NDI4MzM0NWNhYjUxNzM5ZWVmOGQ2ODNmZTFhNDIxOWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Horacek","email":"eric.horacek@openai.com","date":"2026-05-29T18:40:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T18:40:44Z"},"message":"[exec-server] Kill dropped filesystem helpers (#25116)\n\n## Summary\n- terminate sandbox filesystem helpers when the Tokio child handle is\ndropped\n\n## Why\nA sandbox filesystem helper can stall during process startup before\nreading stdin. If the owning async operation is cancelled or torn down,\nthe spawned helper should not remain running as an orphaned process.\n\nSetting `kill_on_drop(true)` gives the filesystem helper the cleanup\nbehavior that Tokio child processes otherwise do not enable by default.\n\nThis intentionally does not add a timeout. It does not detect or recover\nan active hung file edit while the owning future remains alive. A more\nprecise startup-health mechanism can be handled separately.\n\n## Validation\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server` (186 tests passed; benchmark smoke\npassed)\n- `just fmt`\n- `just fix -p codex-exec-server`\n- `git diff --check`","tree":{"sha":"6dbbddf64c89d6a5cbceef65757348d623c63efb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6dbbddf64c89d6a5cbceef65757348d623c63efb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/451b38644283345cab51739eef8d683fe1a4219c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGd2sCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIxoQADXimrizPLY1d5YxzyFliQdQ\nwkVqJ+Le1jiZGeI9cbHo26HdPDtweZ8JVOrKmq36O5WorgivkHXwgVuBuZJmHylU\nUYxxj0l4u0mc5cNlRrMxaN3dQhh6+Mzr47CQ4yREEFQ7oAA+FF6a0OKbH2JqT8UT\nOiFqYQQtwzszFV/qTNm23WdyOHE17x9xIghzt8cs47weLDmGIOX+4V9hhWWODUSW\nwvXE18KA2+NMuAVc1aqfPlZc7sXHKzrkHdOeG4Aip4VW7krN4wRjOp5v8YR+3RCp\njhYX5dOOtL9z41iV2t5WBUflxtTxABoeexoZBSqJXF4+bHEsW9sbpElZi3S/UHuV\nmJUABxknoYVRZZ4xHjBJ/yeqY5jnxeqVpksJTFlTGyciy61IIrZP6iX1D0vTYnwq\nwz3vzdzsyOqo3Tgl9cjb5NLA1KQ0rMigshXzCBvPopBM0KXvP30yjJh88RBGO990\njkKFbkgydEltfiqxX74Z2iwlE7qetso9/bTcN2SQLcA/uMjffpp9Z343SkwlM1OF\nC3YOcp+jclsshBA4KZPH0xRWBSZTTdmpTXxWTVDdk3Lqm0szdhL7HXeLiYEh7VJR\n5YVB6MLsRq34TFZFbJB4F/R2/XvmKlYs0vh/xsd23qroMZ2y8yOC07W0pjKOmL9D\nVBtg1/6mzM+10G/iMhP9\n=YSSM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6dbbddf64c89d6a5cbceef65757348d623c63efb\nparent fc9cf62efb8098fce40b5198d3e7cfc45b4ce441\nauthor Eric Horacek <eric.horacek@openai.com> 1780080044 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780080044 -0700\n\n[exec-server] Kill dropped filesystem helpers (#25116)\n\n## Summary\n- terminate sandbox filesystem helpers when the Tokio child handle is\ndropped\n\n## Why\nA sandbox filesystem helper can stall during process startup before\nreading stdin. If the owning async operation is cancelled or torn down,\nthe spawned helper should not remain running as an orphaned process.\n\nSetting `kill_on_drop(true)` gives the filesystem helper the cleanup\nbehavior that Tokio child processes otherwise do not enable by default.\n\nThis intentionally does not add a timeout. It does not detect or recover\nan active hung file edit while the owning future remains alive. A more\nprecise startup-health mechanism can be handled separately.\n\n## Validation\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server` (186 tests passed; benchmark smoke\npassed)\n- `just fmt`\n- `just fix -p codex-exec-server`\n- `git diff --check`","verified_at":"2026-05-29T18:40:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/451b38644283345cab51739eef8d683fe1a4219c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/451b38644283345cab51739eef8d683fe1a4219c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/451b38644283345cab51739eef8d683fe1a4219c/comments","author":{"login":"erichoracek","id":438313,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzODMxMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/438313?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/erichoracek","html_url":"https://github.com/erichoracek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erichoracek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erichoracek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erichoracek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erichoracek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erichoracek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erichoracek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erichoracek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erichoracek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erichoracek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fc9cf62efb8098fce40b5198d3e7cfc45b4ce441","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fc9cf62efb8098fce40b5198d3e7cfc45b4ce441","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/fc9cf62efb8098fce40b5198d3e7cfc45b4ce441"}]},{"sha":"fc9cf62efb8098fce40b5198d3e7cfc45b4ce441","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGZjOWNmNjJlZmI4MDk4ZmNlNDBiNTE5OGQzZTdjZmM0NWI0Y2U0NDE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Owen Lin","email":"owenlin0@gmail.com","date":"2026-05-29T18:28:12Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T18:28:12Z"},"message":"Add subagent lineage metadata for responsesapi (#24161)\n\n## Why\n\nWe recently added `forked_from_thread_id` which lets us trace where a\nthread's _context_ comes from, but we also want to understand subagent\nlineage (e.g. which parent thread spawned this subagent? what kind of\nsubagent is it?) which is orthogonal.\n\nThis PR adds `parent_thread_id` and `subagent_kind` to the\n`x-codex-turn-metadata` header sent to ResponsesAPI.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Adds `parent_thread_id` and `subagent_kind` to core-owned\n`x-codex-turn-metadata`.\n- Restores persisted `SessionSource` and `ThreadSource` from resumed\nsession metadata so cold-resumed subagent threads keep their lineage on\nlater Responses API requests.\n- Centralizes parent-thread extraction on `SessionSource` /\n`SubAgentSource` and reuses it in the Responses client, analytics, agent\ncontrol, and state parsing paths.\n- Extends reserved-key, git-enrichment, thread-spawn, and app-server v2\nmetadata coverage for the new lineage fields.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Not run locally per request.\n- Added focused coverage in `core/src/turn_metadata_tests.rs` and\n`app-server/tests/suite/v2/client_metadata.rs`.","tree":{"sha":"f924d177e740c75a42bbd9c641a9f5d03118254d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f924d177e740c75a42bbd9c641a9f5d03118254d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/fc9cf62efb8098fce40b5198d3e7cfc45b4ce441","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGdq8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+bEQAKbFMbmEv7y66/j2c1MPBinz\nDjMcwqWhTnRpKb5ZyO9GRrsegEGbAJ9vjo4dL+Q2QaB2oKhDtgkVq9uxY/tifVzb\n/P3gvLKArgrj60KmBGf+Ub0VA21D3wAdymDDIFxTxOVPC8xHVvfzSXTEVcS/RKAh\n5wpFG0NA/vm1nEQR2jm8SU92hJEqiA6rucEWoU6WF5KZmNmFxYpllcZ6/M4k3HZr\n5m7MhB7c7rpWoPr1fqBwZsTzX+B/KUBar59G7HkTj3RWaf5Z0gCwBzxiHoCUsAAA\nqVKWtvmJdCGAIQ2dSbDlGs6/0HPMx68T32JnqFHSy5oPDYZlx8yxQZXtg5mQM1Wb\nuNS3JG0BLAE/RhigK8Nt8FUUJMwqet8PsAgaOzPG32rJROwdaOzgzRG+j7TbETtL\n842VqOYJ0uPTNahflJ3BdjmJ+ERAZnguxBk/XMxaPAPv8bVPAYzVJoN1HBtFST1F\ntG2rh8c9FunfspyFA0s0NpRW61+Y0IUv+50EyBu6M5fpwd8dd2K74oe8UBEEEwnw\nVLwBMLjSgyRaR1ZoOs4QLWJPfTBuazEhdMRYvfy2bMpM5zi1sgvvc9uMc1Bc027k\nQNC+DM7+NT0rrzBVwh8NpQry9dUQCtIBvbJfOQVi84Jqx8NNQ+faN/C6oCjgOJH4\nAjN3M3S0l4Y9O0fv5zCN\n=WqKn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f924d177e740c75a42bbd9c641a9f5d03118254d\nparent 62039e8d356a3e983c5a4af82e09458810fc3355\nauthor Owen Lin <owenlin0@gmail.com> 1780079292 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780079292 -0700\n\nAdd subagent lineage metadata for responsesapi (#24161)\n\n## Why\n\nWe recently added `forked_from_thread_id` which lets us trace where a\nthread's _context_ comes from, but we also want to understand subagent\nlineage (e.g. which parent thread spawned this subagent? what kind of\nsubagent is it?) which is orthogonal.\n\nThis PR adds `parent_thread_id` and `subagent_kind` to the\n`x-codex-turn-metadata` header sent to ResponsesAPI.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Adds `parent_thread_id` and `subagent_kind` to core-owned\n`x-codex-turn-metadata`.\n- Restores persisted `SessionSource` and `ThreadSource` from resumed\nsession metadata so cold-resumed subagent threads keep their lineage on\nlater Responses API requests.\n- Centralizes parent-thread extraction on `SessionSource` /\n`SubAgentSource` and reuses it in the Responses client, analytics, agent\ncontrol, and state parsing paths.\n- Extends reserved-key, git-enrichment, thread-spawn, and app-server v2\nmetadata coverage for the new lineage fields.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Not run locally per request.\n- Added focused coverage in `core/src/turn_metadata_tests.rs` and\n`app-server/tests/suite/v2/client_metadata.rs`.","verified_at":"2026-05-29T18:28:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fc9cf62efb8098fce40b5198d3e7cfc45b4ce441","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/fc9cf62efb8098fce40b5198d3e7cfc45b4ce441","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fc9cf62efb8098fce40b5198d3e7cfc45b4ce441/comments","author":{"login":"owenlin0","id":947871,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk0Nzg3MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/947871?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0","html_url":"https://github.com/owenlin0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"62039e8d356a3e983c5a4af82e09458810fc3355","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/62039e8d356a3e983c5a4af82e09458810fc3355","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/62039e8d356a3e983c5a4af82e09458810fc3355"}]},{"sha":"62039e8d356a3e983c5a4af82e09458810fc3355","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDYyMDM5ZThkMzU2YTNlOTgzYzVhNGFmODJlMDk0NTg4MTBmYzMzNTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-05-29T18:09:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T18:09:40Z"},"message":"Use session wording in `/rename` confirmation (#25035)\n\n## Why\n\nThe TUI `/rename` confirmation should use the term \"session\" for\nconsistency.","tree":{"sha":"e62d44d72c1e9c93b0c555f79a187a067f5d610c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e62d44d72c1e9c93b0c555f79a187a067f5d610c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/62039e8d356a3e983c5a4af82e09458810fc3355","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGdZkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZhQQAEmtEkoJ1ZBUr7spwmBLiaIj\n95y2SK/2kR4+T+tdL0JB2L75BhnP7hxmMsCsBn55x7zibhI68ARnxY8+vRYxOBRb\nP/FSrVLCMNx2iqLFfVenYQyQYsYfp8j2q1W6O6xM8p6D2Hdal+SIIB40AuQiP08s\nk/d+ZSKcuqB9yUzWKao+rUMamH1VMY4lTAF3K1jTBbmH6Td6EOxghBK0/iL5VuE8\nXRN03xKjerek+bL5etkHqYDGUvT4hx116/EkAJEaxSnf0zKOrSBtERz0mDQW6s0t\nd+jGz2F0c0rtdiyHAaUWUP2dbJItXL0zOs8VaYofjJ3VrNxIdSVNLqOW4ENUVup6\nnAD5ULg+jFEFStnvR082iC4YM4R/m43xh2oqkvVcwe3WgNugX18R4e/dd2AwUNyk\np2AbJMjlkWHVlhUEHCeor1Iheu6B/aODqy5JJe5fi2kYkKn6EvrOKA09WhG/7HhW\n2m99FoRceGss7mZX+7IinaL4YIFQ4qBU2Zq2Ki4lrctNJA5Eqh5Jwe/RGJiP7Qi+\nDEgpo3/x7dtIRZ7ZMjeNQyq/UltHVB9E9F60Dc9zAJBo+AibaLXRyI3OEDTHx7f4\na+4dNyk7sjE2bYWkPO1M4kRsXwUWWhVHvIIAZxWEjCXTympYtPAAa7MtzM8LpcnT\nNgxA+2DcxQ2ek3tA3v0z\n=nRHi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e62d44d72c1e9c93b0c555f79a187a067f5d610c\nparent 36cd36626db4c16244957d9b4dfa6d041ca440f7\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1780078180 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780078180 -0700\n\nUse session wording in `/rename` confirmation (#25035)\n\n## Why\n\nThe TUI `/rename` confirmation should use the term \"session\" for\nconsistency.","verified_at":"2026-05-29T18:09:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/62039e8d356a3e983c5a4af82e09458810fc3355","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/62039e8d356a3e983c5a4af82e09458810fc3355","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/62039e8d356a3e983c5a4af82e09458810fc3355/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"36cd36626db4c16244957d9b4dfa6d041ca440f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/36cd36626db4c16244957d9b4dfa6d041ca440f7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/36cd36626db4c16244957d9b4dfa6d041ca440f7"}]},{"sha":"36cd36626db4c16244957d9b4dfa6d041ca440f7","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDM2Y2QzNjYyNmRiNGMxNjI0NDk1N2Q5YjRkZmE2ZDA0MWNhNDQwZjc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-05-29T18:07:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T18:07:19Z"},"message":"Add `/archive` slash command (#25027)\n\n## Why\n\nTUI users can archive saved sessions from other surfaces, but there is\nno in-session command for archiving the active session. Since archiving\nthe active session also exits the TUI, the command should ask for\nexplicit confirmation instead of firing immediately.\n\nI'm also working on [a companion\nPR](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/25021) that adds `codex\narchive` and `codex unarchive` top-level CLI commands.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Adds a new `/archive` slash command described as `archive this session\nand exit`.\n- Shows a confirmation dialog with `No, don't archive` selected first\nand `Yes, archive and exit` as the explicit action.\n- On confirmation, calls the existing `thread/archive` app-server RPC\nfor the active main session and exits after success.\n- Keeps `/archive` disabled while a task is running and unavailable in\nside conversations.\n\n## Verification\n\nAdded focused TUI coverage for the `/archive` confirmation flow,\ndisabled-while-task-running behavior, and the `/ar` slash-command popup\nsnapshot.","tree":{"sha":"2c1e07ab214c6bd113c49f3b2a6b8596f2dbaa7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2c1e07ab214c6bd113c49f3b2a6b8596f2dbaa7a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/36cd36626db4c16244957d9b4dfa6d041ca440f7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGdXXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8YgQAKtVuDkRY2hwUFO78oSfyh5L\nYeEVahRRYzhhyJT5Wai1Xdoom5Q25kcW0G9yndiWg48Gl8uVa8jCGsqGVsfzU9YD\n7QQAM6LpxZLEMVhHCClGcY2NDbNVq2lbAs4veW3dpk3xlHUW9VxcUquQ5XUbeWfY\nEpa0aDrNgvdu5OL8O48DSIJTTBRKFgPI+fOAIggHOwHmrhdG4Ky7PB69VNUSTYjv\nPyMI8pkNb56Il8ixvKYSi+7AEbxebBaeLtehETBQpIqB8eCUkpcDZRrsXf/y4n+S\nAGLc0x8ltEO8HlJQrIz4YJT8DKMh1kWE9zTgItjFHYKtAt1ciR7Nw/yhPFjYrrRH\nSeEp2eaSPCOfmllkksCF73rvBwyCQTa7Oqa5jIMsIKJDXmWNUvSacK0NTYoZ57jX\nHr8YL7Yh4mBE41CN+xQyQJ81NCLNzMrLH/XFO6cek552NQ+OXOP7c50OrtV3+GWf\nP9c66qxAX0dNmpJOZ/WFT2FgJdOSHT83XYeO+NkgVlA2Cb6vWjdgnqsY7lpUYdXu\n9ZCvmPA3k2R24RuM+DbECEHFVP9QByD58RftfGxe8zoIJpyu/Py0vYdG9YuUJgkd\nK1hELOy6R+YM715NyFyLzW9H7QuWkOPOWpUJG+Rvl0uU4FQaShT+4KjzSeazTR/w\nVqF/nOqNzOQM6e27P2nh\n=oqH5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2c1e07ab214c6bd113c49f3b2a6b8596f2dbaa7a\nparent 1333f4a68907e82e6477256c76997c004e363289\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1780078039 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780078039 -0700\n\nAdd `/archive` slash command (#25027)\n\n## Why\n\nTUI users can archive saved sessions from other surfaces, but there is\nno in-session command for archiving the active session. Since archiving\nthe active session also exits the TUI, the command should ask for\nexplicit confirmation instead of firing immediately.\n\nI'm also working on [a companion\nPR](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/25021) that adds `codex\narchive` and `codex unarchive` top-level CLI commands.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Adds a new `/archive` slash command described as `archive this session\nand exit`.\n- Shows a confirmation dialog with `No, don't archive` selected first\nand `Yes, archive and exit` as the explicit action.\n- On confirmation, calls the existing `thread/archive` app-server RPC\nfor the active main session and exits after success.\n- Keeps `/archive` disabled while a task is running and unavailable in\nside conversations.\n\n## Verification\n\nAdded focused TUI coverage for the `/archive` confirmation flow,\ndisabled-while-task-running behavior, and the `/ar` slash-command popup\nsnapshot.","verified_at":"2026-05-29T18:07:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/36cd36626db4c16244957d9b4dfa6d041ca440f7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/36cd36626db4c16244957d9b4dfa6d041ca440f7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/36cd36626db4c16244957d9b4dfa6d041ca440f7/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1333f4a68907e82e6477256c76997c004e363289","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1333f4a68907e82e6477256c76997c004e363289","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1333f4a68907e82e6477256c76997c004e363289"}]},{"sha":"1333f4a68907e82e6477256c76997c004e363289","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDEzMzNmNGE2ODkwN2U4MmU2NDc3MjU2Yzc2OTk3YzAwNGUzNjMyODk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-05-29T18:06:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T18:06:40Z"},"message":"Align TUI permissions labels with app (#25017)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe desktop app now presents the on-request permissions mode as `Ask for\napproval` and the manual-review-backed mode as `Approve for me`. The TUI\nstill exposed older/internal labels like `Default` and `Auto-review`,\nwhich made the same underlying settings look different across clients.\n\nThis updates the TUI UX copy to match the app without changing the\nunderlying default behavior. Fresh threads continue to use the existing\non-request approval mode, now displayed as `Ask for approval`.\n\nThe label changes cover `/permissions`, explicit profile permissions\nmenus, status surfaces, config persistence history/error text, and the\ncorresponding TUI snapshots.\n\n### Before\n<img width=\"1181\" height=\"119\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-05-28 at 10 19\n47 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0664846b-b6dd-4931-b4dd-d0af0d42058e\"\n/>\n<img width=\"523\" height=\"19\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-05-28 at 10 21 29 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7899c33e-b35d-4684-8389-97e357803423\"\n/>\n\n### After\n<img width=\"1216\" height=\"117\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-05-28 at 10 19\n32 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/015aab43-ac97-411f-8031-75cdd887251b\"\n/>\n<img width=\"567\" height=\"18\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-05-28 at 10 20 24 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/28b6422c-b823-4298-b221-c83d46d09d66\"\n/>","tree":{"sha":"c3cd45d40ee02b0474457a7ba96366bf80371228","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c3cd45d40ee02b0474457a7ba96366bf80371228"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/1333f4a68907e82e6477256c76997c004e363289","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGdWwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAy5IQAF+LIyDhVUjvhpVIP8Wsi0EP\nGGLQOs/0wDYT1+Qx76mnTIYSEQKBSPVoxWOAKfDjC6oFDZaNo5wJ/M7Meyuzdso0\nQaGD1c/4oKYJEWBzEdeUEreJsgTCom1RKgRPN6CZkj2M6nRCrqznxulssS2sammO\nbfuXfx2BDrUCmO9iq5e+8ojbyALul6jWP3UVt/smwYiPrvRQQR8ZvV56ugzQq/Si\nvHUGL1GGj3PgqmkzrRubpseYDVX7RkHDvfVrCx5Bjy6elnc5rm6tBve+zivTtsJv\nhH/f8aEt7fRBkJSNq7fW+vFT2mYrsRnE/elpXvcRJrPWIqEqG0wIzby0Lkzirank\nh3Tz+9cEorypnQEXwXfQppe1TcBreC+Oezlbw8YpvyCZcNXWLcrX5GeCb/O+qJQG\nCHshssKey7D69d4XJ5214bXQ731bDpYr+baYx6PtH2j7kQ6KRWjV2swOPufXjv8c\nJr/lSv4APJD7/G1ZESZ0zz32tIUw/2jZH82Xd/FLPtlw38EuiwKNbpjSVP4Uhwx5\nWpdJ8bU9lhUQ6ayGKE7yYcmnNFbv17T/RnbsrbwqEgX88SBSf+6+gQN3GHjKb0Vn\nR+eqvc3io1RMeO9uPQXcEyiDbC1PPJGHm14aXiv6ztfwAxbctaPi42n3C5thdYIJ\nCXnlnkfCqjGBox7Pxn6C\n=VSeX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c3cd45d40ee02b0474457a7ba96366bf80371228\nparent cb9178e8b30293d695d0bebea09c62b21116e9de\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1780078000 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780078000 -0700\n\nAlign TUI permissions labels with app (#25017)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe desktop app now presents the on-request permissions mode as `Ask for\napproval` and the manual-review-backed mode as `Approve for me`. The TUI\nstill exposed older/internal labels like `Default` and `Auto-review`,\nwhich made the same underlying settings look different across clients.\n\nThis updates the TUI UX copy to match the app without changing the\nunderlying default behavior. Fresh threads continue to use the existing\non-request approval mode, now displayed as `Ask for approval`.\n\nThe label changes cover `/permissions`, explicit profile permissions\nmenus, status surfaces, config persistence history/error text, and the\ncorresponding TUI snapshots.\n\n### Before\n<img width=\"1181\" height=\"119\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-05-28 at 10 19\n47 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0664846b-b6dd-4931-b4dd-d0af0d42058e\"\n/>\n<img width=\"523\" height=\"19\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-05-28 at 10 21 29 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7899c33e-b35d-4684-8389-97e357803423\"\n/>\n\n### After\n<img width=\"1216\" height=\"117\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-05-28 at 10 19\n32 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/015aab43-ac97-411f-8031-75cdd887251b\"\n/>\n<img width=\"567\" height=\"18\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-05-28 at 10 20 24 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/28b6422c-b823-4298-b221-c83d46d09d66\"\n/>","verified_at":"2026-05-29T18:06:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1333f4a68907e82e6477256c76997c004e363289","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1333f4a68907e82e6477256c76997c004e363289","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1333f4a68907e82e6477256c76997c004e363289/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cb9178e8b30293d695d0bebea09c62b21116e9de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cb9178e8b30293d695d0bebea09c62b21116e9de","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/cb9178e8b30293d695d0bebea09c62b21116e9de"}]},{"sha":"cb9178e8b30293d695d0bebea09c62b21116e9de","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGNiOTE3OGU4YjMwMjkzZDY5NWQwYmViZWEwOWM2MmIyMTExNmU5ZGU","commit":{"author":{"name":"iceweasel-oai","email":"iceweasel@openai.com","date":"2026-05-29T18:01:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T18:01:44Z"},"message":"Add Windows sandbox provisioning setup command (#24831)\n\n## Why\n\nSome Windows users do not have local admin access, so they cannot\ncomplete the elevated portion of the Windows sandbox setup when Codex\nfirst needs it. This adds an alpha provisioning path that an admin or IT\ndeployment script can run ahead of time for the Codex user.\n\nThe intended managed-deployment shape is:\n\n```powershell\ncodex sandbox setup --elevated --user \"$env:COMPUTERNAME\\Alice\" --codex-home \"C:\\Users\\Alice\\.codex\"\n```\n\n`--elevated` is treated as the requested sandbox setup level, not as\nproof that the process is elevated. The Windows sandbox setup\norchestration still checks that the caller is actually elevated before\nlaunching the helper without a UAC prompt.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added `codex sandbox setup --elevated` with explicit user selection\nvia either `--current-user` or `--user ... --codex-home ...`.\n- Moved the CLI implementation into `cli/src/sandbox_setup.rs` instead\nof growing `cli/src/main.rs`.\n- Added a Windows sandbox `ProvisionOnly` helper mode that runs the\nelevation-required provisioning work without requiring a workspace cwd\nor runtime sandbox policy.\n- Reused the existing elevated helper path for creating/updating sandbox\nusers, configuring firewall/WFP rules, and applying sandbox directory\nACLs.\n- Persisted `windows.sandbox = \"elevated\"` into the target `CODEX_HOME`\nso the desktop app does not show the initial sandbox setup banner after\npre-provisioning succeeds.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo fmt -p codex-windows-sandbox -p codex-core -p codex-cli`\n- `cargo test -p codex-cli sandbox_setup --target-dir\ntarget\\sandbox-setup-check`\n- `cargo test -p codex-windows-sandbox\npayload_accepts_provision_only_mode --target-dir\ntarget\\sandbox-setup-check`\n- `git diff --check`\n- Manual Windows alpha flow with a standard local user (`Mandi Lavida`):\nran the new setup command from an admin shell, verified the target\n`.codex` contents, sandbox marker/secrets, ACLs, firewall rules, and\ndesktop startup without the sandbox setup banner once experimental\nnetwork proxy requirements were disabled.\n\n## Notes\n\nThis intentionally does not solve later elevated update coordination for\nIT-managed deployments. The setup command can still apply provisioning\nupdates when run again, but a broader coordination/process story is out\nof scope for this alpha.","tree":{"sha":"922062ae9a7fd2dd3caf976fdfdcac9b2a9d788d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/922062ae9a7fd2dd3caf976fdfdcac9b2a9d788d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/cb9178e8b30293d695d0bebea09c62b21116e9de","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGdSICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGUAQAKqRclI0m684XdKWj4X/v2el\n5UcaiCOELsSSe57BGDcQj9huDJrRwgWmjUMYWL6rp8KlmBwDoxm7OxkJzzCmRTtd\n3pSBnm4pZbfVDaToIQ6adm/YWYYJ73BgTEd9wOTkkNh//a16p+nR8cIuZsK/NPQm\nEF/bTh6Rm2cY4sUVHNfninFSo6Tr4hGI5kaA85Go5ZUcv5iYED4TyutVsM4+nnBJ\niPOFseTvVywmbwn8XO3lI/OBzaiEoqSoNS9HhW5kDNfqZk05Di3GfA81nmxYdW/S\nP+XjzdVcJMbyR70fxSNchGTXF+ued3a+w9eeU48t1/d9LTES1n5BhwF5JpV8gfbM\nEOVwmP7k7BFNQKiuV6EJSeK2vORRlBGRLyq46yHUgFOUAQQ5XLvl7ZVOKfh0NEz1\n4RhymLuv7n2/74BEbmnHjXwLG6HooBH1FMIrOlVeOttZg6TlEgG0Mqx9I7TZqf/j\nzeWv6PfnSbePx2H6u1HNMOV6pmKo0yuEYWcrxj9L0/ISqLwtFaYB67r0IZMJ0tVQ\nCGM6rjCH9wqxEar2atR5jzKoy3xx2BtXWJkblbfutpiu5wm2iWmV6Bm/JDhN1Vsm\nH0lGi0e/2ZyqDNa3xSPWg8IETFTSZoAcM/StHUtFomh1Gtts3x2sCpbbas5UUq8V\nDKdgHspvsmWN1q8bCPb/\n=Q6xB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 922062ae9a7fd2dd3caf976fdfdcac9b2a9d788d\nparent 10b03990345bd99bbc44f32f4226d065ea310d5f\nauthor iceweasel-oai <iceweasel@openai.com> 1780077704 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780077704 -0700\n\nAdd Windows sandbox provisioning setup command (#24831)\n\n## Why\n\nSome Windows users do not have local admin access, so they cannot\ncomplete the elevated portion of the Windows sandbox setup when Codex\nfirst needs it. This adds an alpha provisioning path that an admin or IT\ndeployment script can run ahead of time for the Codex user.\n\nThe intended managed-deployment shape is:\n\n```powershell\ncodex sandbox setup --elevated --user \"$env:COMPUTERNAME\\Alice\" --codex-home \"C:\\Users\\Alice\\.codex\"\n```\n\n`--elevated` is treated as the requested sandbox setup level, not as\nproof that the process is elevated. The Windows sandbox setup\norchestration still checks that the caller is actually elevated before\nlaunching the helper without a UAC prompt.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added `codex sandbox setup --elevated` with explicit user selection\nvia either `--current-user` or `--user ... --codex-home ...`.\n- Moved the CLI implementation into `cli/src/sandbox_setup.rs` instead\nof growing `cli/src/main.rs`.\n- Added a Windows sandbox `ProvisionOnly` helper mode that runs the\nelevation-required provisioning work without requiring a workspace cwd\nor runtime sandbox policy.\n- Reused the existing elevated helper path for creating/updating sandbox\nusers, configuring firewall/WFP rules, and applying sandbox directory\nACLs.\n- Persisted `windows.sandbox = \"elevated\"` into the target `CODEX_HOME`\nso the desktop app does not show the initial sandbox setup banner after\npre-provisioning succeeds.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo fmt -p codex-windows-sandbox -p codex-core -p codex-cli`\n- `cargo test -p codex-cli sandbox_setup --target-dir\ntarget\\sandbox-setup-check`\n- `cargo test -p codex-windows-sandbox\npayload_accepts_provision_only_mode --target-dir\ntarget\\sandbox-setup-check`\n- `git diff --check`\n- Manual Windows alpha flow with a standard local user (`Mandi Lavida`):\nran the new setup command from an admin shell, verified the target\n`.codex` contents, sandbox marker/secrets, ACLs, firewall rules, and\ndesktop startup without the sandbox setup banner once experimental\nnetwork proxy requirements were disabled.\n\n## Notes\n\nThis intentionally does not solve later elevated update coordination for\nIT-managed deployments. The setup command can still apply provisioning\nupdates when run again, but a broader coordination/process story is out\nof scope for this alpha.","verified_at":"2026-05-29T18:01:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cb9178e8b30293d695d0bebea09c62b21116e9de","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/cb9178e8b30293d695d0bebea09c62b21116e9de","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cb9178e8b30293d695d0bebea09c62b21116e9de/comments","author":{"login":"iceweasel-oai","id":234057055,"node_id":"U_kgDODfNtXw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234057055?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/iceweasel-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"10b03990345bd99bbc44f32f4226d065ea310d5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/10b03990345bd99bbc44f32f4226d065ea310d5f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/10b03990345bd99bbc44f32f4226d065ea310d5f"}]},{"sha":"10b03990345bd99bbc44f32f4226d065ea310d5f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDEwYjAzOTkwMzQ1YmQ5OWJiYzQ0ZjMyZjQyMjZkMDY1ZWEzMTBkNWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Won Park","email":"won@openai.com","date":"2026-05-29T17:33:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T17:33:13Z"},"message":"Route extension image generation through the native image completion pipeline (#24972)\n\n## Why\n\nThe standalone `image_gen.imagegen` extension should behave like native\nimage generation for artifact persistence and UI completion, while\nreturning its save-location guidance as part of the tool result instead\nof injecting a developer message.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added an image-generation completion hook for extension tools so core\ncan persist generated images and emit the existing `ImageGeneration`\nlifecycle events.\n- Reused core image artifact persistence for extension output and\nremoved extension-local save-path/file-writing logic.\n- Split shared image persistence from built-in finalization so native\nimage generation keeps its existing developer-message instruction\nbehavior.\n- Returned the generated image save-location instruction through the\nextension `FunctionCallOutput`, alongside the generated image input for\nmodel follow-up.\n- Preserved the existing image-generation event shape for current UI and\nreplay compatibility.\n- Avoided cloning the full generated-image base64 payload when emitting\nthe in-progress image item.\n- Removed dependencies no longer needed after moving persistence out of\nthe extension crate.\n\n## Fast Follow\n- Adjust the existing Extension API and add a general `TurnItem`\nfinalization path for re-usability of code\n\n## Validation\n\n- Ran `just fmt`.\n- Ran `just bazel-lock-update`.\n- Ran `just bazel-lock-check`.\n- Ran `just test -p codex-tools -p codex-extension-api -p\ncodex-image-generation-extension`.\n- Ran `just test -p codex-core\nimage_generation_publication_is_finalized_by_core`.\n- Ran `just test -p codex-core\nhandle_output_item_done_records_image_save_history_message`.\n- Ran `just fix -p codex-tools -p codex-extension-api -p codex-core -p\ncodex-image-generation-extension`.","tree":{"sha":"12509ca97c05799e104da7d6faf180ac600da8ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/12509ca97c05799e104da7d6faf180ac600da8ee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/10b03990345bd99bbc44f32f4226d065ea310d5f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGc3ZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkiEQAHHTKKkqjSAvqjtrq0xyYeQ9\nznG3RbH/ZLgPUB/wNz+ZwK1wcf7i50BzBnP7fZyRTEv37EtBRLm/AwEiFZfuKoBY\nWY4+4w6elN4llqhlNcdK2tByD96/IMwecGXPwDFBjrbazX/d1uo0/W4S+lFPP9pR\nu2CgK+weGoJb4XDuLCHXByxh3KQETJI1+kZGUEzoKhdGozcW+YgaSr/8efX9t6gX\nXFf6rR0CsCCYRbgK4YwzO9wVQliZ2ft4whNYxCGw56MmUOhKh4T8q7MWP/bNEPnU\nPfynWeYYO7SWQPiJ30tqtrQ5qnNS0HFExqCGnqP6NiDMpXXdGQ63RWUNlUd3ofL8\nE7Oy21eCVM3C6nEeHgeJooURFH2oD8/qqTdEjCZkX2OVQv7pIeLRA83ZRQOLxLrG\nAiYzNtUsTMeoSNRymeimcgRy3jTs+7gSVzuK+5n/JF5bEAxU/1DHeYLD8krw0MkQ\najtf6HasYrD/uZK/tVpnlxHwVq1ct1JqUWe27sqJ2B65N2njWnU+KmJSmgUQEbSU\nQ5cjarZrw7sur/lmrlOW9sGVHRx72Vw6CBIeTPuiH4lTK427LdaNz53xvDoczIdz\nh/IKTpfZj0xjQ2RhNL3qcqWeqjuK8htG6kUhegrHsNzPmv7azrXs2o6D9Qips9P7\nIjhqbyLe4JgHa7w8miIA\n=l/Rl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 12509ca97c05799e104da7d6faf180ac600da8ee\nparent 3e666dd32ac7ca3faf28dd2e9252d563e32bfa0a\nauthor Won Park <won@openai.com> 1780075993 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780075993 +0000\n\nRoute extension image generation through the native image completion pipeline (#24972)\n\n## Why\n\nThe standalone `image_gen.imagegen` extension should behave like native\nimage generation for artifact persistence and UI completion, while\nreturning its save-location guidance as part of the tool result instead\nof injecting a developer message.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added an image-generation completion hook for extension tools so core\ncan persist generated images and emit the existing `ImageGeneration`\nlifecycle events.\n- Reused core image artifact persistence for extension output and\nremoved extension-local save-path/file-writing logic.\n- Split shared image persistence from built-in finalization so native\nimage generation keeps its existing developer-message instruction\nbehavior.\n- Returned the generated image save-location instruction through the\nextension `FunctionCallOutput`, alongside the generated image input for\nmodel follow-up.\n- Preserved the existing image-generation event shape for current UI and\nreplay compatibility.\n- Avoided cloning the full generated-image base64 payload when emitting\nthe in-progress image item.\n- Removed dependencies no longer needed after moving persistence out of\nthe extension crate.\n\n## Fast Follow\n- Adjust the existing Extension API and add a general `TurnItem`\nfinalization path for re-usability of code\n\n## Validation\n\n- Ran `just fmt`.\n- Ran `just bazel-lock-update`.\n- Ran `just bazel-lock-check`.\n- Ran `just test -p codex-tools -p codex-extension-api -p\ncodex-image-generation-extension`.\n- Ran `just test -p codex-core\nimage_generation_publication_is_finalized_by_core`.\n- Ran `just test -p codex-core\nhandle_output_item_done_records_image_save_history_message`.\n- Ran `just fix -p codex-tools -p codex-extension-api -p codex-core -p\ncodex-image-generation-extension`.","verified_at":"2026-05-29T17:33:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/10b03990345bd99bbc44f32f4226d065ea310d5f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/10b03990345bd99bbc44f32f4226d065ea310d5f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/10b03990345bd99bbc44f32f4226d065ea310d5f/comments","author":{"login":"won-openai","id":262224683,"node_id":"U_kgDOD6E7Kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/262224683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/won-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3e666dd32ac7ca3faf28dd2e9252d563e32bfa0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3e666dd32ac7ca3faf28dd2e9252d563e32bfa0a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3e666dd32ac7ca3faf28dd2e9252d563e32bfa0a"}]},{"sha":"3e666dd32ac7ca3faf28dd2e9252d563e32bfa0a","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDNlNjY2ZGQzMmFjN2NhM2ZhZjI4ZGQyZTkyNTJkNTYzZTMyYmZhMGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-05-29T17:22:27Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T17:22:27Z"},"message":"[codex] Wait for MCP readiness in core integration tests (#24964)\n\nEnsures MCP-backed `codex-core` integration tests exercise initialized\nservers instead of racing server startup.\n\nI've been idly investigating a few flakes and the failure modes are much\nmore confusing when a tool call fails because of a failed server start\nthan when the failed server start causes the test to fail directly.","tree":{"sha":"80e7806a5173206708f6b8de1da11c93d444f48f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/80e7806a5173206708f6b8de1da11c93d444f48f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/3e666dd32ac7ca3faf28dd2e9252d563e32bfa0a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGctTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVrwQAA8AK+aiVBdaS5ij30c45o2T\nUwY5N52KP3B5i5C3T5cocuG2ylI+qqFAnPuSAnoo0asH6GajMYNeFsa8kdAb1lyo\nSqU3MH0SG9qj/ZdSR19zwyyeFVaKUBfv5Odl5q0PcpxyGlBU9yCHEF3ip3jKqxam\ngbMutb5qbHHAvwrzOQdnZbbUsaVAFI1++p+U1q/bvGxYgODCEU7wWh2VawzivN8v\nXF/lon09tj4Ai9/bRozpcfQt820T+QX2TjqLNdMu0WfTCTu0M5p/5055fiapk5C1\n+NJYmfzcg5EaJX61/VR6tjDb8Lov73CT84cGUnI94Da8jT4MJ1aS/3grChZECc/q\nAfod6O4eJyHcZOU8xqO2M6KOHu4auwCSTUi3wkGcUs3jDriOj1yiJu5vHLHXroll\nq8fr67rj0tLc9nROKqvtDZB8gtF8QiP1ONf50FYf/AFdRgVrLYROjKfMPZVPG3Fa\nBJtMsrAaK2H7kz1wUuYoGQQC7CoiNFH9IsK0msF8qv+lD6B7ohC242ZpAtKKtcG1\nt+mbsHhh7wS+RHsotGYruAGo3NM1qgMuOSz0dPignuvhCvbwR9Xg1bFZvPpqJXDy\nGrkmNGMK46cRfGJfYYwqV6AYd3qLBcrEKUc1f9y9vhTL7vKPjPbsef+dG5cKeoET\nNuoiSZzJulK+t57azNts\n=JmlY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 80e7806a5173206708f6b8de1da11c93d444f48f\nparent e29bbb53688ea44f5a59b15eb4fa34bc75fa3fcc\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1780075347 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780075347 -0700\n\n[codex] Wait for MCP readiness in core integration tests (#24964)\n\nEnsures MCP-backed `codex-core` integration tests exercise initialized\nservers instead of racing server startup.\n\nI've been idly investigating a few flakes and the failure modes are much\nmore confusing when a tool call fails because of a failed server start\nthan when the failed server start causes the test to fail directly.","verified_at":"2026-05-29T17:22:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3e666dd32ac7ca3faf28dd2e9252d563e32bfa0a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3e666dd32ac7ca3faf28dd2e9252d563e32bfa0a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3e666dd32ac7ca3faf28dd2e9252d563e32bfa0a/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e29bbb53688ea44f5a59b15eb4fa34bc75fa3fcc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e29bbb53688ea44f5a59b15eb4fa34bc75fa3fcc","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e29bbb53688ea44f5a59b15eb4fa34bc75fa3fcc"}]},{"sha":"e29bbb53688ea44f5a59b15eb4fa34bc75fa3fcc","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGUyOWJiYjUzNjg4ZWE0NGY1YTU5YjE1ZWI0ZmEzNGJjNzVmYTNmY2M","commit":{"author":{"name":"xl-openai","email":"xl@openai.com","date":"2026-05-29T17:09:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T17:09:33Z"},"message":"feat: Add focused diagnostics for MCP HTTP send failures (#25013)\n\nAdds failure-only logging for MCP streamable HTTP post_message calls and\nthe underlying reqwest send path, capturing the MCP method/request id,\nendpoint shape, auth-header presence, timeout/connect classification,\nand sanitized error source chain without logging headers, bodies,\ntokens, or full URLs.","tree":{"sha":"e9092becb16a11193befed0e05dd67dc8baa9520","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e9092becb16a11193befed0e05dd67dc8baa9520"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e29bbb53688ea44f5a59b15eb4fa34bc75fa3fcc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGchNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoQoQAHNT6yGbl/nERvl3uPuCDvI5\nvSUb6IQW8CtEFFygFsivmmGGr5wGCUzauvUs3KuQIa1DAyUD7SCMJerN/8EmsLns\noH4/XaozPtKVqeS8NIx+ZwkERFuC3pn2gUQ40O9bBopSVIfMQm0lV7hR7tDGEKyT\n3Krn5OtyTJXVqwOT7IdT7TBTidBTi7N8+saYkNZQzX9TPu1TG7wjEEoYNo6qyZ78\nesD1zPzouiiwgti9NnmPeeG9rNTaeGKwIeMzV9GnRgNuKBUAvUlDDpcO/u6oS9DL\ntBNDig2PEbOL0mkGEE2C7DBZXFJN7q8waey48oZj/yNSqUMPLLgOk3yJ2xZJyvsH\nS0twTYRP25fHlLCRIjtrYqliaR4p5NGfeuyWhlWFhaBken24vM60KCQKVtLnKCxb\nHWSYo6JcaumZykqdRF/fLpw7sEjrIn1+3P8MB1V2OSyDX4jsft90ElIo8UFSowxs\nldoLGGdWLzxuduKQma/dx7E8hVFgQNwur9VFQXqzjdu0mZ6TviJ98ptoMiFYbRpQ\nqO3pS5hY8yl7I3YF2lJoHP9M/NZ91nrN5Jl/OW7HDDaL2y+xU4n3a7iHDHbOMtqa\nHnla2icA0brTs060onvdFkId4BBueS+fV5BHiLXOpaMNKbevtLCmMOEWiKMMLsXh\nlxtLLaihVLp8THEAGgE7\n=x26T\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e9092becb16a11193befed0e05dd67dc8baa9520\nparent f4e9d2caac760c6f293f556e38957091f8b85bbf\nauthor xl-openai <xl@openai.com> 1780074573 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780074573 -0700\n\nfeat: Add focused diagnostics for MCP HTTP send failures (#25013)\n\nAdds failure-only logging for MCP streamable HTTP post_message calls and\nthe underlying reqwest send path, capturing the MCP method/request id,\nendpoint shape, auth-header presence, timeout/connect classification,\nand sanitized error source chain without logging headers, bodies,\ntokens, or full URLs.","verified_at":"2026-05-29T17:09:33Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e29bbb53688ea44f5a59b15eb4fa34bc75fa3fcc","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e29bbb53688ea44f5a59b15eb4fa34bc75fa3fcc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e29bbb53688ea44f5a59b15eb4fa34bc75fa3fcc/comments","author":{"login":"xl-openai","id":184293535,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvwYnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184293535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/xl-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f4e9d2caac760c6f293f556e38957091f8b85bbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f4e9d2caac760c6f293f556e38957091f8b85bbf","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f4e9d2caac760c6f293f556e38957091f8b85bbf"}]},{"sha":"f4e9d2caac760c6f293f556e38957091f8b85bbf","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGY0ZTlkMmNhYWM3NjBjNmYyOTNmNTU2ZTM4OTU3MDkxZjhiODViYmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif-oai","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-05-29T16:49:21Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T16:49:21Z"},"message":"Move config document helpers into their own module (#25110)\n\n## Why\n\n`core/src/config/edit.rs` owns the config edit state machine, but it\nalso carried the TOML document helper code inline as a nested module.\nMoving those helpers into their own file keeps the edit orchestration\neasier to scan without changing the config persistence behavior.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Moved the existing `document_helpers` module from\n`core/src/config/edit.rs` into\n`core/src/config/edit/document_helpers.rs`.\n- Added `mod document_helpers;` so the existing `pub(super)` helper API\nremains available to the rest of `config::edit`.\n\n## Testing\n\nNot run; this is a refactor-only module extraction with no intended\nbehavior change.","tree":{"sha":"37a54d88d78c82421922d3ddc77f11ecfabb6694","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/37a54d88d78c82421922d3ddc77f11ecfabb6694"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f4e9d2caac760c6f293f556e38957091f8b85bbf","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGcORCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4XsQAJn/x304e5oRig9V/OCt4Asd\nfDVmrWG0ZT6Kd/0N6syv59Di/bNX0OL5lIUqJ3DQnukE/OvcZpe+kJDu+5u8dQxI\nf59ofNoEhKoKzC8IxPzxXjdj5qh7y2N819FoXaZhAvLaZhDsxuOdXgTuOYtzf+zS\nmUiVdIJP4V6B2vT2iQ36/bbp6wTv1ljzlD4F9H84cjpCjA/ubHNmfQ9UwMlVqq1e\nLLSkKmMIEQhWzTlX1AnlxVXYYTaeh1lttFBBwLHn9L0IP+d23xrKSXt1kKfY2KXk\nAOUicBUXa8U/h2E4Qchf1xmRoZbQYcJb9fTX8sfGUn9VUIoSqTJuocP2wAkPYfy6\nCdoa3GXHyTPqDtx5W4mq3ifrRDFwHR47zyu1+nzGie0bOoel0o3karEjidPLa7BQ\nzUljShIWWw1v0J0dAgsP/O8virchzHMZYvH1ZH3SFXiL+egyusIM19NsiN6RWtDg\nzNWKsJbnQqNF0XPei1ZUKjnwp9xSZlKJTfIn3IQhfJUC608y9BTs6S4CAlKJVPUJ\nmEnJxvde6+6F94uVx5rwytzC+DJnv4Y9hKlo2idkD69CD443z1q1kcw74xLEiAOi\nsafqc2QJm6IwLSXd9i4a1cbFBEm77BT+5WnTRWjmDEDpqn9X318P5xd1emyifm3A\nFZIkFGM9NaV+zygLkWky\n=pjE/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 37a54d88d78c82421922d3ddc77f11ecfabb6694\nparent 96f1347fa3504dca512ef11aa97027a5dfcbfc56\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1780073361 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780073361 +0200\n\nMove config document helpers into their own module (#25110)\n\n## Why\n\n`core/src/config/edit.rs` owns the config edit state machine, but it\nalso carried the TOML document helper code inline as a nested module.\nMoving those helpers into their own file keeps the edit orchestration\neasier to scan without changing the config persistence behavior.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Moved the existing `document_helpers` module from\n`core/src/config/edit.rs` into\n`core/src/config/edit/document_helpers.rs`.\n- Added `mod document_helpers;` so the existing `pub(super)` helper API\nremains available to the rest of `config::edit`.\n\n## Testing\n\nNot run; this is a refactor-only module extraction with no intended\nbehavior change.","verified_at":"2026-05-29T16:49:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f4e9d2caac760c6f293f556e38957091f8b85bbf","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f4e9d2caac760c6f293f556e38957091f8b85bbf","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f4e9d2caac760c6f293f556e38957091f8b85bbf/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"96f1347fa3504dca512ef11aa97027a5dfcbfc56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/96f1347fa3504dca512ef11aa97027a5dfcbfc56","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/96f1347fa3504dca512ef11aa97027a5dfcbfc56"}]},{"sha":"96f1347fa3504dca512ef11aa97027a5dfcbfc56","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDk2ZjEzNDdmYTM1MDRkY2E1MTJlZjExYWE5NzAyN2E1ZGZjYmZjNTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"sayan-oai","email":"sayan@openai.com","date":"2026-05-29T16:12:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T16:12:58Z"},"message":"Show activity for standalone web search calls (#24693)\n\n## Why\n\nStandalone `web.run` calls run in the extension, so they need normal\nweb-search progress activity while a request is in flight and durable\ncompleted activity after a thread is reloaded.\n\nFollow-up to #23823; uses the extension turn-item emission path added in\n#24813.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Emit standalone `web.run` start/completion items through the host\nturn-item emitter, preserving standard client delivery and rollout\npersistence.\n- Include useful completion detail for queries, image queries, and\nliteral-URL `open`/`find` commands.\n- Render completed searches as `Searched the web` or `Searched the web\nfor <detail>`, with snapshot coverage for the detail-free case.\n- Extend the app-server round-trip test to verify completed search\nactivity is reconstructed by `thread/read` after a fresh-process reload.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-web-search-extension`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server -E\n\"test(standalone_web_search_round_trips_encrypted_output)\"`","tree":{"sha":"8f1953d0b9837af63e04eac7ed17dffe3335d102","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/8f1953d0b9837af63e04eac7ed17dffe3335d102"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/96f1347fa3504dca512ef11aa97027a5dfcbfc56","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGbsKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAq5kQAC9F9X67Y/kRq4bo4IVamk/G\nX3txkf4v4zDDE30k9ZeHVQFg1U0ord7V/w9zwsVBNpYEZW2FzxAzH1qF0Fym17W3\nlsbgpQQnxLJXTK4uPmPN3QEnVJkuyUjJD7I/XEtX9YccfDpKQMSu0F7W9puld2k9\nXBvRaVmswR5ftXG+5fRXDL9j/Tai0wOmxHQSm/2dTel2gqvKrrj+70P6pO/Z8Yhu\nhXO/qcj9YrPXlxcMR/93+eXRwsIiipDdTo4x6N83s0KtFRJTQXYG01FAvrBKNMMY\nFQlQTfpi1U26HfVQ8wdLGRsocHKJRPspAMJrReuFWntU1NBxBLo6Go1jKK7KUQJU\nIg6YYxoAOXTDlbvgeCvUa/fQ5iOVQhsS2lz6Rkdq6KbH5jOWDVOKSRFwnxCn2gBg\nkjdVzAmoE3hns6wc45IZ4LQcOMH/Zw3SXvvUySuLUUQjW84kMHh5JZcV0hQcm4k+\n32WVGMqn8IRo8CC7LD2zoNkvgmv7o4KhzEYmEWNVUC9S4Q5/9D2azfRaSDmrzcTB\nUT6tFo+k+ahQce/uNH8VkJSHa4cMLghqQY4fsQ4qZ4A76ond6/lfATiLGb2PVM+7\nPN8+fOF42itr83g9KORwWW1K/NqbWUCXIxAnD2H5pFjeaDbnXzZdJh53q3q6NEyF\nHKalEFLZlv4MGyrSVv6q\n=X33c\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8f1953d0b9837af63e04eac7ed17dffe3335d102\nparent 5577a9e1482ed867318dad51a01e5d18a5c5e5fa\nauthor sayan-oai <sayan@openai.com> 1780071178 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780071178 +0000\n\nShow activity for standalone web search calls (#24693)\n\n## Why\n\nStandalone `web.run` calls run in the extension, so they need normal\nweb-search progress activity while a request is in flight and durable\ncompleted activity after a thread is reloaded.\n\nFollow-up to #23823; uses the extension turn-item emission path added in\n#24813.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Emit standalone `web.run` start/completion items through the host\nturn-item emitter, preserving standard client delivery and rollout\npersistence.\n- Include useful completion detail for queries, image queries, and\nliteral-URL `open`/`find` commands.\n- Render completed searches as `Searched the web` or `Searched the web\nfor <detail>`, with snapshot coverage for the detail-free case.\n- Extend the app-server round-trip test to verify completed search\nactivity is reconstructed by `thread/read` after a fresh-process reload.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-web-search-extension`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server -E\n\"test(standalone_web_search_round_trips_encrypted_output)\"`","verified_at":"2026-05-29T16:12:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/96f1347fa3504dca512ef11aa97027a5dfcbfc56","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/96f1347fa3504dca512ef11aa97027a5dfcbfc56","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/96f1347fa3504dca512ef11aa97027a5dfcbfc56/comments","author":{"login":"sayan-oai","id":244841968,"node_id":"U_kgDODpf98A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244841968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/sayan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5577a9e1482ed867318dad51a01e5d18a5c5e5fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5577a9e1482ed867318dad51a01e5d18a5c5e5fa","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5577a9e1482ed867318dad51a01e5d18a5c5e5fa"}]},{"sha":"5577a9e1482ed867318dad51a01e5d18a5c5e5fa","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDU1NzdhOWUxNDgyZWQ4NjczMThkYWQ1MWEwMWU1ZDE4YTVjNWU1ZmE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ahmed Ibrahim","email":"aibrahim@openai.com","date":"2026-05-29T16:05:05Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T16:05:05Z"},"message":"[codex] Add model tool mode selector (#25031)\n\n## Why\nSome models need to select their code-execution behavior through model\ncatalog metadata. Models without that metadata must continue to follow\nthe existing `CodeMode` and `CodeModeOnly` feature flags, including when\na newer server sends an enum value this client does not recognize.\n\n## What changed\n- add optional `ModelInfo.tool_mode` metadata with `direct`,\n`code_mode`, and `code_mode_only`\n- treat omitted and unknown wire values as `None`\n- resolve `None` from the existing feature flags\n- carry the resolved `ToolMode` directly on `TurnContext`, outside\n`Config`\n- use the resolved value for turn creation, model switches, review\nturns, tool planning, and code execution\n\n## Coverage\n- add protocol coverage for omitted, known, and unknown enum values\n- add focused coverage for flag fallback and explicit metadata\noverriding feature flags\n- add core integration coverage that fetches remote model metadata\nthrough `/v1/models` and verifies the outbound `/responses` tools for\nexplicit `direct` and `code_mode_only` selectors\n\n## Stack\n- followed by #25032","tree":{"sha":"3bba5ab92421dd2f4c83ec5fec12d417e12cd4a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/3bba5ab92421dd2f4c83ec5fec12d417e12cd4a8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/5577a9e1482ed867318dad51a01e5d18a5c5e5fa","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGbkxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvRAQAKi1UEy8/K4+QvTIjTS2Moda\nzFg7usDfLNAWDzZr1/kVKmFTzOo6B7VdcsVBHp+VjvOoW93NsHFdFksKLfWHzdkn\ncQ8nZ6Ut05+spCG+QMNMVmMcPcMqyEgEBSFj2YGd6NRAwA+pdk8wIErgYNluujnd\nLHVWwahaB4WfX9obLIQLowyTdnsWTQ+tsWFCBkNNpQ4ZdeYDYWqAZ7y0hGh7ovdp\nf5dYXP5NoWqzqH1EUIABefDZkcqYXu/Lnq5tZfjfyNGmHaie2hxf4DMflYWov+Q9\n6z2I+aXdWTUacq6h1PBOhS+oU+iUh2ZVG2coTcxW+jQ2kXPlpNdfif68tqXfHGZd\n1p2cpusUjPgBpJ7kAEIEaqQ/sEJC+Mm9xqNF+onBKDi77jFT/UBuvxYz3/i0Zdtf\nWxxZZTnHmFvr3liGzw/NLQKcdmEAsZYWpA2NEy07ogY28pW9jsnEeHjxNp9VqgeY\njWKi3DXG5/LJNSouUN81+ONtEmM3cbjGMKApSYBBTzIuIIgc5GAl+QH2/Wp8JoYJ\ndCqe1yTK6mhzWyMSZS7j+xe9bJxlGDqw0+Dw3kPUwsrZeGb76IqzjEaAvgoNPxFV\nTchgyKebDTkGhv1fG29PxYFmCIvZrOQyOGO5I8wD8kByrZAdrU1iFaakDDoyohr0\n/QsqNwsMrwkZ3K6YsnOO\n=rM+x\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3bba5ab92421dd2f4c83ec5fec12d417e12cd4a8\nparent 251b2412b2350ba850c92f395a54ba9b666f0c54\nauthor Ahmed Ibrahim <aibrahim@openai.com> 1780070705 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780070705 -0700\n\n[codex] Add model tool mode selector (#25031)\n\n## Why\nSome models need to select their code-execution behavior through model\ncatalog metadata. Models without that metadata must continue to follow\nthe existing `CodeMode` and `CodeModeOnly` feature flags, including when\na newer server sends an enum value this client does not recognize.\n\n## What changed\n- add optional `ModelInfo.tool_mode` metadata with `direct`,\n`code_mode`, and `code_mode_only`\n- treat omitted and unknown wire values as `None`\n- resolve `None` from the existing feature flags\n- carry the resolved `ToolMode` directly on `TurnContext`, outside\n`Config`\n- use the resolved value for turn creation, model switches, review\nturns, tool planning, and code execution\n\n## Coverage\n- add protocol coverage for omitted, known, and unknown enum values\n- add focused coverage for flag fallback and explicit metadata\noverriding feature flags\n- add core integration coverage that fetches remote model metadata\nthrough `/v1/models` and verifies the outbound `/responses` tools for\nexplicit `direct` and `code_mode_only` selectors\n\n## Stack\n- followed by #25032","verified_at":"2026-05-29T16:05:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5577a9e1482ed867318dad51a01e5d18a5c5e5fa","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5577a9e1482ed867318dad51a01e5d18a5c5e5fa","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5577a9e1482ed867318dad51a01e5d18a5c5e5fa/comments","author":{"login":"aibrahim-oai","id":219906144,"node_id":"U_kgDODRuAYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219906144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/aibrahim-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"251b2412b2350ba850c92f395a54ba9b666f0c54","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/251b2412b2350ba850c92f395a54ba9b666f0c54","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/251b2412b2350ba850c92f395a54ba9b666f0c54"}]},{"sha":"251b2412b2350ba850c92f395a54ba9b666f0c54","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDI1MWIyNDEyYjIzNTBiYTg1MGM5MmYzOTVhNTRiYTliNjY2ZjBjNTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Abhinav","email":"abhinav@openai.com","date":"2026-05-29T15:12:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T15:12:40Z"},"message":"Render multiline hook output in TUI (#24965)\n\n# Why\n\nFixes #24529. Completed hook output in the TUI rendered each\n`HookOutputEntry` as one ratatui line, so explicit newlines inside hook\noutput were not shown as separate transcript rows. That made multiline\n`SessionStart.additionalContext` hard to inspect even though the\nmodel-facing context path preserved the original text.\n\n# What\n\n- Split completed hook output entries on explicit newlines before\nrendering them in `codex-rs/tui/src/history_cell/hook_cell.rs`.\n- Keep the hook output prefix, such as `hook context:` or `warning:`, on\nthe first physical line only.\n- Preserve explicit blank lines and render continuation lines with the\nhook body indent.\n- Add unit coverage for multiline context and warning output, plus a\nchatwidget snapshot regression for `SessionStart` history output.\n\n# Testing\n\n- `cargo nextest run -p codex-tui completed_hook_multiline\nhook_completed_before_reveal_renders_completed_without_running_flash`\n- `just argument-comment-lint -p codex-tui -- --ignore-rust-version\n--lib --tests`","tree":{"sha":"9b4a6546864da56760bd601e2047f016a85a818e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/9b4a6546864da56760bd601e2047f016a85a818e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/251b2412b2350ba850c92f395a54ba9b666f0c54","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGazoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIsoQAEPxuek9eEvPDdCt1xjDqnHp\nY5i9Z3QOK0vyj8TCOGjM/1hwY8oLAXAJwjrCQk91ZP7VNUWQ8ZoPUdUpjvqb6nW+\n/9PbGvEqXc4jY3riTAaBxxi9447b21oH8NNfwarpAx3p99C/PGA1uumYp/WuSK9s\n9sIVylyUKs9gTjpDS9FrtdviUWkcSxRA9pJIlcCupEtbjhMdoueWv8Y2SL9niMjH\ns3z/4sm9GBpL6BQGRU9/NUKzw8HQ1MwQ/9OaCuMfzqN2ubdB7vscM/HUqWu4yfTt\npjiGGRd0SHPClPX/0ooQMj5dPpPUPq3l5/hg3BP+Z0YWHaUXK2sLt09KVur7yYxi\n6KcP1sRkWrgwQznZYsOCVSrqtWgKmyYHEnpw53gSxydef6+xGpYtXsCZCxyGRxs1\nE21DkLc2h8K6v39RMMdhZvzT8gDV4eva0TAZpzE8OjruJskUzLDWmPYUZLIc18bD\nbehTAqGB9cA9LJFbkFEKhFZBaNaRLxmQysHZ88BLQ5a+zARZRwaHHmya39lfx7oa\nrR8qHSXjXJH26zhrYcwNecYB7C0SNo3CtM2P/ZN7h5pC2R1OGKiEcvuQxrNmMGZk\nyI8d7+CfbjA2NRvH4qGKfsWKx3vtBh2lXIzY7VyBYXQEo/mI/dT9455oY/hyj0Ua\nf4cvPE/cZst88aIg2XhZ\n=SjwH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9b4a6546864da56760bd601e2047f016a85a818e\nparent b40ad0d84dea8a2c2c4b32e73ef73aff85c5af78\nauthor Abhinav <abhinav@openai.com> 1780067560 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780067560 +0000\n\nRender multiline hook output in TUI (#24965)\n\n# Why\n\nFixes #24529. Completed hook output in the TUI rendered each\n`HookOutputEntry` as one ratatui line, so explicit newlines inside hook\noutput were not shown as separate transcript rows. That made multiline\n`SessionStart.additionalContext` hard to inspect even though the\nmodel-facing context path preserved the original text.\n\n# What\n\n- Split completed hook output entries on explicit newlines before\nrendering them in `codex-rs/tui/src/history_cell/hook_cell.rs`.\n- Keep the hook output prefix, such as `hook context:` or `warning:`, on\nthe first physical line only.\n- Preserve explicit blank lines and render continuation lines with the\nhook body indent.\n- Add unit coverage for multiline context and warning output, plus a\nchatwidget snapshot regression for `SessionStart` history output.\n\n# Testing\n\n- `cargo nextest run -p codex-tui completed_hook_multiline\nhook_completed_before_reveal_renders_completed_without_running_flash`\n- `just argument-comment-lint -p codex-tui -- --ignore-rust-version\n--lib --tests`","verified_at":"2026-05-29T15:12:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/251b2412b2350ba850c92f395a54ba9b666f0c54","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/251b2412b2350ba850c92f395a54ba9b666f0c54","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/251b2412b2350ba850c92f395a54ba9b666f0c54/comments","author":{"login":"abhinav-oai","id":274334565,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFoDZQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274334565?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/abhinav-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.git