0027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8f6a945ec93debbf8e7963b84222b4e007b24a84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8f6a945ec93debbf8e7963b84222b4e007b24a84","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8f6a945ec93debbf8e7963b84222b4e007b24a84"}]},{"sha":"8f6a945ec93debbf8e7963b84222b4e007b24a84","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhmNmE5NDVlYzkzZGViYmY4ZTc5NjNiODQyMjJiNGUwMDdiMjRhODQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif-oai","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-05-29T09:24:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T09:24:39Z"},"message":"Use inject_if_running for active goal steering (#24924)\n\n## Why\n\nThis PR is stacked on #24918, which moves goal steering onto\nsource-labeled internal model context fragments. Active-turn goal\nsteering should use the same running-turn injection path as other\nruntime steering, so those fragments enter the pending input queue as\n`ResponseItem`s through the existing\n[`Session::inject_if_running`](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/8d6f6cdf69b055c27682e7cdea9caf72a3e2ee7f/codex-rs/core/src/session/inject.rs#L12-L27)\nbehavior instead of through a goal-specific conversion wrapper.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Exposes a narrow `CodexThread::inject_if_running` bridge for callers\nthat only hold a thread handle.\n- Changes `ext/goal` active-turn steering to pass `ResponseItem`s\ndirectly.\n- Builds goal steering prompts as contextual internal model context\n`ResponseItem`s before injecting them into the running turn.\n\n## Testing\n\nNot run locally; PR metadata update only.","tree":{"sha":"5038a4220452c7a50f2cac38e4f13a59f5079166","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/5038a4220452c7a50f2cac38e4f13a59f5079166"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8f6a945ec93debbf8e7963b84222b4e007b24a84","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGVtXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWkIQALE+Ybu2aKVDhagP3M2AD/19\nQgJ1j/a+D24/NqdNkUUGEb2i/gmuUXZJQitCwq8SPGwYRmqB3y8fnHrGLIbgeXTR\nA8NYwWEmB4zrCDI30ySmRxHNZojan/jkEA0IjcKNYxXrEtJyA6jEYG04MVvenXUW\n3EP/VstsULsiLQQK+KmXKFJxogav8cqecKVfr3GswXMDaMZH+zdzz7LCUJUBY3Vq\n7tRavLAPyI/Ga3ehRIfiF0/sbsvUfwqUxBat/4IMqT5wKteA88h80c/9Ki9aPx25\nxH+7zj3+Xg9EqT7im1yKGiPt2EScA8MteuBeA4hebH6J0GCK1XLGICzIOsKfOl79\npD9dzdMb5CAHhtwKXga6PEkWRLuYtVCCxxmN90y+FoYmZhTzG+mjGlHAUmsjbTBC\nuDRACva7aFfOyS1nfnRcqcEAXKdcjGsutNN/vCwz3sYMHzX4oDOJF8p4HW72pWNu\nDaeNODKoMgvLvruKTsccsBEo4ar4fcrHc0E2uiDus/BF8KEKWMJZ/ZpuGNqFxyq1\nxk1+myqEZzOPI4lMlkpwphqDH3pRjA8JlPj5NS/UeSf66RHw8h0UPdwQJJ0Tp3E/\nCJ+m04TVRZiDH6zNkmI2OfkxoqMY16/+rQUEWrLoW0iX9Fq15AdzVRZ8P9Yb/OkF\nD4N6r21yNStFSSXoC5eA\n=7dRR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5038a4220452c7a50f2cac38e4f13a59f5079166\nparent 740d942f901a5a63421298c74dafbeb4255e946d\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1780046679 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780046679 +0200\n\nUse inject_if_running for active goal steering (#24924)\n\n## Why\n\nThis PR is stacked on #24918, which moves goal steering onto\nsource-labeled internal model context fragments. Active-turn goal\nsteering should use the same running-turn injection path as other\nruntime steering, so those fragments enter the pending input queue as\n`ResponseItem`s through the existing\n[`Session::inject_if_running`](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/8d6f6cdf69b055c27682e7cdea9caf72a3e2ee7f/codex-rs/core/src/session/inject.rs#L12-L27)\nbehavior instead of through a goal-specific conversion wrapper.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Exposes a narrow `CodexThread::inject_if_running` bridge for callers\nthat only hold a thread handle.\n- Changes `ext/goal` active-turn steering to pass `ResponseItem`s\ndirectly.\n- Builds goal steering prompts as contextual internal model context\n`ResponseItem`s before injecting them into the running turn.\n\n## Testing\n\nNot run locally; PR metadata update only.","verified_at":"2026-05-29T09:24:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8f6a945ec93debbf8e7963b84222b4e007b24a84","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8f6a945ec93debbf8e7963b84222b4e007b24a84","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8f6a945ec93debbf8e7963b84222b4e007b24a84/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"740d942f901a5a63421298c74dafbeb4255e946d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/740d942f901a5a63421298c74dafbeb4255e946d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/740d942f901a5a63421298c74dafbeb4255e946d"}]},{"sha":"740d942f901a5a63421298c74dafbeb4255e946d","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDc0MGQ5NDJmOTAxYTVhNjM0MjEyOThjNzRkYWZiZWI0MjU1ZTk0NmQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif-oai","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-05-29T08:28:25Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T08:28:25Z"},"message":"Use internal model context fragments for goal steering (#24918)\n\n## Why\n\nGoal steering is one form of runtime-owned model context, but the old\n`<goal_context>` wrapper made the contextual-fragment hiding path\ngoal-specific. Using a source-labeled internal context fragment gives\ncore and extensions a shared shape for hidden model steering while\nkeeping those prompts out of visible turn history.\n\nThe change also keeps legacy `<goal_context>` messages recognized as\nhidden contextual input so existing stored history does not start\nrendering old goal-steering prompts as user-visible turn items.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Replaces `GoalContext` with `InternalModelContextFragment` plus a\nvalidated `InternalContextSource`.\n- Renders goal steering as `<codex_internal_context\nsource=\"goal\">...</codex_internal_context>`.\n- Updates core goal steering and `ext/goal` steering to inject the new\ninternal-context fragment.\n- Updates contextual-fragment, event-mapping, goal, and session tests\nfor the new wrapper.\n\n## Test Coverage\n\n- Adds coverage for detecting the new internal model context fragment.\n- Preserves coverage for hiding legacy `<goal_context>` fragments.\n- Verifies invalid internal context sources are rejected and arbitrary\ncontext tags are not hidden.\n- Updates goal steering/session assertions to expect the new\n`source=\"goal\"` wrapper.","tree":{"sha":"b9d5ad711f731ee7d24aa4c9efd5177d61c07a35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/b9d5ad711f731ee7d24aa4c9efd5177d61c07a35"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/740d942f901a5a63421298c74dafbeb4255e946d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGU4pCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/toQALFL6grF/CdDNA+hhwQkA96H\nIHEXcW3JHiX8cMdzfIBz8YYx8smVCxR27ZcPhI2ajxjm1z0FXMMmEoainrIKtzGf\nQ7gAyDLRbYS5As7iwIriD1PD2Fz8NtrdjYJ6wN3WZ2bdJu4TjrMPcJw9yjelndln\n6vheSWlMWlL8c6OhkBhL0HBLzU7pAkmdPbVgNCxRIh/Dw61L2MYbzscBt/00StHq\nqywwuV0ShQdvUHZy6946oIVA3mPE4Dqq/C6PDyNIscisAABQYWqlGNpq2+sSJEvT\njvHuJQ0EeSNj5f7g6w1FVZErUURm5mDZGf3qg2L/dkvt59DXphz4rGXroFajHJd2\noMrT8vVhM/XbzimfmwsdhDckP+QIwEE+X5P0Z6doFH+qhBLE7drc1NWfaLk4d5i0\n2f+Dgxt/955XB+Rfq1jYG0HRYlK4E/TUoa7IYdzgsbyvHO7Leo2Xh38uGe29X2g5\nvxcjzVcrrLRFzGNZoro6MaRPSWvMWNkRKNJl+7kQAxA0y7u6D7V9e5nxoH7wP1YY\nltak+WNAn4Sgs9g/GjwNBwrci5N/SzmVp2POulczavw0VfvFOlYKDF2uvXeZW2jn\ndpl12RSdXz3Zu4tycDUKrC7dqLL+Bym5I10xsOHVSJgY8zd9o1MEzFW3aG1kJ6wD\n67HrWYmRr+nKHwZE8vB0\n=MfOU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b9d5ad711f731ee7d24aa4c9efd5177d61c07a35\nparent 522f549922f6e7b8edbd5e9be3fc720ddb9b256a\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1780043305 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780043305 +0200\n\nUse internal model context fragments for goal steering (#24918)\n\n## Why\n\nGoal steering is one form of runtime-owned model context, but the old\n`<goal_context>` wrapper made the contextual-fragment hiding path\ngoal-specific. Using a source-labeled internal context fragment gives\ncore and extensions a shared shape for hidden model steering while\nkeeping those prompts out of visible turn history.\n\nThe change also keeps legacy `<goal_context>` messages recognized as\nhidden contextual input so existing stored history does not start\nrendering old goal-steering prompts as user-visible turn items.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Replaces `GoalContext` with `InternalModelContextFragment` plus a\nvalidated `InternalContextSource`.\n- Renders goal steering as `<codex_internal_context\nsource=\"goal\">...</codex_internal_context>`.\n- Updates core goal steering and `ext/goal` steering to inject the new\ninternal-context fragment.\n- Updates contextual-fragment, event-mapping, goal, and session tests\nfor the new wrapper.\n\n## Test Coverage\n\n- Adds coverage for detecting the new internal model context fragment.\n- Preserves coverage for hiding legacy `<goal_context>` fragments.\n- Verifies invalid internal context sources are rejected and arbitrary\ncontext tags are not hidden.\n- Updates goal steering/session assertions to expect the new\n`source=\"goal\"` wrapper.","verified_at":"2026-05-29T08:28:25Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/740d942f901a5a63421298c74dafbeb4255e946d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/740d942f901a5a63421298c74dafbeb4255e946d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/740d942f901a5a63421298c74dafbeb4255e946d/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"522f549922f6e7b8edbd5e9be3fc720ddb9b256a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/522f549922f6e7b8edbd5e9be3fc720ddb9b256a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/522f549922f6e7b8edbd5e9be3fc720ddb9b256a"}]},{"sha":"522f549922f6e7b8edbd5e9be3fc720ddb9b256a","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDUyMmY1NDk5MjJmNmU3YjhlZGJkNWU5YmUzZmM3MjBkZGI5YjI1NmE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-05-29T06:09:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T06:09:55Z"},"message":"Fix fs/watch debounce batching (#24716)\n\n## Summary\n\n`fs/watch` was using a local debounce wrapper whose deadline was\ninitialized once and then reused after the first batch. Once that stale\ndeadline was in the past, later file changes could bypass the intended\n200ms debounce and send noisier `fs/changed` notifications.\n\nThis moves the debounce wrapper into `codex-file-watcher` as\n`DebouncedWatchReceiver`, resets the debounce deadline for each event\nbatch, preserves pending paths across cancelled receives, and updates\napp-server `fs/watch` to use the shared wrapper.\n\nFixes #24692.","tree":{"sha":"7b205a69f0f306adcf821e70addb46d8666de072","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/7b205a69f0f306adcf821e70addb46d8666de072"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/522f549922f6e7b8edbd5e9be3fc720ddb9b256a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGS2zCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA018QAGaudZ8bQSaZvr6ptZzstv+m\n89/PdoAO55IUSCmPEoIX3XPwFO9C4vzzhHNMm38KhM3SCFUzSQmWqUNuPSJhgB6w\nKrJQYZSkwCeYYTdDRkkSkYptmDZa7Zls7ue82wK88KdC9BkMfLNstjw33gZFnt8h\nrZiVzU3xY2KfAs+zb1yMYwoZcYUOmwJJWdKZvNs9tgAOESYI8TmFlCt1WTOvJ05h\nl8LivOHS9ReDolV5hhZPzcO6PCyx8nxsQIdveQkAGjwgOGaP2PRDhcicKgM1FfHp\nPRMI/OotJKBvNZxpt33y8o/SdnM/VDT+kf38yAEiVYbhJw6SePxtvko3stKsgqIf\nG5XS7LBcMSqCJtt9nUmYJed5S18QFBwOXhoNP6fz135ub5c5hx2RDCwNm+2x1Ott\n+qJm3mp7jdrbs5Di3gwA2AJcd6rKVVrHRXXlT5V6fwYFEJPvq1rjDTau/Y0vIZ/B\nmrONyfBmfp2K9cHkbY6ywx2l/2EL2eWGGJFjOWgQMqb13eSs1PcKX01yfxuQ4AhE\npUGfoDrDb6RtDC6uN/BLW7jghkRpbFNTGmkeZNS9PZlqoU1a6tXf1AJJ7W59GQDS\nxXxE1Fi3QK0QSIdDLrNm8Yb4IsAlqUK7gxniWKYizR0FOorNuW0QqQ6DUERqlFH2\nHJTahydFHiDThJjM+eea\n=ESex\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7b205a69f0f306adcf821e70addb46d8666de072\nparent 6e1014219979acdadaadd3a1a3b65a0859a11b7e\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1780034995 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780034995 -0700\n\nFix fs/watch debounce batching (#24716)\n\n## Summary\n\n`fs/watch` was using a local debounce wrapper whose deadline was\ninitialized once and then reused after the first batch. Once that stale\ndeadline was in the past, later file changes could bypass the intended\n200ms debounce and send noisier `fs/changed` notifications.\n\nThis moves the debounce wrapper into `codex-file-watcher` as\n`DebouncedWatchReceiver`, resets the debounce deadline for each event\nbatch, preserves pending paths across cancelled receives, and updates\napp-server `fs/watch` to use the shared wrapper.\n\nFixes #24692.","verified_at":"2026-05-29T06:09:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/522f549922f6e7b8edbd5e9be3fc720ddb9b256a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/522f549922f6e7b8edbd5e9be3fc720ddb9b256a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/522f549922f6e7b8edbd5e9be3fc720ddb9b256a/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6e1014219979acdadaadd3a1a3b65a0859a11b7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6e1014219979acdadaadd3a1a3b65a0859a11b7e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6e1014219979acdadaadd3a1a3b65a0859a11b7e"}]},{"sha":"6e1014219979acdadaadd3a1a3b65a0859a11b7e","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDZlMTAxNDIxOTk3OWFjZGFkYWFkZDNhMWEzYjY1YTA4NTlhMTFiN2U","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-05-29T05:49:37Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T05:49:37Z"},"message":"fix: preserve deny-read sandboxing for safe commands (#23943)\n\n## Why\n\nPermission profiles can mark filesystem entries as unreadable with\n`deny` rules, including glob patterns. Several shell execution paths\ntreated known-safe commands or execpolicy `allow` rules as sufficient to\nrun outside the filesystem sandbox. That is not valid for read-capable\ncommands: for example, `cat` or `ls` may be reasonable to allow\ngenerally, but dropping the sandbox would also drop deny-read\nconstraints such as `**/*.env`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added a shared check that treats active deny-read restrictions as\nincompatible with unsandboxed execution.\n- Kept first-attempt execution sandboxed for explicit escalation and\nexecpolicy allow bypasses when deny-read entries are present.\n- Prevented no-sandbox retry after a sandbox denial when the active\nfilesystem policy contains deny-read entries.\n- Updated the zsh-fork execve path so prefix-rule `allow` decisions\ncontinue inside the current sandbox when deny-read restrictions are\nactive.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo test -p codex-core tools::sandboxing::tests`\n- `cargo test -p codex-core\ntools::runtimes::shell::unix_escalation::tests`\n- `cargo test -p codex-core\nshell_command_enforces_glob_deny_read_policy`","tree":{"sha":"69d7ad38b622807ac372006e366b193e0d719ffa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/69d7ad38b622807ac372006e366b193e0d719ffa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6e1014219979acdadaadd3a1a3b65a0859a11b7e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGSjxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3wsQAEtnHoiwUAkcr5a/oHCCVkFq\nMWagtnLKpQBIUW8BvHu81yJQZ+WFCkJICoji8NOuQ4L0vNmXsF/4PC/dFHkOZLAW\n7dPiM+macv3JxtAG+5LTEc+tGmB4TZ2rXzZ0P2YLrzMa2g63n7Yf+8VASOwoUHjp\nnQdpKlYPuD1CdUaWDA6Z5wc8Ii8t3U7F/UprEuVFKLK9QdDR2RQkZNW/wfGAoAXu\nlHdWjK75FpSBZtzheIfGdzL/ew5HDg4ez2bacil1D20ES5czcy5sDew3QhrMWSM9\nb8KC0ZZO7kz/1++XbV8bn0xU5Z9fmKaBzQxbi68ODVmR+BAwT9ZThmhAh66e/BJZ\nC9GHUrmaX11nCsaV330pKWkl9GqgFMJ0HShCxkwRLShNRte5lzKY7dPKY+bXMsWs\njK87D/M7JEtTkmfNaWiZS4rdQrsW6sy/WuzeraBzq125zBimOIYpa7r0DCHBM3V3\nlJJLjCmnER+3YT1XtX7nm2Zzr8R3xn+9qJi61/hrurQOMA1EQNIttcdqNeGo66Gg\nrA9VJBDF3vLu25az5K06Nb0VzIMlOldLWsQzr9nXKcAZvGTQg5ocSCdIPR8yVQ9s\nnUH+TjbQwubrIWSciDG/j0mJXM229hEQ6ed4I74lPQl+Y2bLGG6OX4VxsX51lSlc\nvYzTw6ar1n5oxTDOpV9c\n=4kNm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 69d7ad38b622807ac372006e366b193e0d719ffa\nparent 56958f25125a36777a1cb640297b762e3c4b4a3d\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1780033777 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780033777 -0700\n\nfix: preserve deny-read sandboxing for safe commands (#23943)\n\n## Why\n\nPermission profiles can mark filesystem entries as unreadable with\n`deny` rules, including glob patterns. Several shell execution paths\ntreated known-safe commands or execpolicy `allow` rules as sufficient to\nrun outside the filesystem sandbox. That is not valid for read-capable\ncommands: for example, `cat` or `ls` may be reasonable to allow\ngenerally, but dropping the sandbox would also drop deny-read\nconstraints such as `**/*.env`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added a shared check that treats active deny-read restrictions as\nincompatible with unsandboxed execution.\n- Kept first-attempt execution sandboxed for explicit escalation and\nexecpolicy allow bypasses when deny-read entries are present.\n- Prevented no-sandbox retry after a sandbox denial when the active\nfilesystem policy contains deny-read entries.\n- Updated the zsh-fork execve path so prefix-rule `allow` decisions\ncontinue inside the current sandbox when deny-read restrictions are\nactive.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo test -p codex-core tools::sandboxing::tests`\n- `cargo test -p codex-core\ntools::runtimes::shell::unix_escalation::tests`\n- `cargo test -p codex-core\nshell_command_enforces_glob_deny_read_policy`","verified_at":"2026-05-29T05:49:37Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6e1014219979acdadaadd3a1a3b65a0859a11b7e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6e1014219979acdadaadd3a1a3b65a0859a11b7e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6e1014219979acdadaadd3a1a3b65a0859a11b7e/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"56958f25125a36777a1cb640297b762e3c4b4a3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/56958f25125a36777a1cb640297b762e3c4b4a3d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/56958f25125a36777a1cb640297b762e3c4b4a3d"}]},{"sha":"56958f25125a36777a1cb640297b762e3c4b4a3d","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDU2OTU4ZjI1MTI1YTM2Nzc3YTFjYjY0MDI5N2I3NjJlM2M0YjRhM2Q","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-05-29T05:08:05Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T05:08:05Z"},"message":"Seed prompt history from resumed messages (#24298)\n\n## Why\n\nWhen the TUI resumes a thread, transcript replay renders prior user\nmessages but did not seed the composer history. That leaves the resumed\nsession with empty in-memory prompt history, so pressing Up can fall\nthrough to persisted global history and surface a prompt from another\nthread.\n\nThe expected behavior is that prompts from the resumed thread are\nrecalled first, with global history only as a fallback.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Record replayed user messages into the composer history during resume\nreplay.\n- Preserve the existing persisted history format and avoid any startup\nhistory scan.\n- Add focused TUI coverage showing replayed prompts are recalled before\npersisted global history.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Added `replayed_user_messages_seed_composer_history` in\n`codex-rs/tui/src/chatwidget/tests/history_replay.rs`.\n- `just test -p codex-tui replayed_user_messages_seed_composer_history`\npassed.","tree":{"sha":"daf20916e890556dc185bf09add1ece9d6c9f986","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/daf20916e890556dc185bf09add1ece9d6c9f986"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/56958f25125a36777a1cb640297b762e3c4b4a3d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGR81CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3m0QAF1YoXbMPIPMT5F7pXNUbNGD\nTIwG400ZDvTSa92WPD8OD6X0IeOh3f1v79v33Od0vODjB5HHcNf9QnkPqHDhPKWu\nVQYgWu31OzbvSUzL6PkWeiRLtMuHtFaLIyTE09xPY3iqAIcRj9fOzQJ/VVmQctek\nW7H3xfkEn5CQFTe6sH6wqZ/5JnVdEzD1TPp8RcciCPycZzPDJHbMtzzVkzgBJh6Y\n1CCHParLEytMvNA9DJxlLQW1r7N3zXlo0aaq0oU+I1lLmNlAuZM9rUxJLElCWG7u\noK0jia69OOG/ozFuFP/aLvpGNwSMia1/pj3LP8evS1iQBBusM/cRRirw6q/k4Ss1\nz7x4ERkgpMDmcB/WaXMkvXUPwes4TfotnE1M4ZyhZTqyKHXGa3/x+JfXoua3/L0K\nq3mVZtXa/c0uvRFsQjT+xgPwx1qt0n2mSTZxWuorslVanRjr8JHW2PRbMseNHYZE\nogYnuzL72GgAtu/r2KAlIkoBlo6NXQ08HU+m54pwhmpK+3PJ51//u/ztN9vc02GH\nALSWsPaPbOLntevJ0kyebpgOdyPKy23XdMJcSGfNJcqN5TT9fcvvliIcT+jfk9vk\nIyfIdoWqiv5a85EfzFuShC6tZXBlTwxK2UnI+HPRYrCU0jyZyOciGwpGAYYah5sh\nenU55PvBPnJmJWJRGGTG\n=/rc8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree daf20916e890556dc185bf09add1ece9d6c9f986\nparent f0a839ea0c594a53704b83f6bfde1d557b473cf0\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1780031285 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780031285 -0700\n\nSeed prompt history from resumed messages (#24298)\n\n## Why\n\nWhen the TUI resumes a thread, transcript replay renders prior user\nmessages but did not seed the composer history. That leaves the resumed\nsession with empty in-memory prompt history, so pressing Up can fall\nthrough to persisted global history and surface a prompt from another\nthread.\n\nThe expected behavior is that prompts from the resumed thread are\nrecalled first, with global history only as a fallback.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Record replayed user messages into the composer history during resume\nreplay.\n- Preserve the existing persisted history format and avoid any startup\nhistory scan.\n- Add focused TUI coverage showing replayed prompts are recalled before\npersisted global history.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Added `replayed_user_messages_seed_composer_history` in\n`codex-rs/tui/src/chatwidget/tests/history_replay.rs`.\n- `just test -p codex-tui replayed_user_messages_seed_composer_history`\npassed.","verified_at":"2026-05-29T05:08:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/56958f25125a36777a1cb640297b762e3c4b4a3d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/56958f25125a36777a1cb640297b762e3c4b4a3d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/56958f25125a36777a1cb640297b762e3c4b4a3d/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f0a839ea0c594a53704b83f6bfde1d557b473cf0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f0a839ea0c594a53704b83f6bfde1d557b473cf0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f0a839ea0c594a53704b83f6bfde1d557b473cf0"}]},{"sha":"f0a839ea0c594a53704b83f6bfde1d557b473cf0","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGYwYTgzOWVhMGM1OTRhNTM3MDRiODNmNmJmZGUxZDU1N2I0NzNjZjA","commit":{"author":{"name":"xl-openai","email":"xl@openai.com","date":"2026-05-29T04:14:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T04:14:34Z"},"message":"Add runtime extra skill roots API (#24977)\n\n## Summary\n- Add v2 `skills/extraRoots/set` to replace app-server process-local\nstandalone skill roots. The setting is not persisted, accepts missing\nroots, and `extraRoots: []` clears the runtime set.\n- Wire runtime roots into core skill discovery for `skills/list` and\nturn loads, clear skill caches on set, and register the roots with the\nskills watcher so later filesystem changes emit `skills/changed`.\n- Update app-server docs, generated JSON/TypeScript schemas, and\ncoverage for serialization, missing roots, empty clears, and restart\nbehavior.\n\n## Testing\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `cargo test -p codex-core-skills`\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server\nskills_extra_roots_set_updates_process_runtime_roots`\n- `just fix -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just fix -p codex-core-skills`\n- `just fix -p codex-app-server`","tree":{"sha":"1d5a2536ffea1e88e992b79f28c44eb29153677d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/1d5a2536ffea1e88e992b79f28c44eb29153677d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f0a839ea0c594a53704b83f6bfde1d557b473cf0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGRKqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7qUQACkzLceBmAwS76AM/5/wCW0m\nyyYQJHzl6jsvULzSNtMlqq9Gt2qlHRdBVWHb0baNYdM1IRZ8NEVxHEm6gKyRUFdN\ngcgsNmghC4pnrTyGL4T27IHdntINFTEfAn3oXjst79zn7ho1HXTIRiustpuWyydp\nN1Ma5slL4dRtaxJbsBa86Okc8cBmlhHaQeIIWXqXyLF/BRu9syuhmx9kxIali3K+\n3XX3mvbuP5RiQZl/NQsdCOwhqKKqpmzXRZ6sIO+ISfvs1chKSvD5c6q4vl9psBKr\nH6/+bZ2nKZwVJGuPpYX6NOm9VwWB+tUPhjH1n0Xe6QhF81XwA9aIxyyktxV2RZ1M\n/HtyMNrVSPLTMi5hzKJNjjQTUWoDoTy3EmW3CAmPp2g9HKwYRUxmUJpYtHpmxv6/\nbERQ9R1Cf/E/0/B5B6kE1mz/UKRJ/CS/QeUW4vyoYG3bJNcWeQg6jrPBeUVUbkUl\nSFVDn3dZncIKcCuS2NShtKD+MbRcFn+Q3ALdtwqd7bkxQTbXS5zc9MwD5zgtdy4/\nIdETbJdl4M5ZAkSOqF5uqLt6kK1gxrbm8JZEZUgc6h0Z/nz8DVB9kCNOMWCAWTWr\nRJoO8tfS3eJ6Azr/6D++WgNZTPW/VmkB0BfCHO+t/LcJatpCVMh5BiqgA8yNdrsN\nC+CMpPEoQcchI8zgRKDW\n=1Nbd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1d5a2536ffea1e88e992b79f28c44eb29153677d\nparent 42c80385cd6e2c8efc8b85c39bb9bde5edf01fc3\nauthor xl-openai <xl@openai.com> 1780028074 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780028074 -0700\n\nAdd runtime extra skill roots API (#24977)\n\n## Summary\n- Add v2 `skills/extraRoots/set` to replace app-server process-local\nstandalone skill roots. The setting is not persisted, accepts missing\nroots, and `extraRoots: []` clears the runtime set.\n- Wire runtime roots into core skill discovery for `skills/list` and\nturn loads, clear skill caches on set, and register the roots with the\nskills watcher so later filesystem changes emit `skills/changed`.\n- Update app-server docs, generated JSON/TypeScript schemas, and\ncoverage for serialization, missing roots, empty clears, and restart\nbehavior.\n\n## Testing\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `cargo test -p codex-core-skills`\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server\nskills_extra_roots_set_updates_process_runtime_roots`\n- `just fix -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just fix -p codex-core-skills`\n- `just fix -p codex-app-server`","verified_at":"2026-05-29T04:14:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f0a839ea0c594a53704b83f6bfde1d557b473cf0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f0a839ea0c594a53704b83f6bfde1d557b473cf0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f0a839ea0c594a53704b83f6bfde1d557b473cf0/comments","author":{"login":"xl-openai","id":184293535,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvwYnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184293535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/xl-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"42c80385cd6e2c8efc8b85c39bb9bde5edf01fc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/42c80385cd6e2c8efc8b85c39bb9bde5edf01fc3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/42c80385cd6e2c8efc8b85c39bb9bde5edf01fc3"}]},{"sha":"42c80385cd6e2c8efc8b85c39bb9bde5edf01fc3","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDQyYzgwMzg1Y2Q2ZTJjOGVmYzhiODVjMzliYjliZGU1ZWRmMDFmYzM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adrian","email":"145513011+adrian-openai@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-05-29T03:00:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T03:00:35Z"},"message":"[codex] Avoid PowerShell safety parsing off Windows (#24946)\n\n## Summary\n\nThis fixes BUGB-17567 by preventing non-Windows command safety\nclassification from invoking the Windows PowerShell safelist/parser\npath.\n\nPreviously, `is_known_safe_command` called the Windows PowerShell\nclassifier on every platform. That classifier recognizes\n`pwsh`/`powershell` by basename and delegates script parsing to the\nPowerShell AST parser. The parser starts the supplied executable, so on\nmacOS/Linux a repository-controlled `pwsh` path could execute during\nsafety parsing before the normal sandboxed command execution path.\n\nThe change gates the Windows PowerShell classifier and module behind\n`#[cfg(windows)]`. On macOS/Linux, PowerShell-looking commands are no\nlonger auto-approved by the Windows classifier and instead fall through\nto the normal non-Windows safe-command logic.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `/private/tmp/codex-tools/bin/just fmt`\n- `PATH=/private/tmp/codex-tools/bin:$PATH\n/private/tmp/codex-tools/bin/just test -p codex-shell-command`\n\nThe focused test run passed 135 tests with 0 skipped and completed the\ncrate bench-smoke step.\n\n## Notes\n\nThis PR is scoped to the BUGB-17567 macOS/Linux path. Windows still uses\nthe PowerShell classifier; a separate hardening follow-up should ensure\nWindows safety parsing only executes a trusted PowerShell parser binary\nand does not spawn the command's `argv[0]` when that path may be\nrepository-controlled.","tree":{"sha":"e3a4cfd8168877964c9df29a589035552c0fa65e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e3a4cfd8168877964c9df29a589035552c0fa65e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/42c80385cd6e2c8efc8b85c39bb9bde5edf01fc3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGQFTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8pcQAI5atnzahuVyUtDhy3Tsm9YG\n51kgUIizlxvU9j/rFqZ59bhRx/FnvRnZzes7yl1S3VRkR6P0JaaGC+/02ahyTO+y\nhKPINQLQ+QKMkwDjjfTFXinMOOpHjhCM8I0rqlmDSe6IDVpRVtGqyx79igOHRPUY\nt/r7eTkSIz6erGDNqMiGTjJgqRTqdE38v6QdtLpkKQ/qzI9Q7trHzyk+NI0DBb6w\nrgfqg7Q6ZZmjcVP/CsqpckmeIButBj9Jsvij3Kt1dQsPKnUvBndnbwmXS/mfPIwD\nLt8ncO20kDsU2EBmwFPabRZdsn53WRFVU3iTphqEDxYoQ1FNfmhs2mSsEtmn03+X\n0njOXKuvjeEbQvOTKBQsguFJPkwt/3LwDmDce61eJSl1cjmKAqGdOgdEcZkiK42w\nL3njn3x2RL4Jtvksn+clbp3aXjmJnsNHtsZM0X7vleafI/ysoc87MB5bB6KfKnOY\npqWhvJEJ2wdZTSNxslGs/RuB2fkxZDgiej+sM9sfYmvKljbPRuvNE8N/9Ml4MX9w\nXeOi5skCN/ZOGXK2LZgxfR1QsrgAxZxScPJPZUkGiidCCtDnjLQngEwsCqhFNmET\nsXP5DCKpIl9x51CQT8z7w3rng/3iqreOEy3i/DfB9g5NfIyYijfe3IvmK/v7rE9D\nbtfpaIgxeXMY0xupjpLr\n=wIU0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e3a4cfd8168877964c9df29a589035552c0fa65e\nparent bf72be59278e23002a352a53207182985cabb9d0\nauthor Adrian <145513011+adrian-openai@users.noreply.github.com> 1780023635 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780023635 +0000\n\n[codex] Avoid PowerShell safety parsing off Windows (#24946)\n\n## Summary\n\nThis fixes BUGB-17567 by preventing non-Windows command safety\nclassification from invoking the Windows PowerShell safelist/parser\npath.\n\nPreviously, `is_known_safe_command` called the Windows PowerShell\nclassifier on every platform. That classifier recognizes\n`pwsh`/`powershell` by basename and delegates script parsing to the\nPowerShell AST parser. The parser starts the supplied executable, so on\nmacOS/Linux a repository-controlled `pwsh` path could execute during\nsafety parsing before the normal sandboxed command execution path.\n\nThe change gates the Windows PowerShell classifier and module behind\n`#[cfg(windows)]`. On macOS/Linux, PowerShell-looking commands are no\nlonger auto-approved by the Windows classifier and instead fall through\nto the normal non-Windows safe-command logic.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `/private/tmp/codex-tools/bin/just fmt`\n- `PATH=/private/tmp/codex-tools/bin:$PATH\n/private/tmp/codex-tools/bin/just test -p codex-shell-command`\n\nThe focused test run passed 135 tests with 0 skipped and completed the\ncrate bench-smoke step.\n\n## Notes\n\nThis PR is scoped to the BUGB-17567 macOS/Linux path. Windows still uses\nthe PowerShell classifier; a separate hardening follow-up should ensure\nWindows safety parsing only executes a trusted PowerShell parser binary\nand does not spawn the command's `argv[0]` when that path may be\nrepository-controlled.","verified_at":"2026-05-29T03:00:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/42c80385cd6e2c8efc8b85c39bb9bde5edf01fc3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/42c80385cd6e2c8efc8b85c39bb9bde5edf01fc3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/42c80385cd6e2c8efc8b85c39bb9bde5edf01fc3/comments","author":{"login":"adrian-openai","id":145513011,"node_id":"U_kgDOCKxaMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145513011?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/adrian-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adrian-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bf72be59278e23002a352a53207182985cabb9d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bf72be59278e23002a352a53207182985cabb9d0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bf72be59278e23002a352a53207182985cabb9d0"}]},{"sha":"bf72be59278e23002a352a53207182985cabb9d0","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGJmNzJiZTU5Mjc4ZTIzMDAyYTM1MmE1MzIwNzE4Mjk4NWNhYmI5ZDA","commit":{"author":{"name":"viyatb-oai","email":"viyatb@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T23:53:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T23:53:26Z"},"message":"fix(config): use deny for Unix socket permissions (#24970)\n\n## Why\n\nUnix socket permissions still accepted and displayed `\"none\"` while file\npermissions use the clearer `\"deny\"` spelling. This keeps network Unix\nsocket policy vocabulary consistent with filesystem policy vocabulary.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Replace the Unix socket permission variant and serialized spelling\nfrom `none` to `deny` across config, feature configuration, and network\nproxy types.\n- Update app-server v2 serialization, TUI debug output, focused tests,\nand generated schemas to expose `\"deny\"`.\n- Add coverage for denied Unix socket entries in managed requirements\nand profile overlay behavior.\n\n## Security\n\nThis is a vocabulary change for explicit Unix socket rejection, not a\nnetwork access expansion. Denied entries continue to be omitted from the\neffective allowlist.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just write-config-schema`\n- `just write-app-server-schema`\n- `just test -p codex-config -p codex-core -p codex-app-server-protocol\n-p codex-tui -E\n'test(network_requirements_are_preserved_as_constraints_with_source) |\ntest(network_permission_containers_project_allowed_and_denied_entries) |\ntest(network_toml_overlays_unix_socket_permissions_by_path) |\ntest(permissions_profiles_resolve_extends_parent_first_with_child_overrides)\n| test(network_requirements_serializes_canonical_and_legacy_fields) |\ntest(debug_config_output_formats_unix_socket_permissions)'`\\n- Automatic\n`bench-smoke` follow-up from `just test`\\n- `cargo clippy -p\ncodex-config -p codex-core -p codex-features -p codex-network-proxy -p\ncodex-app-server-protocol -p codex-app-server -p codex-tui --all-targets\n-- -D warnings`","tree":{"sha":"5cea5d07b95c2a9fef308adb7e9a0fdffaed0d28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/5cea5d07b95c2a9fef308adb7e9a0fdffaed0d28"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/bf72be59278e23002a352a53207182985cabb9d0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGNV2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJdoQAAONBi9Ou5DVYI00VrUYgL4P\nozIvfos9Cx4frpPkw+Tljnd9jSdwZXZEiHb7YwWzgXR493vijqsyQjageztsM95L\nXR9raUFIfKMoWXNTEPk9DCD+kpziuZ80/QSD1equiWGwXEIZHOPhqfoQdKRFP1Da\n0xHWbbjMhTDOOqV/duyHwiLCiAPC1wax1p+ssAbpixk2M6Sb0fT11kwSsYPY+fql\nDdJzAgehu7s0GkAal0bH9ycPF46YRu64pg89bHVpR7lfJIZHqFTbgmCEaLRWpv2s\n5KWZvPmtUJZ1/vCXKQz0nOGOcitZyBQzwbbjoPzqUm5zfw5BXy23RcNs/EKMkpnx\nI0f+TAcMpAody3y3N/Gk/3Z48AHajzCe3TkwzjOlnLN3Rvg/slpFxDcpot2sAak4\ndO57DJ5LWrGXt0EEqFviS5PipZk9wM0RlsQswjoRs9xbkRglKTBc4h1Mq0cIi4bz\n/te3uIeBHEi9puP9NO2hKx9ynqR1bMnUvpmJR2XN2J3TE5DeQp+wtPgAGaR/d6YM\n2P1UkCFLaMcVkBEcronWfE0ZSrb6UY6Lan0+rCeOXdZXUvwK0RvUhf4xyjuvdQsg\n9NsAySCqS3AcdHZGDzB5tb63fDfxdq1MgF+jtP/EU4DLjglfyQS+qq+XykO0zMkA\nhNR0NBsBR55nquOK38ua\n=Bw2o\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5cea5d07b95c2a9fef308adb7e9a0fdffaed0d28\nparent 912d7d4f75767a52b9baac64ee49ad9159cb7bb9\nauthor viyatb-oai <viyatb@openai.com> 1780012406 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780012406 +0000\n\nfix(config): use deny for Unix socket permissions (#24970)\n\n## Why\n\nUnix socket permissions still accepted and displayed `\"none\"` while file\npermissions use the clearer `\"deny\"` spelling. This keeps network Unix\nsocket policy vocabulary consistent with filesystem policy vocabulary.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Replace the Unix socket permission variant and serialized spelling\nfrom `none` to `deny` across config, feature configuration, and network\nproxy types.\n- Update app-server v2 serialization, TUI debug output, focused tests,\nand generated schemas to expose `\"deny\"`.\n- Add coverage for denied Unix socket entries in managed requirements\nand profile overlay behavior.\n\n## Security\n\nThis is a vocabulary change for explicit Unix socket rejection, not a\nnetwork access expansion. Denied entries continue to be omitted from the\neffective allowlist.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just write-config-schema`\n- `just write-app-server-schema`\n- `just test -p codex-config -p codex-core -p codex-app-server-protocol\n-p codex-tui -E\n'test(network_requirements_are_preserved_as_constraints_with_source) |\ntest(network_permission_containers_project_allowed_and_denied_entries) |\ntest(network_toml_overlays_unix_socket_permissions_by_path) |\ntest(permissions_profiles_resolve_extends_parent_first_with_child_overrides)\n| test(network_requirements_serializes_canonical_and_legacy_fields) |\ntest(debug_config_output_formats_unix_socket_permissions)'`\\n- Automatic\n`bench-smoke` follow-up from `just test`\\n- `cargo clippy -p\ncodex-config -p codex-core -p codex-features -p codex-network-proxy -p\ncodex-app-server-protocol -p codex-app-server -p codex-tui --all-targets\n-- -D warnings`","verified_at":"2026-05-28T23:53:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bf72be59278e23002a352a53207182985cabb9d0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bf72be59278e23002a352a53207182985cabb9d0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bf72be59278e23002a352a53207182985cabb9d0/comments","author":{"login":"viyatb-oai","id":234056686,"node_id":"U_kgDODfNr7g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234056686?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/viyatb-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"912d7d4f75767a52b9baac64ee49ad9159cb7bb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/912d7d4f75767a52b9baac64ee49ad9159cb7bb9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/912d7d4f75767a52b9baac64ee49ad9159cb7bb9"}]},{"sha":"912d7d4f75767a52b9baac64ee49ad9159cb7bb9","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDkxMmQ3ZDRmNzU3NjdhNTJiOWJhYWM2NGVlNDlhZDkxNTljYjdiYjk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Anton Panasenko","email":"apanasenko@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T22:57:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T22:57:08Z"},"message":"feat(app-server): migrate remote control to server tokens (#24141)\n\n## Why\n\n`codex-backend` now authenticates remote-control server websocket\nconnections with short-lived server tokens instead of the user's ChatGPT\naccess token. `app-server` needs to mint and refresh those server tokens\nwithout persisting them, so a restart can reconnect from durable\nenrollment identity while keeping the bearer token memory-only.\n\n## What Changed\n\nUpdated the remote-control transport to consume `remote_control_token`\nand `expires_at` from server enroll responses and added\n`/server/refresh` support for persisted enrollments or expiring cached\ntokens.\n\nWebsocket handshakes now send `Authorization: Bearer\n<remote_control_token>` with the existing server identity headers, and\nno longer send the ChatGPT bearer token or `chatgpt-account-id` on that\nwebsocket path.\n\nThe in-memory enrollment state now owns the ephemeral server token\ncache, while SQLite still persists only `server_id`, `environment_id`,\nand `server_name`. Websocket `401`/`403` clears only the cached token\nfor refresh on reconnect; websocket or refresh `404` clears stale\npersisted enrollment and re-enrolls. Response body previews redact\n`remote_control_token` before surfacing parse errors.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-transport`\n- Manual prod smoke with an isolated `CODEX_HOME`: `codex remote-control\n--json -c 'chatgpt_base_url=\"https://chatgpt.com/backend-api\"'` reached\n`status:\"connected\"` with\n`environmentId:\"env_i_6a17d9f1d764832986da2e80f4554f1b\"`.","tree":{"sha":"04f5c4b7648afeebdd0b61e19d88e6714c41a453","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/04f5c4b7648afeebdd0b61e19d88e6714c41a453"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/912d7d4f75767a52b9baac64ee49ad9159cb7bb9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGMhECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQQAQAC10qSzoxnpqnvTM4JKBdP7L\nWkmJ7vjAJLVuPR3kgecdBT6KV9+edLiAMeqpmGZEqlvhV9vzvahS98vNITcY7pMI\nTLqT71GA38YRP2y16wnGbMmSJY8P0DPjQN9zpHF6RbLRXj13Q08RAMN1CFrZa4Eg\nLSwlcSSpXq7hqst9AsHe+tksd71/YwOU1Z2hnbEIKfP9oYtioqCUvhymwbO/0vzh\n96FFz6SrNSnNUEw1kVmx0L02qR6jruglhFyloK9PDTg/4oUgnd49+IfAo2Prq+JX\nKBhwtYh7+zwOUUHMAqbr159Fz/tgBUpARoO9+zM4KeHYi+quZ6TmveOb9pyPrNkn\nx/K1R7Fw1Yqk6fxvRkAZs08CRZB+bu7NXfj5ZnVFgTglmbB5zSt9G5Y64oS7oBHq\ngnYpeb7zopUIkQhI6UJcp7anAnHLwFlqJwWvRhptdWH1ViDA+M0UICYBU7cAAXnL\nBCrwRScNwaF9liiyqDk2YWGf4zVQhdRDoiiGpvfTTtAsIKiGI9J8fxRzWntQj6d4\n7EA/+/HB7wc5cjrkCD8hgSfmZRm0c0rfio6pGwuQC5WQ9zjySttDGvnJCJvWQqBP\n1tFh4LhJwxLHGq3w2TmJudpmYR3B9Pb0Qf2ecvc3JmL9Amyxe2PI+6AAatXFuYXK\nsZxd5xhDk3GiLNjZea6d\n=DtkI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 04f5c4b7648afeebdd0b61e19d88e6714c41a453\nparent a576be2b7337dcbb3b46f6f4975a3f3409603683\nauthor Anton Panasenko <apanasenko@openai.com> 1780009028 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780009028 -0700\n\nfeat(app-server): migrate remote control to server tokens (#24141)\n\n## Why\n\n`codex-backend` now authenticates remote-control server websocket\nconnections with short-lived server tokens instead of the user's ChatGPT\naccess token. `app-server` needs to mint and refresh those server tokens\nwithout persisting them, so a restart can reconnect from durable\nenrollment identity while keeping the bearer token memory-only.\n\n## What Changed\n\nUpdated the remote-control transport to consume `remote_control_token`\nand `expires_at` from server enroll responses and added\n`/server/refresh` support for persisted enrollments or expiring cached\ntokens.\n\nWebsocket handshakes now send `Authorization: Bearer\n<remote_control_token>` with the existing server identity headers, and\nno longer send the ChatGPT bearer token or `chatgpt-account-id` on that\nwebsocket path.\n\nThe in-memory enrollment state now owns the ephemeral server token\ncache, while SQLite still persists only `server_id`, `environment_id`,\nand `server_name`. Websocket `401`/`403` clears only the cached token\nfor refresh on reconnect; websocket or refresh `404` clears stale\npersisted enrollment and re-enrolls. Response body previews redact\n`remote_control_token` before surfacing parse errors.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-transport`\n- Manual prod smoke with an isolated `CODEX_HOME`: `codex remote-control\n--json -c 'chatgpt_base_url=\"https://chatgpt.com/backend-api\"'` reached\n`status:\"connected\"` with\n`environmentId:\"env_i_6a17d9f1d764832986da2e80f4554f1b\"`.","verified_at":"2026-05-28T22:57:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/912d7d4f75767a52b9baac64ee49ad9159cb7bb9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/912d7d4f75767a52b9baac64ee49ad9159cb7bb9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/912d7d4f75767a52b9baac64ee49ad9159cb7bb9/comments","author":{"login":"apanasenko-oai","id":228802911,"node_id":"U_kgDODaNBXw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228802911?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/apanasenko-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a576be2b7337dcbb3b46f6f4975a3f3409603683","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a576be2b7337dcbb3b46f6f4975a3f3409603683","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a576be2b7337dcbb3b46f6f4975a3f3409603683"}]},{"sha":"a576be2b7337dcbb3b46f6f4975a3f3409603683","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGE1NzZiZTJiNzMzN2RjYmIzYjQ2ZjZmNDk3NWEzZjM0MDk2MDM2ODM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Abhinav","email":"abhinav@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T22:55:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T22:55:40Z"},"message":"Tighten hook output event schemas (#24962)\n\n# Why\n\nFixes #23993.\n\nHook command output schemas are published as the contract for hook\nauthors and schema-driven tooling. The event-specific output schemas\npreviously described `hookSpecificOutput.hookEventName` as the global\n`HookEventNameWire` enum, so a `pre-tool-use.command.output` schema\nwould validate mismatched values like `PostToolUse`. That made the\nschemas less precise than the intended event-specific contract.\n\n# What\n\nConstrain each hook-specific output schema to the matching literal\n`hookEventName` value, mirroring the existing input-schema shape.\n\nAlso split `SubagentStartHookSpecificOutputWire` from the session-start\noutput wire so `subagent-start.command.output.schema.json` can emit\n`const: \"SubagentStart\"` instead of sharing the session-start\ndefinition.\n\n# Verification\n\n- `cargo nextest run -p codex-hooks`\n- `just fix -p codex-hooks`\n- `just argument-comment-lint -p codex-hooks -- --all-targets`","tree":{"sha":"8548ac66c9c83a035efb2022cbee21576502910c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/8548ac66c9c83a035efb2022cbee21576502910c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a576be2b7337dcbb3b46f6f4975a3f3409603683","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGMfsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvB4QAFPJoDo0AocHorGLBC0O3NLF\nI5TRZl9LjSEWi55SKF0Uft/F3IDNAwn4Ew8FNW5KLELkJ1CvUeVspbkhwk5VxMyQ\nMiqHiR/5/F+OG8J6eVwXENFMKf+SpsxetT3cMaCG/A7DA3lCxxayFc9C6kB2lW4V\nQQO5euucNnLem7c6josq+Kq9KZNULLUq0rr0JVWkkRTZhAoUp9rtTHpICTKgsBTc\nwZNM5aSKxPSaTMK/edYcO0uNizVPmAPWW5TBJiMFJSqd7G3CTRiMsZ26FbEf1M3X\nkbTt2R4GJkknco0JlaLCLXetH4kYdD63zb9BYU1+sGB85rYhFmfwbyhTJRrCO+NW\nNPjL6DGK0epDb10BwgWMfuSTL84lkRpJGmQCDUI4pNo2bTrEWHFRpQXY8tgbh3Np\n26u56LaYklpCPAJsu8mlbBBeoXrBE2xjbIbZgxUM8KAvjM+llU1damei0nkhvDAt\nGYKc/Usqd2Z1Vx3qwzQRN3U/dah8/simtLXPMoPqb5IuB3F6+BiSAWoaasADlyV8\ndvd1ZLmOcrd3spJr+tPxujVYeBlL6w1UBmCi92ygxRDyhFj5puQ1SVLDaDSzPfHR\ngA4jRDlE77VuEBoKNECewIoDIpg13x37vemEE/weN7cOe+GQHjKt2bVDOAnq3fgD\nBnWO3TuBKKh6rDaSNu3y\n=VMGO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8548ac66c9c83a035efb2022cbee21576502910c\nparent bcf2b559577285ea0fda54b142f30d1d718b9254\nauthor Abhinav <abhinav@openai.com> 1780008940 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780008940 -0700\n\nTighten hook output event schemas (#24962)\n\n# Why\n\nFixes #23993.\n\nHook command output schemas are published as the contract for hook\nauthors and schema-driven tooling. The event-specific output schemas\npreviously described `hookSpecificOutput.hookEventName` as the global\n`HookEventNameWire` enum, so a `pre-tool-use.command.output` schema\nwould validate mismatched values like `PostToolUse`. That made the\nschemas less precise than the intended event-specific contract.\n\n# What\n\nConstrain each hook-specific output schema to the matching literal\n`hookEventName` value, mirroring the existing input-schema shape.\n\nAlso split `SubagentStartHookSpecificOutputWire` from the session-start\noutput wire so `subagent-start.command.output.schema.json` can emit\n`const: \"SubagentStart\"` instead of sharing the session-start\ndefinition.\n\n# Verification\n\n- `cargo nextest run -p codex-hooks`\n- `just fix -p codex-hooks`\n- `just argument-comment-lint -p codex-hooks -- --all-targets`","verified_at":"2026-05-28T22:55:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a576be2b7337dcbb3b46f6f4975a3f3409603683","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a576be2b7337dcbb3b46f6f4975a3f3409603683","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a576be2b7337dcbb3b46f6f4975a3f3409603683/comments","author":{"login":"abhinav-oai","id":274334565,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFoDZQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274334565?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/abhinav-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bcf2b559577285ea0fda54b142f30d1d718b9254","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bcf2b559577285ea0fda54b142f30d1d718b9254","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bcf2b559577285ea0fda54b142f30d1d718b9254"}]},{"sha":"bcf2b559577285ea0fda54b142f30d1d718b9254","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGJjZjJiNTU5NTc3Mjg1ZWEwZmRhNTRiMTQyZjMwZDFkNzE4YjkyNTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T22:51:27Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T22:51:27Z"},"message":"windows-sandbox: fix capture cancellation test roots (#24974)\n\n## Why\n\nThe Windows Bazel job on `main` started failing after #24108 because one\nWindows-only capture test still passed `cwd.as_path()` to\n`run_windows_sandbox_capture`. That helper now expects the explicit\n`workspace_roots` slice introduced by #24108, so the Windows test target\nno longer compiled.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Updates `legacy_capture_cancellation_is_not_reported_as_timeout` to\npass `workspace_roots_for(cwd.as_path()).as_slice()`, matching the\nadjacent capture test and the new runner signature.\n\n## Verification\n\n- GitHub Actions CI is the important validation for this Windows-only\ncompile path.\n- Created quickly to get Windows CI running while the separate Ubuntu\n`compact_resume_fork` timeout is still under investigation.","tree":{"sha":"05082e0ed467d50c3b68f7936ab9cada13108416","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/05082e0ed467d50c3b68f7936ab9cada13108416"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/bcf2b559577285ea0fda54b142f30d1d718b9254","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGMbvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArxgQAJDDVEDZL/ZnZsGCOf4TT99w\neY47eEg6TCsteE3EQMblaciFxMWfyDVrnUSkH0ZJLUsmeuuC8iU0mt+91pBzkqDI\n7LDivbQVBKhivtQiT0m0k/h87ygy7ZcfS0svSUMw9Rd+NIfs+hpUH09pdOpy5cdi\nu8nga+auJE73xaH+4VTVol3ppS/PinW0F8EQBVCKEIaHdXY6zeF8Xca7MjGSpKez\nnMeH1F6pJxwmsdMtiy2RrTCiToDVZoggNwQZ/61Okwf2svSQfik/ry9Pb4l+3s13\nZukyAAcQxwpXSXqRhyPkeVt5vZNtz5YjxD2uOme6VZMVU9eytnf51rRtUoZzyCfk\nKTW9UhFBugJ8oqhVnq6LchVFcn76R4UfCB7/MLCdQIAUyV+8mDWQmUUJe5vIOla+\n6fl8xXirUqUY/3AVlMwNq8TRuHg88rlTkKbxpJRpd99k4VGk5GOh+RIZeyKMBuG4\nZvir4vvTNejUf2Kc9PsYP3/Sod/OQcUFPdmwYQOlaN1oYkItylXb7gLT/k9aFrbN\nwC7xwIhBA3EIqsCBptf+iSDSLK2haXUhgjGEUm97XbE/5NIzP89idc2su5x9DrqG\nzde0vLH+D1aX+xDzDTpvIhuN51/jaYBy3v3L3DNRlMbobHq5cyJk/nz6QZfFEY5N\nZpW4M2IJaaV/W0MtG8St\n=bBJH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 05082e0ed467d50c3b68f7936ab9cada13108416\nparent 986c60467b96ca13850217f6e5adadef6ba70ab3\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1780008687 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780008687 -0700\n\nwindows-sandbox: fix capture cancellation test roots (#24974)\n\n## Why\n\nThe Windows Bazel job on `main` started failing after #24108 because one\nWindows-only capture test still passed `cwd.as_path()` to\n`run_windows_sandbox_capture`. That helper now expects the explicit\n`workspace_roots` slice introduced by #24108, so the Windows test target\nno longer compiled.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Updates `legacy_capture_cancellation_is_not_reported_as_timeout` to\npass `workspace_roots_for(cwd.as_path()).as_slice()`, matching the\nadjacent capture test and the new runner signature.\n\n## Verification\n\n- GitHub Actions CI is the important validation for this Windows-only\ncompile path.\n- Created quickly to get Windows CI running while the separate Ubuntu\n`compact_resume_fork` timeout is still under investigation.","verified_at":"2026-05-28T22:51:28Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bcf2b559577285ea0fda54b142f30d1d718b9254","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bcf2b559577285ea0fda54b142f30d1d718b9254","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bcf2b559577285ea0fda54b142f30d1d718b9254/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"986c60467b96ca13850217f6e5adadef6ba70ab3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/986c60467b96ca13850217f6e5adadef6ba70ab3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/986c60467b96ca13850217f6e5adadef6ba70ab3"}]},{"sha":"986c60467b96ca13850217f6e5adadef6ba70ab3","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDk4NmM2MDQ2N2I5NmNhMTM4NTAyMTdmNmU1YWRhZGVmNmJhNzBhYjM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T22:26:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T22:26:55Z"},"message":"windows-sandbox: pass workspace roots to runner (#24108)\n\n## Why\n\n#23813 switches the Windows sandbox runner path to `PermissionProfile`,\nbut it still left one runtime anchor for resolving symbolic\n`:workspace_roots` entries. That is not enough once a turn has multiple\neffective workspace roots: exact entries and deny globs under\n`:workspace_roots` need to be materialized for every runtime root before\nthe command runner chooses token mode or builds ACL plans.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Replaces the Windows runner/setup `permission_profile_cwd` plumbing\nwith `workspace_roots: Vec<AbsolutePathBuf>`.\n- Resolves Windows-local `PermissionProfile` data with\n`materialize_project_roots_with_workspace_roots(...)` instead of the\nsingle-cwd helper.\n- Threads `Config::effective_workspace_roots()` through core execution,\nunified exec, TUI setup/read-grant flows, app-server setup, app-server\n`command/exec`, and `debug sandbox` on Windows.\n- Preserves those workspace roots through the zsh-fork escalation\nexecutor instead of rebuilding them from `sandbox_policy_cwd`.\n- Makes `ExecRequest::new(...)` and the remaining\n`build_exec_request(...)` helper path take\n`windows_sandbox_workspace_roots` explicitly so new call sites cannot\nsilently fall back to `vec![cwd]`.\n- Clarifies the `debug sandbox` non-Windows comment: remaining\ncwd-dependent resolution still uses `sandbox_policy_cwd`, while\n`:workspace_roots` entries are already materialized from config roots.\n- Updates elevated runner IPC `SpawnRequest` to send `workspace_roots`\nand bumps the framed IPC protocol version to `3` for the payload shape\nchange.\n- Adds Windows-local resolver coverage for expanding exact and glob\n`:workspace_roots` entries across multiple roots, plus core helper\ncoverage proving explicit roots are preserved.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo check -p codex-windows-sandbox -p codex-core -p codex-tui -p\ncodex-cli -p codex-app-server`\n- `cargo test -p codex-windows-sandbox`\n- `cargo test -p codex-core windows_sandbox`\n- `cargo test -p codex-core unix_escalation`\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server windows_sandbox`\n- `cargo test -p codex-tui windows_sandbox`\n- `cargo test -p codex-cli debug_sandbox`\n- `just test -p codex-core unified_exec`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nbuild_exec_request_preserves_windows_workspace_roots`\n- `env -u CODEX_NETWORK_PROXY_ACTIVE -u\nCODEX_NETWORK_ALLOW_LOCAL_BINDING just test -p codex-app-server --lib\ncommand_exec`\n- `just test -p codex-windows-sandbox`\n- `just test -p codex-exec sandbox`\n- `just fix -p codex-core -p codex-app-server -p codex-windows-sandbox`\n\nA local macOS cross-check with `cargo check --target\nx86_64-pc-windows-msvc ...` did not reach crate Rust code because native\ndependencies require Windows SDK headers (`windows.h` / `assert.h`) in\nthis environment; Windows CI remains the real target validation.\n\nTwo local targeted filters compile but do not run assertions on macOS:\n`env -u CODEX_NETWORK_PROXY_ACTIVE -u CODEX_NETWORK_ALLOW_LOCAL_BINDING\njust test -p codex-app-server --lib command_exec_processor` matched zero\ntests, and `just test -p codex-linux-sandbox landlock` matched zero\ntests because the landlock suite is Linux-only.","tree":{"sha":"a6878a7aaa85483af2cd3347a5b2b2ff08903506","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a6878a7aaa85483af2cd3347a5b2b2ff08903506"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/986c60467b96ca13850217f6e5adadef6ba70ab3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGMEvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAukMQAG9ErbjOtEJCUg2QdfHq4UN1\nfC8X4buijWgzLufcSC3snYvzs0Vos7gBI5ebZB8F+LCZONT+SAj+ugT2YDETZu0P\n1XN3CA7yvQVLJhnh19gjo3BzIVn0AeNIPsCHCHq5hY5nX1EiZ7An0e/+Y/HtsmGw\nsGY/c/+MJcAoWBCE2yHaHb73BxBHIMjxndNfEWV31LG3I9KouLG3RYbBl8tMcNGv\nDrRw550cGWeG8OHbnxjTo/ol5QDwRxGpK+QdslfQeCCi1NiPVIxJE3Bz6lR3NqeJ\nUvMIVECD8j/CNOwLiiRiflg3wxOfcnEAcL9eZuu0MA+x27Gmr/PkerrkqREYA0wV\nSzuOTJ8hNfYtvZ+k7PiflPS3qZ8U8zVOhGnbxT3L6ptGpoHFcOzOEEtJ/e9NGgNT\nNlT5GhlBmmVoDpEsuKXLUVTMnY2hwcPxy4qg9dpfIBwlMJBpP6D/KjDJ+ayBF1JD\nJ85OIZsUokcPJ81v2dD0JvOKfTzs0aAhx+nW3Kp17i2S61Nvm9JVbqpNwXGyaTqz\njktVyGl4987tjl0uzc+9kxux8dVHgJ519DgAYDBD0Uljx26srW+M6maWM/ss0kZe\nP8lcx4y/63N+e/g7pyRvvAtzm0dPtynL3rJM0btI9K1JQB+vrZcvtxIPLafHSu0O\nbaprq33iwypxZB3+J5J/\n=rxUK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a6878a7aaa85483af2cd3347a5b2b2ff08903506\nparent e7dda8070e4eb2ba9de215545ff0db3b0ee4c519\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1780007215 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780007215 -0700\n\nwindows-sandbox: pass workspace roots to runner (#24108)\n\n## Why\n\n#23813 switches the Windows sandbox runner path to `PermissionProfile`,\nbut it still left one runtime anchor for resolving symbolic\n`:workspace_roots` entries. That is not enough once a turn has multiple\neffective workspace roots: exact entries and deny globs under\n`:workspace_roots` need to be materialized for every runtime root before\nthe command runner chooses token mode or builds ACL plans.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Replaces the Windows runner/setup `permission_profile_cwd` plumbing\nwith `workspace_roots: Vec<AbsolutePathBuf>`.\n- Resolves Windows-local `PermissionProfile` data with\n`materialize_project_roots_with_workspace_roots(...)` instead of the\nsingle-cwd helper.\n- Threads `Config::effective_workspace_roots()` through core execution,\nunified exec, TUI setup/read-grant flows, app-server setup, app-server\n`command/exec`, and `debug sandbox` on Windows.\n- Preserves those workspace roots through the zsh-fork escalation\nexecutor instead of rebuilding them from `sandbox_policy_cwd`.\n- Makes `ExecRequest::new(...)` and the remaining\n`build_exec_request(...)` helper path take\n`windows_sandbox_workspace_roots` explicitly so new call sites cannot\nsilently fall back to `vec![cwd]`.\n- Clarifies the `debug sandbox` non-Windows comment: remaining\ncwd-dependent resolution still uses `sandbox_policy_cwd`, while\n`:workspace_roots` entries are already materialized from config roots.\n- Updates elevated runner IPC `SpawnRequest` to send `workspace_roots`\nand bumps the framed IPC protocol version to `3` for the payload shape\nchange.\n- Adds Windows-local resolver coverage for expanding exact and glob\n`:workspace_roots` entries across multiple roots, plus core helper\ncoverage proving explicit roots are preserved.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo check -p codex-windows-sandbox -p codex-core -p codex-tui -p\ncodex-cli -p codex-app-server`\n- `cargo test -p codex-windows-sandbox`\n- `cargo test -p codex-core windows_sandbox`\n- `cargo test -p codex-core unix_escalation`\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server windows_sandbox`\n- `cargo test -p codex-tui windows_sandbox`\n- `cargo test -p codex-cli debug_sandbox`\n- `just test -p codex-core unified_exec`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nbuild_exec_request_preserves_windows_workspace_roots`\n- `env -u CODEX_NETWORK_PROXY_ACTIVE -u\nCODEX_NETWORK_ALLOW_LOCAL_BINDING just test -p codex-app-server --lib\ncommand_exec`\n- `just test -p codex-windows-sandbox`\n- `just test -p codex-exec sandbox`\n- `just fix -p codex-core -p codex-app-server -p codex-windows-sandbox`\n\nA local macOS cross-check with `cargo check --target\nx86_64-pc-windows-msvc ...` did not reach crate Rust code because native\ndependencies require Windows SDK headers (`windows.h` / `assert.h`) in\nthis environment; Windows CI remains the real target validation.\n\nTwo local targeted filters compile but do not run assertions on macOS:\n`env -u CODEX_NETWORK_PROXY_ACTIVE -u CODEX_NETWORK_ALLOW_LOCAL_BINDING\njust test -p codex-app-server --lib command_exec_processor` matched zero\ntests, and `just test -p codex-linux-sandbox landlock` matched zero\ntests because the landlock suite is Linux-only.","verified_at":"2026-05-28T22:26:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/986c60467b96ca13850217f6e5adadef6ba70ab3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/986c60467b96ca13850217f6e5adadef6ba70ab3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/986c60467b96ca13850217f6e5adadef6ba70ab3/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e7dda8070e4eb2ba9de215545ff0db3b0ee4c519","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e7dda8070e4eb2ba9de215545ff0db3b0ee4c519","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e7dda8070e4eb2ba9de215545ff0db3b0ee4c519"}]},{"sha":"e7dda8070e4eb2ba9de215545ff0db3b0ee4c519","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGU3ZGRhODA3MGU0ZWIyYmE5ZGUyMTU1NDVmZjBkYjNiMGVlNGM1MTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T21:56:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T21:56:53Z"},"message":"Surface filesystem permission profiles in prompt context (#23924)\n\n## Summary\nSome permission profiles can encode filesystem reads that should remain\nunavailable to the agent. Before this change, the model-visible context\nand automatic approval review prompt summarized the effective\npermissions as a legacy sandbox mode, which can omit permission-profile\nfilesystem entries from escalation decisions.\n\nFor example, a profile can grant workspace access while denying a\nprivate subtree across every workspace root:\n\n```toml\ndefault_permissions = \"restricted-workspace\"\n\n[permissions.restricted-workspace.workspace_roots]\n\"/Users/alice/project\" = true\n\"/Users/alice/other-project\" = true\n\n[permissions.restricted-workspace.filesystem]\n\":minimal\" = \"read\"\n\n[permissions.restricted-workspace.filesystem.\":workspace_roots\"]\n\".\" = \"write\"\n\"private\" = \"deny\"\n\"private/**\" = \"deny\"\n```\n\nThe context window now describes the workspace roots and effective\nfilesystem side of the `PermissionProfile` directly, with deny entries\nmarked as non-escalatable:\n\n```xml\n<environment_context>\n  <cwd>/Users/alice/project</cwd>\n  <shell>zsh</shell>\n  <filesystem><workspace_roots><root>/Users/alice/project</root><root>/Users/alice/other-project</root></workspace_roots><permission_profile type=\"managed\"><file_system type=\"restricted\"><entry access=\"read\"><special>:minimal</special></entry><entry access=\"write\"><path>/Users/alice/project</path></entry><entry access=\"write\"><path>/Users/alice/other-project</path></entry><entry access=\"deny\" escalatable=\"false\"><path>/Users/alice/project/private</path></entry><entry access=\"deny\" escalatable=\"false\"><path>/Users/alice/other-project/private</path></entry><entry access=\"deny\" escalatable=\"false\"><glob>/Users/alice/project/private/**</glob></entry><entry access=\"deny\" escalatable=\"false\"><glob>/Users/alice/other-project/private/**</glob></entry></file_system></permission_profile></filesystem>\n</environment_context>\n```\n\nManaged requirements can impose the same kind of deny-read restriction:\n\n```toml\n[permissions.filesystem]\ndeny_read = [\n  \"/Users/alice/project/private\",\n  \"/Users/alice/project/private/**\",\n]\n```\n\nThe automatic approval review prompt also receives the parent turn's\ndenied-read context, so review decisions can account for the active\npermission profile.\n\n## What Changed\n- Render the effective filesystem profile in `<environment_context>`,\nincluding profile type, filesystem entries, workspace roots, and\nnon-escalatable deny entries.\n- Persist effective `workspace_roots` in `TurnContextItem` so\nresumed/replayed context does not have to bind `:workspace_roots`\nthrough legacy `cwd` fallback.\n- Add explicit permission instructions that denied reads are policy\nrestrictions, not escalation targets.\n- Pass the parent turn's denied-read context into automatic approval\nreviews.\n- Add targeted coverage for prompt rendering, workspace-root\nmaterialization, replay context, and review prompt context.\n- Keep the prompt-context test expectations platform-aware so the same\nfilesystem rendering assertions pass on Unix and Windows paths.\n\n## Testing\n- `just test -p codex-core\ncontext::environment_context::tests::serialize_environment_context_with_full_filesystem_profile`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ncontext::environment_context::tests::turn_context_item_filesystem_uses_workspace_roots_instead_of_cwd`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ncontext::permissions_instructions::permissions_instructions_tests::builds_permissions_from_profile_with_denied_reads`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n\nI also attempted `just test -p codex-core`; the changed prompt-context\ntests passed, but the full local run did not complete cleanly in this\nsandboxed macOS environment due unrelated user-shell `CODEX_SANDBOX*`\nexpectations and integration-test timeouts.","tree":{"sha":"cafe5e95d01faf6f047e60b520693c5fd7a87387","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/cafe5e95d01faf6f047e60b520693c5fd7a87387"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e7dda8070e4eb2ba9de215545ff0db3b0ee4c519","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGLolCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgHUQAGFXz9jWDRTGmnfAgrRilkqh\nH1USVy4GW75a4NJZE22Ah/bCKNyCavczq8Wl94bLQgR2NtDFXFd4O/el6j2wg4j4\naPVCfVu42Sbz5jSbpVk60fHhe8Mn/QG7ipCzsQxfa6NUBVlLtL7KhnQxMGXDJaDr\nPEN7taWw3g8UU+FaEe5LXCfcBGImkAfOAcnCGCXMdcY2RLeoB/qz8Ghex5ORcQiX\n15IkCBeezRirz9QXHQC5fQJ86Y2yDR4zb4WXhfHGODYNWHdX+qw5Ilet46ATTcD0\n/LOjNl77qTopLP0jHkTs1gDSev8KUlwxFePBUIpkc6T8rj8h1UUSfblIBULM8nTA\n/t7MNJ4u9bc7yqbJ/jXMGer8V9xjUNm7wALrUQftEMwhbOw/KzMP8sh02vKxK2Oo\nb8M6JG2NXZVWHdHKTlq60nVQQ/zfbgeoZaUuKdaTMREqzx3mbb18WGV5L3WMfFtd\nMSTJw/GM259FqMmtcNbmVgp8w/QSfgriAkBe9bU5B0X3nh07QIdPDGXzo6CsdhL+\nrAQCVaLmR1gMT+9wiW2a/nQJIHOlyxDAPcOdoL2Tow9HmpP7Y2wb7iJk2LCgvL7l\nkOU/JcQaG5tnda22JcfK2UukBgEwmsjVllbOpG0Zdbz5u8CaLFEHeV5wBKLQ6duV\nmy28h8/OqZmg5SeEHhSo\n=mm5j\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree cafe5e95d01faf6f047e60b520693c5fd7a87387\nparent e92c952b2e3d04a77d1efae02299a11454b7d409\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1780005413 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780005413 -0700\n\nSurface filesystem permission profiles in prompt context (#23924)\n\n## Summary\nSome permission profiles can encode filesystem reads that should remain\nunavailable to the agent. Before this change, the model-visible context\nand automatic approval review prompt summarized the effective\npermissions as a legacy sandbox mode, which can omit permission-profile\nfilesystem entries from escalation decisions.\n\nFor example, a profile can grant workspace access while denying a\nprivate subtree across every workspace root:\n\n```toml\ndefault_permissions = \"restricted-workspace\"\n\n[permissions.restricted-workspace.workspace_roots]\n\"/Users/alice/project\" = true\n\"/Users/alice/other-project\" = true\n\n[permissions.restricted-workspace.filesystem]\n\":minimal\" = \"read\"\n\n[permissions.restricted-workspace.filesystem.\":workspace_roots\"]\n\".\" = \"write\"\n\"private\" = \"deny\"\n\"private/**\" = \"deny\"\n```\n\nThe context window now describes the workspace roots and effective\nfilesystem side of the `PermissionProfile` directly, with deny entries\nmarked as non-escalatable:\n\n```xml\n<environment_context>\n  <cwd>/Users/alice/project</cwd>\n  <shell>zsh</shell>\n  <filesystem><workspace_roots><root>/Users/alice/project</root><root>/Users/alice/other-project</root></workspace_roots><permission_profile type=\"managed\"><file_system type=\"restricted\"><entry access=\"read\"><special>:minimal</special></entry><entry access=\"write\"><path>/Users/alice/project</path></entry><entry access=\"write\"><path>/Users/alice/other-project</path></entry><entry access=\"deny\" escalatable=\"false\"><path>/Users/alice/project/private</path></entry><entry access=\"deny\" escalatable=\"false\"><path>/Users/alice/other-project/private</path></entry><entry access=\"deny\" escalatable=\"false\"><glob>/Users/alice/project/private/**</glob></entry><entry access=\"deny\" escalatable=\"false\"><glob>/Users/alice/other-project/private/**</glob></entry></file_system></permission_profile></filesystem>\n</environment_context>\n```\n\nManaged requirements can impose the same kind of deny-read restriction:\n\n```toml\n[permissions.filesystem]\ndeny_read = [\n  \"/Users/alice/project/private\",\n  \"/Users/alice/project/private/**\",\n]\n```\n\nThe automatic approval review prompt also receives the parent turn's\ndenied-read context, so review decisions can account for the active\npermission profile.\n\n## What Changed\n- Render the effective filesystem profile in `<environment_context>`,\nincluding profile type, filesystem entries, workspace roots, and\nnon-escalatable deny entries.\n- Persist effective `workspace_roots` in `TurnContextItem` so\nresumed/replayed context does not have to bind `:workspace_roots`\nthrough legacy `cwd` fallback.\n- Add explicit permission instructions that denied reads are policy\nrestrictions, not escalation targets.\n- Pass the parent turn's denied-read context into automatic approval\nreviews.\n- Add targeted coverage for prompt rendering, workspace-root\nmaterialization, replay context, and review prompt context.\n- Keep the prompt-context test expectations platform-aware so the same\nfilesystem rendering assertions pass on Unix and Windows paths.\n\n## Testing\n- `just test -p codex-core\ncontext::environment_context::tests::serialize_environment_context_with_full_filesystem_profile`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ncontext::environment_context::tests::turn_context_item_filesystem_uses_workspace_roots_instead_of_cwd`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ncontext::permissions_instructions::permissions_instructions_tests::builds_permissions_from_profile_with_denied_reads`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n\nI also attempted `just test -p codex-core`; the changed prompt-context\ntests passed, but the full local run did not complete cleanly in this\nsandboxed macOS environment due unrelated user-shell `CODEX_SANDBOX*`\nexpectations and integration-test timeouts.","verified_at":"2026-05-28T21:56:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e7dda8070e4eb2ba9de215545ff0db3b0ee4c519","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e7dda8070e4eb2ba9de215545ff0db3b0ee4c519","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e7dda8070e4eb2ba9de215545ff0db3b0ee4c519/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e92c952b2e3d04a77d1efae02299a11454b7d409","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e92c952b2e3d04a77d1efae02299a11454b7d409","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e92c952b2e3d04a77d1efae02299a11454b7d409"}]},{"sha":"e92c952b2e3d04a77d1efae02299a11454b7d409","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGU5MmM5NTJiMmUzZDA0YTc3ZDFlZmFlMDIyOTlhMTE0NTRiN2Q0MDk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Alexi Christakis","email":"167903946+alexi-openai@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-05-28T21:54:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T21:54:39Z"},"message":"[codex] Add user input client ids (#24653)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds an optional `clientId` field to app-server v2 `UserInput` and\ncarries it through the core `UserInput` model so clients can correlate\nechoed user input items without relying on payload equality.\n\n## Details\n\n- Adds `client_id: Option<String>` to core `UserInput` variants.\n- Exposes the v2 app-server field as `clientId` on the wire and in\ngenerated TypeScript.\n- Preserves the id when converting between app-server v2 and core\nprotocol types.\n- Regenerates app-server schema fixtures.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just write-app-server-schema`\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `cargo test -p codex-protocol`\n- `just fix -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just fix -p codex-protocol`\n- `git diff --check`","tree":{"sha":"246b226a5ae8be91fce16576e3508cea5f9ad8c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/246b226a5ae8be91fce16576e3508cea5f9ad8c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e92c952b2e3d04a77d1efae02299a11454b7d409","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGLmfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACxEQAJAaYgn/hZ9GVmg/UNoqhqKk\ncchgPiORH1UICIuONwKENmigSYLPVZ5oOWAipIqbwZp/Ewu0lpTpBn+syO9vgaDx\nLLWNUPRi7c7eRYgKr5ZowHJJNPPG4OH98BGkhcd4hmbIlp2IKaqYTRAMarw/bA2V\n1EnTy77pGHbbSx4W6oTw8dfMgNiWo7pNuZKByt9LqE9a6luuigLC5H/Sq2Vy7mN2\n1IqC28/CoduBnq9cOC6l+5ncRg3GD0mGmV9CQD14nTiMPikle4muixOsmLph62VH\nnZYBCmyu7GCIVu0R/aWwMRszH+5mfss8QH3E8IBAi+HQ0VExz1jlGVykRl/RKda9\npQBDFMkFZsVp5A0fhEyG0EOrtdYFDagvlDRbwwHk04aOnGR6oqZyr6ttk0BW9ODO\n3IHxou8TK34TqA6g7Wb7gAcduY7LWBRoI6Eck4616NDjwpRstGyYvGC3SruPcu5p\ndfrGJ8IKePR/0onoXaG4Q/EbHKpFwL4/4xxDk3Eams/4WD8Gf79n9dnBGoMqnxDo\nBiOLKLGOQBPasqkXlupoms/DYNDGcqf99Cw8SM34qD7gZJOzebiFhbkBTzLW1phY\nzzzlxD1OFWiLciNMEQ5Hxcw4bwLTlIlk1EXbKFHchnJRFVeGoxICK5Q3Tx+OBH3R\nkXZU5cA7fD/4HYCme5uQ\n=0fH/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 246b226a5ae8be91fce16576e3508cea5f9ad8c5\nparent a027135bc6d3b967d370fb58fc00d87286074046\nauthor Alexi Christakis <167903946+alexi-openai@users.noreply.github.com> 1780005279 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780005279 -0700\n\n[codex] Add user input client ids (#24653)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds an optional `clientId` field to app-server v2 `UserInput` and\ncarries it through the core `UserInput` model so clients can correlate\nechoed user input items without relying on payload equality.\n\n## Details\n\n- Adds `client_id: Option<String>` to core `UserInput` variants.\n- Exposes the v2 app-server field as `clientId` on the wire and in\ngenerated TypeScript.\n- Preserves the id when converting between app-server v2 and core\nprotocol types.\n- Regenerates app-server schema fixtures.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just write-app-server-schema`\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `cargo test -p codex-protocol`\n- `just fix -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just fix -p codex-protocol`\n- `git diff --check`","verified_at":"2026-05-28T21:54:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e92c952b2e3d04a77d1efae02299a11454b7d409","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e92c952b2e3d04a77d1efae02299a11454b7d409","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e92c952b2e3d04a77d1efae02299a11454b7d409/comments","author":{"login":"alexi-openai","id":167903946,"node_id":"U_kgDOCgICyg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/167903946?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexi-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/alexi-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexi-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexi-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexi-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexi-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexi-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexi-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexi-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexi-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexi-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a027135bc6d3b967d370fb58fc00d87286074046","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a027135bc6d3b967d370fb58fc00d87286074046","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a027135bc6d3b967d370fb58fc00d87286074046"}]},{"sha":"a027135bc6d3b967d370fb58fc00d87286074046","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGEwMjcxMzViYzZkM2I5NjdkMzcwZmI1OGZjMDBkODcyODYwNzQwNDY","commit":{"author":{"name":"viyatb-oai","email":"viyatb@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T21:44:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T21:44:14Z"},"message":"fix(exec-server): reject websocket requests with Origin headers (#24947)\n\n## Why\n\n`codex exec-server` has a local WebSocket listener, but it did not apply\nthe same browser-origin request handling as the `app-server` WebSocket\ntransport. Requests that carry an `Origin` header should not be upgraded\nby this local transport, keeping both local WebSocket servers consistent\nand avoiding unexpected browser-initiated connections.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added an Axum middleware guard in\n`codex-rs/exec-server/src/server/transport.rs` that returns `403\nForbidden` for requests carrying an `Origin` header.\n- Added an integration test in `codex-rs/exec-server/tests/websocket.rs`\nthat covers rejection of an `Origin`-bearing WebSocket handshake.\n- Kept ordinary WebSocket clients unchanged: existing no-`Origin`\ninitialization and process behavior remains covered by the crate tests.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server` test phase (`186 passed`; run outside\nthe parent macOS sandbox so nested sandbox tests can execute)\n- `just clippy -p codex-exec-server`","tree":{"sha":"a02ad143f0fe60e4d3d219c1c681216a2ab72088","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a02ad143f0fe60e4d3d219c1c681216a2ab72088"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a027135bc6d3b967d370fb58fc00d87286074046","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGLcuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAswUQAJ5j4h5MJfxU8ofl9nt7MxTV\n+FnYFThNMA66JwstXEi0P8xzmVmZgh3VtRQb5M9IZqbFZ63N8W76HMigdqDBNYt5\ndmwF0pYcww7q8jV070/9jcsYfKnc07HEOZcHyvQQ+1hO3wzKb+HpW7aMP8RopeOw\nfi9W2myC5fR4WCkk+DqbMRTCTyEQqiD3GYXSARa/1+CFWW3Vz5t1vId9OQsbAYtZ\ncTWmQWhbYSyoTQUjCJrZpUi6J/IwHiOKtSr1fFEnP2nlwTJRYcDQHR+wVvPFRq9s\nHgFMQyGArSuFUw/3JWTZnXQjaQQl47zwL+6IldbqPgQk6IRaYgiv5KtX6whOg75E\nv70k86aU4up68pd2nd3OQWlg8WADZXGh2mokkIQv/KMdDHevckQ/cWqpvvIv+B3y\nqnaTnDrXS724cfsGKFlvuhfhASwoqGQJ9HXKo32iqgXyYcq6HXmfkDgGBpC3odcG\nghemD7gOJ3IhKOmvBB02kK/3uKW1KgPexqZ6Eh2AYkgMF+0WZSGDq1h+wkdwulDF\nw9xxNyms6B+Ly6MQqjS4eJ44JqSnd8kPEzhyjeh/zgwK5IVCpYu4cvak3siRj3xD\n7XsSCkC40NAC8hhSdgbISpHuVQc/iiYeLwmsg+9YPPS4wKmB3OVjydnGkJsuPgy5\nCP1/iD4dprNZeCFuemrx\n=FEk2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a02ad143f0fe60e4d3d219c1c681216a2ab72088\nparent 3cf737e4e377b0eaa3bda88a0aac8589cf3ae45a\nauthor viyatb-oai <viyatb@openai.com> 1780004654 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780004654 -0700\n\nfix(exec-server): reject websocket requests with Origin headers (#24947)\n\n## Why\n\n`codex exec-server` has a local WebSocket listener, but it did not apply\nthe same browser-origin request handling as the `app-server` WebSocket\ntransport. Requests that carry an `Origin` header should not be upgraded\nby this local transport, keeping both local WebSocket servers consistent\nand avoiding unexpected browser-initiated connections.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added an Axum middleware guard in\n`codex-rs/exec-server/src/server/transport.rs` that returns `403\nForbidden` for requests carrying an `Origin` header.\n- Added an integration test in `codex-rs/exec-server/tests/websocket.rs`\nthat covers rejection of an `Origin`-bearing WebSocket handshake.\n- Kept ordinary WebSocket clients unchanged: existing no-`Origin`\ninitialization and process behavior remains covered by the crate tests.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server` test phase (`186 passed`; run outside\nthe parent macOS sandbox so nested sandbox tests can execute)\n- `just clippy -p codex-exec-server`","verified_at":"2026-05-28T21:44:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a027135bc6d3b967d370fb58fc00d87286074046","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a027135bc6d3b967d370fb58fc00d87286074046","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a027135bc6d3b967d370fb58fc00d87286074046/comments","author":{"login":"viyatb-oai","id":234056686,"node_id":"U_kgDODfNr7g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234056686?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/viyatb-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3cf737e4e377b0eaa3bda88a0aac8589cf3ae45a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3cf737e4e377b0eaa3bda88a0aac8589cf3ae45a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3cf737e4e377b0eaa3bda88a0aac8589cf3ae45a"}]},{"sha":"3cf737e4e377b0eaa3bda88a0aac8589cf3ae45a","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDNjZjczN2U0ZTM3N2IwZWFhM2JkYTg4YTBhYWM4NTg5Y2YzYWU0NWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"viyatb-oai","email":"viyatb@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T21:28:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T21:28:06Z"},"message":"fix: cancel Windows sandbox on network denial (#19880)\n\n## Why\n\nWhen Guardian or the sandbox network proxy detects and denies a network\nattempt, core cancels the associated execution through `ExecExpiration`.\nThe Windows sandbox capture path was only forwarding the timeout\ncomponent of that expiration state. As a result, a sandboxed Windows\ncommand whose network attempt had already been denied could keep running\nuntil its timeout elapsed rather than terminating promptly in response\nto the denial.\n\nThis change closes that cancellation-propagation gap for Windows sandbox\nexecution.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added `WindowsSandboxCancellationToken` as the cancellation hook\nexposed to Windows capture backends.\n- Extracted the cancellation token from `ExecExpiration` in core and\npassed it to both the direct and elevated Windows sandbox capture paths\nalongside the existing timeout.\n- Updated direct capture to poll for either process exit, timeout, or\ncancellation and to terminate cancelled processes without reporting them\nas timed out.\n- Updated elevated capture to watch for cancellation and send the\nexisting `Terminate` IPC frame to the elevated runner. The watcher parks\nfor 50 ms between checks to bound response latency without a tight busy\nwait.\n- Added Windows regression coverage for a long-running PowerShell\ncommand: cancellation ends capture before its timeout and does not set\n`timed_out`.\n- Added a visible skip diagnostic when that PowerShell-dependent\nregression test cannot execute, and consolidated the duplicated\nexpiration-policy branch identified in review.\n\n## Security\n\nThis improves enforcement after a denied network attempt has been\nattributed to a Windows sandboxed execution: the command no longer\nremains alive simply because Windows capture lost the cancellation\nsignal.\n\nThis PR does not claim to make Windows offline mode an airtight\nno-network or no-exfiltration boundary. It does not introduce\nAppContainer or change how network denial is detected; it makes an\nalready-detected denial promptly stop the affected sandboxed command.\n\n## Validation\n\n### Commands run\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `cargo test -p codex-windows-sandbox`\n- `cargo test -p codex-core network_denial`\n- `cargo clippy -p codex-core -p codex-windows-sandbox --tests --no-deps\n-- -D warnings`\n- `just argument-comment-lint -p codex-windows-sandbox -p codex-core`\n\nThe new capture regression is `cfg(target_os = \"windows\")`, so Windows\nCI is the execution coverage for that test path. The local macOS test\nruns validate the host-runnable crate and core network-denial behavior.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Codex <noreply@openai.com>","tree":{"sha":"210ae37772fb6aee3cceb48f00685044d6498ae8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/210ae37772fb6aee3cceb48f00685044d6498ae8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/3cf737e4e377b0eaa3bda88a0aac8589cf3ae45a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGLNmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7PYQAF85eanb2E1k4tQoFi8d9GGj\n7MnA2mx1Fszcf+dLSiuRpKYpk7rq5e9yQu5TfEMC5jr/i49A4ZEYzZ4P7pt7bUu4\nUfYDWidzudnrbzaQi1FJHJXUWVeG5Hfh1CD57LnuBq9Jjg/7A2eJ1XpSssfs5on9\nohx2dk3fFwpHacJaCjS6AE813wV6b0thJdGIOFLjvAznDNI2S9rIorWII9m1hkZX\nRxAzxzsbwFalGzbTIlnxZiCBg5WZ5GdypGzjLw+Bmum3UuOZ+s4fvYQDS8VPl4oF\nRcE6WAwDmUflA3O0gk9f6XN/3sgLELpd0lWn3rF0ye25eGgLmeyYrfuLc+6/fdY1\nFJbfH8QEx8cTfS6ACH6EJwaOddch3qnugFlHpYAMFO+AJNieGsOsloQbUDZ/Dh8S\npCAMyTSkSXrcuIPfvJNgGNKw8pl65wUQLdnpsnRHm5dpuuvCoOUMfGK7KlZ9ZzQn\nMAhTQTd3tB5N6LprR/YW7E0tzScFbedJ0Xzx/NMRZLv04Pu0g2ry6iH2tJRpsE0b\nG0Lugqq4INwXKBpQqA02p9JXRsLpwGj+ewDHfodKiei1D5vYIa25JaaDmeb2ZLHN\ngG8qBwrB/ywlAhD/gMNGtOzPogep8p59Rb0EML0t1mB6Mjfsr7oA2HAXUMxK1ak0\n8QNsXRbAA3rTisV4XYCW\n=Rbj1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 210ae37772fb6aee3cceb48f00685044d6498ae8\nparent bc10e5b3900b26c638aa44c2a9bc15950be733ae\nauthor viyatb-oai <viyatb@openai.com> 1780003686 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780003686 +0000\n\nfix: cancel Windows sandbox on network denial (#19880)\n\n## Why\n\nWhen Guardian or the sandbox network proxy detects and denies a network\nattempt, core cancels the associated execution through `ExecExpiration`.\nThe Windows sandbox capture path was only forwarding the timeout\ncomponent of that expiration state. As a result, a sandboxed Windows\ncommand whose network attempt had already been denied could keep running\nuntil its timeout elapsed rather than terminating promptly in response\nto the denial.\n\nThis change closes that cancellation-propagation gap for Windows sandbox\nexecution.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added `WindowsSandboxCancellationToken` as the cancellation hook\nexposed to Windows capture backends.\n- Extracted the cancellation token from `ExecExpiration` in core and\npassed it to both the direct and elevated Windows sandbox capture paths\nalongside the existing timeout.\n- Updated direct capture to poll for either process exit, timeout, or\ncancellation and to terminate cancelled processes without reporting them\nas timed out.\n- Updated elevated capture to watch for cancellation and send the\nexisting `Terminate` IPC frame to the elevated runner. The watcher parks\nfor 50 ms between checks to bound response latency without a tight busy\nwait.\n- Added Windows regression coverage for a long-running PowerShell\ncommand: cancellation ends capture before its timeout and does not set\n`timed_out`.\n- Added a visible skip diagnostic when that PowerShell-dependent\nregression test cannot execute, and consolidated the duplicated\nexpiration-policy branch identified in review.\n\n## Security\n\nThis improves enforcement after a denied network attempt has been\nattributed to a Windows sandboxed execution: the command no longer\nremains alive simply because Windows capture lost the cancellation\nsignal.\n\nThis PR does not claim to make Windows offline mode an airtight\nno-network or no-exfiltration boundary. It does not introduce\nAppContainer or change how network denial is detected; it makes an\nalready-detected denial promptly stop the affected sandboxed command.\n\n## Validation\n\n### Commands run\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `cargo test -p codex-windows-sandbox`\n- `cargo test -p codex-core network_denial`\n- `cargo clippy -p codex-core -p codex-windows-sandbox --tests --no-deps\n-- -D warnings`\n- `just argument-comment-lint -p codex-windows-sandbox -p codex-core`\n\nThe new capture regression is `cfg(target_os = \"windows\")`, so Windows\nCI is the execution coverage for that test path. The local macOS test\nruns validate the host-runnable crate and core network-denial behavior.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Codex <noreply@openai.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-28T21:28:07Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3cf737e4e377b0eaa3bda88a0aac8589cf3ae45a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3cf737e4e377b0eaa3bda88a0aac8589cf3ae45a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3cf737e4e377b0eaa3bda88a0aac8589cf3ae45a/comments","author":{"login":"viyatb-oai","id":234056686,"node_id":"U_kgDODfNr7g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234056686?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/viyatb-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bc10e5b3900b26c638aa44c2a9bc15950be733ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bc10e5b3900b26c638aa44c2a9bc15950be733ae","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bc10e5b3900b26c638aa44c2a9bc15950be733ae"}]},{"sha":"bc10e5b3900b26c638aa44c2a9bc15950be733ae","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGJjMTBlNWIzOTAwYjI2YzYzOGFhNDRjMmE5YmMxNTk1MGJlNzMzYWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T21:10:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T21:10:40Z"},"message":"runtime: prepend zsh fork bin dir to PATH (#23768)\n\n## Why\n\n#23756 makes packaged Codex builds include and default to the bundled\nzsh fork. The important reason to put that fork's directory at the front\nof `PATH` is to keep executable-level escalation working after a command\nleaves the original shell and later re-enters zsh through `env`.\n\nThe expected chain is:\n\n1. The zsh fork runs the top-level shell command.\n2. That command launches another program, such as `python3`, while\ninheriting the `EXEC_WRAPPER` environment and the escalation socket fd.\n3. That program spawns a shell script whose shebang is `#!/usr/bin/env\nzsh` rather than `#!/bin/zsh`, and it does not close the escalation fd.\n4. `/usr/bin/env` resolves `zsh` through `PATH`, so it must find the\npackaged zsh fork before the system zsh.\n5. Commands inside that nested script are intercepted by the zsh fork\nand can still request escalation from Codex.\n\nIf `PATH` resolves `zsh` to the system shell instead, the nested script\nloses zsh-fork exec interception. Commands that should request\nescalation can then run only in the original sandbox, or fail there,\nwithout Codex ever receiving the approval request.\n\nShell snapshots make this slightly more subtle: a snapshot can restore\nan older `PATH` after the child shell starts. This PR treats the zsh\nfork `PATH` prepend as an explicit environment override so snapshot\nwrapping preserves it.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added shared zsh-fork runtime helpers that prepend the configured zsh\nexecutable parent directory to `PATH` without duplicate entries.\n- Applied the zsh fork `PATH` prepend to both zsh-fork `shell_command`\nlaunches and unified-exec zsh-fork launches before sandbox command\nconstruction.\n- Kept the shell-command zsh-fork backend API narrow: it derives the\nconfigured zsh path from session services and rebuilds its sandbox\nenvironment from `req.env`, rather than accepting a second, competing\nenvironment map or a separately threaded bin dir.\n- Kept Unix-only zsh-fork `PATH` mutation out of Windows clippy-visible\nmutability.\n- Added coverage for duplicate `PATH` entries, for preserving the zsh\nfork prepend through shell snapshot wrapping, and for the nested\n`python3` -> `#!/usr/bin/env zsh` escalation flow.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n\nI left final test validation to CI after the latest review-comment\ncleanup. Before that cleanup, `just test -p codex-core zsh_fork` passed\nlocally for the zsh-fork-focused tests.","tree":{"sha":"8418afb911ab89c1ace9a53bfbf3fc87fbaa58fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/8418afb911ab89c1ace9a53bfbf3fc87fbaa58fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/bc10e5b3900b26c638aa44c2a9bc15950be733ae","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGK9QCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABw8QAK8TDq0exK4xhmmirNRNdo0v\nUdzv1BX7zyEuzaCALnfaMfkNe1+cPxBxnJixv/sQzag9ljdw0Ierzl8LwyAY/pZF\nnQY35TX6ffPUI+KIaoC9JRF8jvfrBmXMVSQJbzLABhYJ8gVa+lrNbMyN2MHMFcjl\nHaybxGEBYDJ1FMVHXEXR4IOVHsuvQZtTZRR6tF3ZE3RBHwGl985Bzs5IrIuCvIox\nSt0uPi3Y1s//sGhCKvYQzSYLY3eC89lGMmcoDP2UY2fwceABG5CdG9nQNKbDPQl+\nxQTJRxJQM5CQXda1JWFsAow/3p8gptdqAQiWO0wptw098C3/z9bLJ2Yk7NuEJsi+\nKEwEiJTbJV7yQV0i61dz2r9W2mLdbPRof27JZPmdwcxJEpXUJnUS8Z3Nq9XTRIMx\nUbJhxbQsURNRC2plRx+GoA1c5GjBQ2jT5x7gTgRqDWmewGiwLEtkR/B1HSHuyK1T\n5Nh0tCbV1XwKdcFgkJ3euhp4tD8qv9ggb2T2xKhM7ZN1PYfzR53h/kCAXb6N8080\nQybNC/36O/OTE2OtAe29reqUxsARArRXeg4PYDE2pQXyzwSRfQzfo+G7+FMD8L/f\nkOZAhfuui4Y1Sr4VT3ruU65BvLeAqDshazECTfKOg3Dsd9Hm7v9hub3dE2CrFROU\nQ1olqwuw5yM/p84JORP4\n=Duyi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8418afb911ab89c1ace9a53bfbf3fc87fbaa58fc\nparent 0a8c835845a04ca963ab37efd467e546b50c8df3\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1780002640 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780002640 -0700\n\nruntime: prepend zsh fork bin dir to PATH (#23768)\n\n## Why\n\n#23756 makes packaged Codex builds include and default to the bundled\nzsh fork. The important reason to put that fork's directory at the front\nof `PATH` is to keep executable-level escalation working after a command\nleaves the original shell and later re-enters zsh through `env`.\n\nThe expected chain is:\n\n1. The zsh fork runs the top-level shell command.\n2. That command launches another program, such as `python3`, while\ninheriting the `EXEC_WRAPPER` environment and the escalation socket fd.\n3. That program spawns a shell script whose shebang is `#!/usr/bin/env\nzsh` rather than `#!/bin/zsh`, and it does not close the escalation fd.\n4. `/usr/bin/env` resolves `zsh` through `PATH`, so it must find the\npackaged zsh fork before the system zsh.\n5. Commands inside that nested script are intercepted by the zsh fork\nand can still request escalation from Codex.\n\nIf `PATH` resolves `zsh` to the system shell instead, the nested script\nloses zsh-fork exec interception. Commands that should request\nescalation can then run only in the original sandbox, or fail there,\nwithout Codex ever receiving the approval request.\n\nShell snapshots make this slightly more subtle: a snapshot can restore\nan older `PATH` after the child shell starts. This PR treats the zsh\nfork `PATH` prepend as an explicit environment override so snapshot\nwrapping preserves it.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added shared zsh-fork runtime helpers that prepend the configured zsh\nexecutable parent directory to `PATH` without duplicate entries.\n- Applied the zsh fork `PATH` prepend to both zsh-fork `shell_command`\nlaunches and unified-exec zsh-fork launches before sandbox command\nconstruction.\n- Kept the shell-command zsh-fork backend API narrow: it derives the\nconfigured zsh path from session services and rebuilds its sandbox\nenvironment from `req.env`, rather than accepting a second, competing\nenvironment map or a separately threaded bin dir.\n- Kept Unix-only zsh-fork `PATH` mutation out of Windows clippy-visible\nmutability.\n- Added coverage for duplicate `PATH` entries, for preserving the zsh\nfork prepend through shell snapshot wrapping, and for the nested\n`python3` -> `#!/usr/bin/env zsh` escalation flow.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n\nI left final test validation to CI after the latest review-comment\ncleanup. Before that cleanup, `just test -p codex-core zsh_fork` passed\nlocally for the zsh-fork-focused tests.","verified_at":"2026-05-28T21:10:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bc10e5b3900b26c638aa44c2a9bc15950be733ae","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bc10e5b3900b26c638aa44c2a9bc15950be733ae","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bc10e5b3900b26c638aa44c2a9bc15950be733ae/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0a8c835845a04ca963ab37efd467e546b50c8df3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0a8c835845a04ca963ab37efd467e546b50c8df3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0a8c835845a04ca963ab37efd467e546b50c8df3"}]},{"sha":"0a8c835845a04ca963ab37efd467e546b50c8df3","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDBhOGM4MzU4NDVhMDRjYTk2M2FiMzdlZmQ0NjdlNTQ2YjUwYzhkZjM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Celia Chen","email":"celia@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T21:10:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T21:10:26Z"},"message":"[codex] Remove Bedrock OSS models from catalog (#24960)\n\nRemove the GPT OSS 120B and 20B entries from the Amazon Bedrock static\nmodel catalog, as they are no longer supported.","tree":{"sha":"cada5eeb4fd7ef76cb3f1fc38a4d8b0121b1167d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/cada5eeb4fd7ef76cb3f1fc38a4d8b0121b1167d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/0a8c835845a04ca963ab37efd467e546b50c8df3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGK9CCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3VoQAIyB0WPWgtvUWUHWNyg0vpwY\nDTvS6jp1rCKVbQ0WLV/1E7QH7tqC/XMZ4Z9sPA2Pb5ZyI846htAugCJ7I1DNoLNP\nnklbMalFCzy+45Ak0mCqKqBhAugdRYloqr45BX/a20n6tu8jWPKsxWwoZ5lV2efo\n1BqvncMZNVvi2No+BVV0R+0D3BcJhzxMuQQ+67VZpUz8lVxo9Pin/FHiKL5876Z3\nQ8bQM0jIf9CPk5EH48VgVq0KbrVLuGSNoyu3xX7AH2T1Kq/KMjnCUDbLq6uZNdNE\na1vDvPjnqlGncDB+cqaAAXS0rhtissviW3wFjZZOdG1GPySZKxftg+g0t29ThDkQ\nGjwQtSZbugUztwE5hMtVQrVG2DK7MQlj42QmyUq1RG/FmhdjqopXkrc6ogHVFlHN\n8cisk9vxu6U/cRGRK/dYnScAdvq17LDVGS8gTkv3uEF/pHcowgduSXkwKypVJr2A\n8o0p/nh+9oKgO92VKAIoJKrxboYwWB7jhIOsA8Rr25jLLhiukK0BG1j18CFLrqOU\n2ZXLKyxiQ43CUkP5VV2Win7FiLyyuXpOzvSYboliU9F6373XNjLMdDIrTisExzzP\npL4Zs4OILozQAZOdf3nsURF0WqH7KsQviLjQupt09sbWdX/cPg0/vL2GPpf9EkbE\n3WLsqlp0ZbZWo154b/F6\n=05aJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree cada5eeb4fd7ef76cb3f1fc38a4d8b0121b1167d\nparent d9f53128b7ab0a0d9b0b079a6ce0268b87263039\nauthor Celia Chen <celia@openai.com> 1780002626 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780002626 -0700\n\n[codex] Remove Bedrock OSS models from catalog (#24960)\n\nRemove the GPT OSS 120B and 20B entries from the Amazon Bedrock static\nmodel catalog, as they are no longer supported.","verified_at":"2026-05-28T21:10:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0a8c835845a04ca963ab37efd467e546b50c8df3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0a8c835845a04ca963ab37efd467e546b50c8df3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0a8c835845a04ca963ab37efd467e546b50c8df3/comments","author":{"login":"celia-oai","id":209693228,"node_id":"U_kgDODH-qLA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/209693228?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/celia-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d9f53128b7ab0a0d9b0b079a6ce0268b87263039","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d9f53128b7ab0a0d9b0b079a6ce0268b87263039","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d9f53128b7ab0a0d9b0b079a6ce0268b87263039"}]},{"sha":"d9f53128b7ab0a0d9b0b079a6ce0268b87263039","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGQ5ZjUzMTI4YjdhYjBhMGQ5YjBiMDc5YTZjZTAyNjhiODcyNjMwMzk","commit":{"author":{"name":"iceweasel-oai","email":"iceweasel@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T20:58:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T20:58:20Z"},"message":"[codex] Handle PowerShell UTF-8 setup failures (#24949)\n\nFixes #12496.\n\n## Why\n\nWindows sandboxed PowerShell commands can run under\n`ConstrainedLanguage` on some machines, especially enterprise-managed\nWindows environments. In that mode, our PowerShell command prelude could\nfail before every command because it directly assigned\n`[Console]::OutputEncoding` to UTF-8. The actual user command still ran,\nbut Codex surfaced noisy `Cannot set property. Property setting is\nsupported only on core types in this language mode.` output for every\nshell call.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Makes the PowerShell UTF-8 output encoding prelude best-effort by\nwrapping the assignment in `try { ... } catch {}`.\n- Keeps the existing UTF-8 behavior when PowerShell allows the\nassignment.\n- Adds focused tests for adding the prelude and avoiding duplicate\nprelude insertion.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo fmt -p codex-shell-command`\n- `cargo check -p codex-shell-command`\n- `git diff --check`\n- Verified a local `ConstrainedLanguage` PowerShell probe prints only\nthe command output with no property-setting error.\n- Verified `codex exec` from a temporary `chcp 437` context reports\n`utf-8` / `65001` and preserves non-ASCII output (`café`, `漢字`).","tree":{"sha":"b829f6640234c5a283ada20be386162e1ed8859a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/b829f6640234c5a283ada20be386162e1ed8859a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/d9f53128b7ab0a0d9b0b079a6ce0268b87263039","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGKxsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARMwQAIJ099MKVT6SBKU+51m/RcL1\n7w3i7wEgGptSO9E3Ze7lJTZvliVfRkxIsGSS3XAEWJyhTrcV4jdlAYpKljODHR2G\nUgTU8OjH1geZRiPfZMcEXyo0G2OuPIJ00N+LS/pURasbRof/VOTsYj/Eyl7KjNN4\nj9MqwRIGr9U/5Pk3EfGj3TX/4t3Z/1Ja3AT5n4bq0LeB6dZYBbBQ/6vnppJ3ZwDJ\n/owi3G0Kl/N62PDpFtmS59bzJ97fTSLRnvrzFRjKmUpfx7W5Ft8d6pEzV0oWjDqG\nl+MmbNlNPtvqYmgZLRHrvbFuA9XYs7S4IY0QDpMYNiVVkxv3elTvvOk8Vyhl9yth\nPUU82MPXQFjaNjitOiizXz3Lm0zZhjkK6x4xWvPdcB/7sCX5NejgaF+Q2d+YSQH8\nkC02lPFK5IhjA2B6dPP4OrlNiskkej+yYr2PPaZq9hONsPaacli2AWzM7fnQptwn\nh0HqJyioakQ6L3zLAyjdJpgHoD2ccMoEhQ+t7oI5PNEli5dQ3Nk1B6SL0O7ENgVG\nxXP/grd63b9fWDx9J4BiySXsb8PDkkXxLwn1vsULoulSCA68AgU06evTbYb2hh0C\nt9QBPXjYehAtWAnHoychg0CMr2E1AXdTs9xrCcPdF+8SZR+2M36GWGLbWUZpyms+\n5VzUupMvefhnHnyo2Ar9\n=jn8/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b829f6640234c5a283ada20be386162e1ed8859a\nparent 2e0c4f4977a042c90505ac5465a924192b198872\nauthor iceweasel-oai <iceweasel@openai.com> 1780001900 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780001900 -0700\n\n[codex] Handle PowerShell UTF-8 setup failures (#24949)\n\nFixes #12496.\n\n## Why\n\nWindows sandboxed PowerShell commands can run under\n`ConstrainedLanguage` on some machines, especially enterprise-managed\nWindows environments. In that mode, our PowerShell command prelude could\nfail before every command because it directly assigned\n`[Console]::OutputEncoding` to UTF-8. The actual user command still ran,\nbut Codex surfaced noisy `Cannot set property. Property setting is\nsupported only on core types in this language mode.` output for every\nshell call.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Makes the PowerShell UTF-8 output encoding prelude best-effort by\nwrapping the assignment in `try { ... } catch {}`.\n- Keeps the existing UTF-8 behavior when PowerShell allows the\nassignment.\n- Adds focused tests for adding the prelude and avoiding duplicate\nprelude insertion.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo fmt -p codex-shell-command`\n- `cargo check -p codex-shell-command`\n- `git diff --check`\n- Verified a local `ConstrainedLanguage` PowerShell probe prints only\nthe command output with no property-setting error.\n- Verified `codex exec` from a temporary `chcp 437` context reports\n`utf-8` / `65001` and preserves non-ASCII output (`café`, `漢字`).","verified_at":"2026-05-28T20:58:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d9f53128b7ab0a0d9b0b079a6ce0268b87263039","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d9f53128b7ab0a0d9b0b079a6ce0268b87263039","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d9f53128b7ab0a0d9b0b079a6ce0268b87263039/comments","author":{"login":"iceweasel-oai","id":234057055,"node_id":"U_kgDODfNtXw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234057055?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/iceweasel-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2e0c4f4977a042c90505ac5465a924192b198872","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2e0c4f4977a042c90505ac5465a924192b198872","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2e0c4f4977a042c90505ac5465a924192b198872"}]},{"sha":"2e0c4f4977a042c90505ac5465a924192b198872","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDJlMGM0ZjQ5NzdhMDQyYzkwNTA1YWM1NDY1YTkyNDE5MmIxOTg4NzI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Felipe Coury","email":"felipe.coury@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T19:53:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T19:53:59Z"},"message":"fix(tui): prevent repository-configured code execution in /diff (#24954)\n\n## Why\n\n`/diff` is intended to display working-tree changes, but its Git\ninvocations honored repository-selected executable helpers. A repository\ncould configure diff/text conversion helpers, clean/process filters,\n`core.fsmonitor`, or `post-index-change` hooks that execute when a user\nruns `/diff`.\n\nFixes\n[PSEC-4395](https://linear.app/openai/issue/PSEC-4395/codex-cli-diff-executes-repository-selected-diff-helpers).\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Pass `--no-textconv` and `--no-ext-diff` for tracked and untracked\ndiff generation.\n- Discover configured `filter.<driver>.clean` and `.process` entries,\nthen neutralize the selected drivers through structured\n`GIT_CONFIG_KEY_*` / `GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_*` overrides, including driver\nnames containing `=`.\n- Run all `/diff` Git probes with `core.fsmonitor=false` and a null\n`core.hooksPath`.\n- Use short submodule reporting while ignoring dirty submodule\nworktrees, since inspecting a checked-out submodule for dirtiness can\nexecute filters from that child repository. This intentionally omits\ndirty-only submodule markers in order to preserve the non-executing\nsecurity boundary.\n- Add real-Git marker tests covering filters, fsmonitor, hooks, and\nconfigured helpers inside checked-out submodules.\n\n## How to Test\n\n1. In a repository with ordinary tracked and untracked edits, run\n`/diff`.\n2. Confirm the normal working-tree diff is shown for top-level files.\n3. Run the targeted tests below; they configure executable marker\nhelpers for repository filters, fsmonitor, hooks, and a checked-out\nsubmodule, then verify `/diff` does not invoke them.\n4. Confirm a dirty-only submodule does not cause Codex to enter the\nsubmodule and execute its configured helper.\n\nTargeted tests:\n- `just test -p codex-tui get_git_diff_`\n\nValidation note: `just test -p codex-tui` runs the new coverage, but\nthis worktree currently also has two unrelated failing guardian tests:\n`app::tests::update_feature_flags_disabling_guardian_clears_review_policy_and_restores_default`\nand\n`app::tests::update_feature_flags_disabling_guardian_clears_manual_review_policy_without_history`.","tree":{"sha":"7f38ef3c1a17acd35d6092611a6822872dbe7566","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/7f38ef3c1a17acd35d6092611a6822872dbe7566"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/2e0c4f4977a042c90505ac5465a924192b198872","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGJ1XCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdV0QAAadgTaScLB6jf2WD2H5Stw/\nqXbkkSnvj56Nu1iyKx21iYYpYOSZ31+VHQksNZDINYOvmeSoKrtgC4z0/kgbuCoV\nzAVkxP93N3lBLrvIbcvuce75MKo9dFcXDGYiLF1RKdx81cxULRK3tmJ7sNWvB/Iv\nt+qB1hEhoYFufgiOJ50jsHdVdeXjthuo1wev+tlvLLg+Uz5g3rgOrRc2ncMbK6a8\nFuonzKDJ19avdeCficTI/dWrdRMlJwcDlmP8Kx7RJigKgom9v3mkUUg/LHR3ytBq\nCi8f+BnxniAfCb7Y6v6yogmwgFjT4RDMhdmTFNJ0WBLZPpRV9XBiDULjx/W20yjW\npZFMU11QQ/G8fVeBlE4UWa1Mfj0W8h6XK2b5b7PfNmgTmb9RslPD75GM8o5SzPbh\nIHYDcB+A6U1tlQg+vo3FYIW211yvZrGXIAYiAw3Sk7Mcx6HtbGPqweJvA4xi9ynv\nfCkSHcm3RUiHoHEUL3swk5JcOBUsd/zECga4I8IomAXkWr/XMujKl5wLbc9BsONk\nFshRshGaYhHoMWCPtd5HQv2IZDwyLU0KZ4+P4kJgEU6x9yAUIjmnE9rIlDe/tXoG\nry4YtxOtjl0wIeDtN4iYGB7uZFhtd/pkdMy/QoaegRPsNGQmYYe3vYWn3hnWBn7i\nT7K5iTZ8MQEXQ/aN8oqr\n=M3UZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7f38ef3c1a17acd35d6092611a6822872dbe7566\nparent b90ec46387927582371ad737cd22981bf26e1614\nauthor Felipe Coury <felipe.coury@openai.com> 1779998039 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779998039 -0300\n\nfix(tui): prevent repository-configured code execution in /diff (#24954)\n\n## Why\n\n`/diff` is intended to display working-tree changes, but its Git\ninvocations honored repository-selected executable helpers. A repository\ncould configure diff/text conversion helpers, clean/process filters,\n`core.fsmonitor`, or `post-index-change` hooks that execute when a user\nruns `/diff`.\n\nFixes\n[PSEC-4395](https://linear.app/openai/issue/PSEC-4395/codex-cli-diff-executes-repository-selected-diff-helpers).\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Pass `--no-textconv` and `--no-ext-diff` for tracked and untracked\ndiff generation.\n- Discover configured `filter.<driver>.clean` and `.process` entries,\nthen neutralize the selected drivers through structured\n`GIT_CONFIG_KEY_*` / `GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_*` overrides, including driver\nnames containing `=`.\n- Run all `/diff` Git probes with `core.fsmonitor=false` and a null\n`core.hooksPath`.\n- Use short submodule reporting while ignoring dirty submodule\nworktrees, since inspecting a checked-out submodule for dirtiness can\nexecute filters from that child repository. This intentionally omits\ndirty-only submodule markers in order to preserve the non-executing\nsecurity boundary.\n- Add real-Git marker tests covering filters, fsmonitor, hooks, and\nconfigured helpers inside checked-out submodules.\n\n## How to Test\n\n1. In a repository with ordinary tracked and untracked edits, run\n`/diff`.\n2. Confirm the normal working-tree diff is shown for top-level files.\n3. Run the targeted tests below; they configure executable marker\nhelpers for repository filters, fsmonitor, hooks, and a checked-out\nsubmodule, then verify `/diff` does not invoke them.\n4. Confirm a dirty-only submodule does not cause Codex to enter the\nsubmodule and execute its configured helper.\n\nTargeted tests:\n- `just test -p codex-tui get_git_diff_`\n\nValidation note: `just test -p codex-tui` runs the new coverage, but\nthis worktree currently also has two unrelated failing guardian tests:\n`app::tests::update_feature_flags_disabling_guardian_clears_review_policy_and_restores_default`\nand\n`app::tests::update_feature_flags_disabling_guardian_clears_manual_review_policy_without_history`.","verified_at":"2026-05-28T19:53:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2e0c4f4977a042c90505ac5465a924192b198872","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2e0c4f4977a042c90505ac5465a924192b198872","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2e0c4f4977a042c90505ac5465a924192b198872/comments","author":{"login":"fcoury-oai","id":272635208,"node_id":"U_kgDOEEAVSA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272635208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/fcoury-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b90ec46387927582371ad737cd22981bf26e1614","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b90ec46387927582371ad737cd22981bf26e1614","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b90ec46387927582371ad737cd22981bf26e1614"}]},{"sha":"b90ec46387927582371ad737cd22981bf26e1614","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGI5MGVjNDYzODc5Mjc1ODIzNzFhZDczN2NkMjI5ODFiZjI2ZTE2MTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T19:43:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T19:43:30Z"},"message":"Add `codex app-server --stdio` alias (#24940)\n\n## Summary\n- Add `--stdio` as a direct alias for `codex app-server --listen\nstdio://`.\n- Keep `--stdio` and `--listen` mutually exclusive.\n- Update the app-server README to document both forms.","tree":{"sha":"8fc0f0b3c948721d18eaaf340d6b0fe6dd55165c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/8fc0f0b3c948721d18eaaf340d6b0fe6dd55165c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/b90ec46387927582371ad737cd22981bf26e1614","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGJriCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArS0QAADcSQPhF+FtB8q4jkz4ak0W\nRaMXtOPfBpK2XH9a7kU/4it7gKvV27+OTnbI/DsHzXEBpbslC/hdXOAZQdrvr/Yl\nq0BgRQ0CyJw0ko6/TnHOyVHPAmqRlM7PXroJ2OWCwJ3QI4tGlMP4bw7t7YrDP/nG\nHPopB70zYf6FmcGge15L+Oj+67I1W/FboO1Wi4S2JkXP/1bYYszrvN7f97LVA7DI\nPaOEHGTJ7OaKx4zYGzYiPfDefG99QKCh7Rg+L8dtVCPfZ6T5AqImXLq6UCuDotfG\nT3UDxmhgVYhKm8B4AS5ZLmTI3YCWhVERN5PhWzniFsogJR1t8ZHFS0BZKuzDHLTj\nG2ZeW1SK2yTgofJfm06VpVPAZDbyapcQKlDZc3OZ1I5lzucMW4Ah/HY9wISwzMk2\n0AXbjBcEtPWgP7F5In0FsEI95bPUAKDBCSGJ28imvbU0/I77HGtRN+dP03dhn8BT\nc9nosR8BBCMdwEGMSkERbW7S+8L3o0CEbxnpCEm+5/QlYxOdgNleKv6/62a9lM10\nhMr5nhMY5ElUwuB3QcfxWcFbQqm1sKtFZQvF/rqVHZcPHMNot6akvTZDPbL9l/Q2\nXqJo6OZETNhWgTQHZPwmy3nXm5sbGwArKrebttLroj7QtvVUDsFizlUhFVhESO/W\nBEid3Wqti6uLHHdsr2QO\n=+KPW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8fc0f0b3c948721d18eaaf340d6b0fe6dd55165c\nparent 9dd39f334e8f9f2953f2314f6cb02e6307d26949\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1779997410 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779997410 -0700\n\nAdd `codex app-server --stdio` alias (#24940)\n\n## Summary\n- Add `--stdio` as a direct alias for `codex app-server --listen\nstdio://`.\n- Keep `--stdio` and `--listen` mutually exclusive.\n- Update the app-server README to document both forms.","verified_at":"2026-05-28T19:43:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b90ec46387927582371ad737cd22981bf26e1614","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b90ec46387927582371ad737cd22981bf26e1614","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b90ec46387927582371ad737cd22981bf26e1614/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9dd39f334e8f9f2953f2314f6cb02e6307d26949","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9dd39f334e8f9f2953f2314f6cb02e6307d26949","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9dd39f334e8f9f2953f2314f6cb02e6307d26949"}]},{"sha":"9dd39f334e8f9f2953f2314f6cb02e6307d26949","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDlkZDM5ZjMzNGU4ZjlmMjk1M2YyMzE0ZjZjYjAyZTYzMDdkMjY5NDk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T19:43:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T19:43:04Z"},"message":"Move Bazel Windows jobs onto codex-runners (#24952)\n\nThe codex-windows runner group should be much faster than the default\nGHA runners. Since bazel jobs on windows are frequently the long pole\nfor PRs checks, this will hopefully get people landing a bit faster.","tree":{"sha":"eb6c034aef49121f9ec2a94d04b8d5778d67f6d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/eb6c034aef49121f9ec2a94d04b8d5778d67f6d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/9dd39f334e8f9f2953f2314f6cb02e6307d26949","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGJrICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHhsQAJFwvlQJ7CLQ6KnIuv5uc4dj\nSuK/Hhjo7ie4UnQeBinmCMj1zG4i7D+bvgk4L+C2je8l5F2Q3rUrge/69rDohwDd\njMDnF9FVDwxdiBWYgven4bKM6uX7yydmjN/vfOAhRZiwJARgxyx2SncHtJ/koCPq\nAe4uKC27cOncXnwptrT5UuXrsxn1eP9hmA/l+6P9fiXORNU6ajtLGjLgAcXG5Fa5\nNv34/0akjFCOXVTrf1YBVD9nTO7YDbeYWCl59+5JMduUTXdNT1ZL09qThtVr51zS\n6x4xiKZo8V2g52zA2p4XIpTf7CyPZv80XLZG255rfcOU9tUxVVsCF8YU/lgagP/n\nFDrFtJn+akdD9P73chWFRY8oRbAFwTwdROVMAucC8jR5QbHcidaDxjK7h0aCylaW\nxSyw7S3pP0SFfDSJqiPcwb7FZPphldxHcq+FQefGmIn6jwi8RgUAIkXKp7GmcZea\nGWoxoDXNRUYeNheoLj4WIkEKW0NlKS19FLbyPobAL5fMYSFas3xJWnVm3VI9Ju9+\nD3m8S6880ZgLrXfalxL0zug/1upsy2NXdVu144dUFo7MAoi4hDt9dIDQihgZRYqk\ntxmxAzVgWhV1xikoNHsVPHgmtp1DZI45GJZLid+Nku407Eg916zEhun8aINFo4UF\ngqeEZ4WDeF1E/FxOxJoD\n=zcwg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree eb6c034aef49121f9ec2a94d04b8d5778d67f6d1\nparent ecb41fcb64f22445b051d3943fc970d2ce51d0cd\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1779997384 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779997384 -0700\n\nMove Bazel Windows jobs onto codex-runners (#24952)\n\nThe codex-windows runner group should be much faster than the default\nGHA runners. Since bazel jobs on windows are frequently the long pole\nfor PRs checks, this will hopefully get people landing a bit faster.","verified_at":"2026-05-28T19:43:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9dd39f334e8f9f2953f2314f6cb02e6307d26949","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9dd39f334e8f9f2953f2314f6cb02e6307d26949","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9dd39f334e8f9f2953f2314f6cb02e6307d26949/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ecb41fcb64f22445b051d3943fc970d2ce51d0cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ecb41fcb64f22445b051d3943fc970d2ce51d0cd","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ecb41fcb64f22445b051d3943fc970d2ce51d0cd"}]},{"sha":"ecb41fcb64f22445b051d3943fc970d2ce51d0cd","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGVjYjQxZmNiNjRmMjI0NDViMDUxZDM5NDNmYzk3MGQyY2U1MWQwY2Q","commit":{"author":{"name":"Won Park","email":"won@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T18:44:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T18:44:55Z"},"message":"Add feature-gated standalone image generation extension (#24723)\n\n## Why\n\nAdd a standalone image generation path that can be exercised\nindependently of hosted Responses image generation, while retaining the\nhosted tool as fallback unless the extension is actually available to\nthe model.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added the `codex-image-generation-extension` crate with standalone\ngenerate/edit execution, prior-image selection for edits, model-visible\nimage output, and local generated-image persistence.\n- Installed the extension in app-server behind the disabled-by-default\n`imagegenext` feature and backend eligibility checks.\n- Updated core tool planning so eligible `image_gen.imagegen` exposure\nreplaces hosted `image_generation`, while unavailable configurations\nretain hosted fallback.\n- Added coverage for extension behavior, edit history reuse, feature\ngating, auth eligibility, and hosted-tool replacement.\n- The extension is installed through app-server only in this PR; other\nexecution paths retain hosted image generation because hosted\nreplacement occurs only when the standalone executor is actually\nregistered and model-visible.\n- The initial extension contract intentionally fixes the image model to\n`gpt-image-2` and uses automatic image parameters.\n- Native generated-image history/card parity and rollout persistence\ncleanup are intentionally deferred follow-up work.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-image-generation-extension`\n- `just test -p codex-features`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nhosted_tools_follow_provider_auth_model_and_config_gates`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server`\n- `just fix -p codex-image-generation-extension -p codex-features -p\ncodex-core -p codex-app-server`\n- `just fmt`\n- `just bazel-lock-update`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: jif-oai <jif@openai.com>","tree":{"sha":"37b2c44835fce4b710a981b1e889b0cac09b9f5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/37b2c44835fce4b710a981b1e889b0cac09b9f5f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/ecb41fcb64f22445b051d3943fc970d2ce51d0cd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGI0nCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbHQQAI9x7RSRuWwIDESgjhjSIdC3\nRb8kQIXN+xs1hvf1kKGSTG7TelfTOzv5BFjM/h4LebrZEz+R60y7fgOTGMB8NVAj\nB3ZZLGLZHTXFTOeeeEhZeVEiElqQZNP7GgeiftHTYmdNcAEaFCErZzmfDJyaFTKu\nk6lw4rMiLUEWSTRa9CjfmZWTA1yzPjldgVHrwF4afTmJoQ7DECPFenv8jgUbhwyi\n2cwMqboNA/CYlSEsqrDbhjgHYSjYyxjTXOale11PYY1jDA5Q+Bwshrloic6QpB54\nCrxEKJfwY4C5vyjszdTxkCx8U02dIsQW6o1sQ8vibZ1TjMU9kL8cmBALcplyq7WX\nFAKkjcRpmdZr91vAvEElxmRAfuvL+KR5KSqy+LehOgg4qLMkmtTUnTpOoqaMx99q\nejZ4Hyn/eXgUu0wUqT7SvSrT9+06oZGucyFi3xW1dxDujbGG5D06GiOPh+drOjOM\njPqNBNQp+iP0Pe9viENg57vO8O0JnshBTqoAZSVCh4taSsauWNyVHbv0wsiLJv1I\nXeT9sLmaivdTorF8+9mzMKx3yrnI5pHoPpK2LBJ7iXKaf6gBcTvW/7uT7H9y5A/p\nDn5FjbuCrXyW64R56xFMWBFKLpzG45ihIsCUUC4WV/Bqb3b+wX5OimCAoB3cASsV\nvjjLI7RRIwUiDksekpUl\n=qYZM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 37b2c44835fce4b710a981b1e889b0cac09b9f5f\nparent 462deb0426bfea72f80ae7d56605958d7206309e\nauthor Won Park <won@openai.com> 1779993895 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779993895 -0700\n\nAdd feature-gated standalone image generation extension (#24723)\n\n## Why\n\nAdd a standalone image generation path that can be exercised\nindependently of hosted Responses image generation, while retaining the\nhosted tool as fallback unless the extension is actually available to\nthe model.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added the `codex-image-generation-extension` crate with standalone\ngenerate/edit execution, prior-image selection for edits, model-visible\nimage output, and local generated-image persistence.\n- Installed the extension in app-server behind the disabled-by-default\n`imagegenext` feature and backend eligibility checks.\n- Updated core tool planning so eligible `image_gen.imagegen` exposure\nreplaces hosted `image_generation`, while unavailable configurations\nretain hosted fallback.\n- Added coverage for extension behavior, edit history reuse, feature\ngating, auth eligibility, and hosted-tool replacement.\n- The extension is installed through app-server only in this PR; other\nexecution paths retain hosted image generation because hosted\nreplacement occurs only when the standalone executor is actually\nregistered and model-visible.\n- The initial extension contract intentionally fixes the image model to\n`gpt-image-2` and uses automatic image parameters.\n- Native generated-image history/card parity and rollout persistence\ncleanup are intentionally deferred follow-up work.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-image-generation-extension`\n- `just test -p codex-features`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nhosted_tools_follow_provider_auth_model_and_config_gates`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server`\n- `just fix -p codex-image-generation-extension -p codex-features -p\ncodex-core -p codex-app-server`\n- `just fmt`\n- `just bazel-lock-update`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: jif-oai <jif@openai.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-28T18:44:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ecb41fcb64f22445b051d3943fc970d2ce51d0cd","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ecb41fcb64f22445b051d3943fc970d2ce51d0cd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ecb41fcb64f22445b051d3943fc970d2ce51d0cd/comments","author":{"login":"won-openai","id":262224683,"node_id":"U_kgDOD6E7Kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/262224683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/won-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"462deb0426bfea72f80ae7d56605958d7206309e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/462deb0426bfea72f80ae7d56605958d7206309e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/462deb0426bfea72f80ae7d56605958d7206309e"}]},{"sha":"462deb0426bfea72f80ae7d56605958d7206309e","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDQ2MmRlYjA0MjZiZmVhNzJmODBhZTdkNTY2MDU5NThkNzIwNjMwOWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif-oai","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T18:05:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T18:05:41Z"},"message":"Wire task completion into thread-idle lifecycle (#24928)\n\n## Why\n\n#24744 introduced the thread idle lifecycle hook so idle continuation\ncan be owned by lifecycle contributors instead of hard-coded goal\nruntime plumbing. Task completion still called\n`goal_runtime_apply(GoalRuntimeEvent::MaybeContinueIfIdle)` directly, so\nthe post-turn idle transition remained goal-specific and did not notify\ngeneric thread lifecycle contributors.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Add `Session::emit_thread_idle_lifecycle_if_idle()` to gate idle\nemission on both no active turn and no queued trigger-turn mailbox work.\n- Call that helper when a task clears the active turn, replacing the\ndirect `GoalRuntimeEvent::MaybeContinueIfIdle` path.\n- Cover the behavior with `codex-core` session tests for emitting after\ntask completion and suppressing idle emission while trigger-turn mailbox\nwork is pending.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New tests in `core/src/session/tests.rs` exercise the idle lifecycle\nemission and trigger-turn mailbox guard.","tree":{"sha":"d078ffd9ac63afbb08fca4651a3c8c1edfdd806f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d078ffd9ac63afbb08fca4651a3c8c1edfdd806f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/462deb0426bfea72f80ae7d56605958d7206309e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGIP1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABP0QAKzePHe5sgXS0OwqHAdlUobC\nzfQquc/gRdQxW1FjSepihnWZ/Lr3DXGCrMmEJmIlqikMCTGiGKXRIdKigj0NZk2D\nUiEZmUXCKnglsEi96z152mT77oZvuZ9t6W1isHTrWmfNt107Liat4OBofBjxJbka\nmNdlpUj2zE6yO+Sd2Usztk3M2O069mQpCsb1UH1wEJMn4SgN4XS+twao6jDXng8A\nkR64sXSeOSiI4TBMla+tFeOb2nUG8KvNl5ESK0di12g0O/nEHZIIkAArzfznoOPV\nyMJt0mbRprCqVZQNlp9/VaRXy5tI3VJpOc1SBpJahefsutVqCv0l7WsOBcZbIYVh\nEKxAK6C82O62kU2tnUuWvLw4PSDIOJaVVzX9owQKf4Z+t4MZw6ZTTHCqkREBZRaB\nI+ors1oR0xRb6mLvd8Fn5Dg9/anzGNF28hemWhswnq4229ji2YQba/6qJG0A4ChE\n85kEdTbJNBDGD9Ys+MEjNmyDFD4mo5jkFtNNRYsOAyFe7wJrF/bsCeToxAvNDz3B\nsGS/gajMZJuGtIN+AGKWX+joTgOTPCDBqwqNH0LP1opT4hRyNkbdU3f3Ued8LtjT\nGBB+cSwp+PidFMRGy/AuvbG2p8nHVPAMb3Sj+VEW8nWGDVHiOjfFZ9k9+vXlTqCo\nV/jB6nCtDRv9Ca1NTQlu\n=EE8+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d078ffd9ac63afbb08fca4651a3c8c1edfdd806f\nparent c2508db60db0eae343d12a586dcfbc37e491f122\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1779991541 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779991541 +0200\n\nWire task completion into thread-idle lifecycle (#24928)\n\n## Why\n\n#24744 introduced the thread idle lifecycle hook so idle continuation\ncan be owned by lifecycle contributors instead of hard-coded goal\nruntime plumbing. Task completion still called\n`goal_runtime_apply(GoalRuntimeEvent::MaybeContinueIfIdle)` directly, so\nthe post-turn idle transition remained goal-specific and did not notify\ngeneric thread lifecycle contributors.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Add `Session::emit_thread_idle_lifecycle_if_idle()` to gate idle\nemission on both no active turn and no queued trigger-turn mailbox work.\n- Call that helper when a task clears the active turn, replacing the\ndirect `GoalRuntimeEvent::MaybeContinueIfIdle` path.\n- Cover the behavior with `codex-core` session tests for emitting after\ntask completion and suppressing idle emission while trigger-turn mailbox\nwork is pending.\n\n## Verification\n\n- New tests in `core/src/session/tests.rs` exercise the idle lifecycle\nemission and trigger-turn mailbox guard.","verified_at":"2026-05-28T18:05:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/462deb0426bfea72f80ae7d56605958d7206309e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/462deb0426bfea72f80ae7d56605958d7206309e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/462deb0426bfea72f80ae7d56605958d7206309e/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c2508db60db0eae343d12a586dcfbc37e491f122","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c2508db60db0eae343d12a586dcfbc37e491f122","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c2508db60db0eae343d12a586dcfbc37e491f122"}]},{"sha":"c2508db60db0eae343d12a586dcfbc37e491f122","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGMyNTA4ZGI2MGRiMGVhZTM0M2QxMmE1ODZkY2ZiYzM3ZTQ5MWYxMjI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T17:49:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@gi