m/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2a1158b8e2f941afed79db95731b16c8a8db5774","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2a1158b8e2f941afed79db95731b16c8a8db5774","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2a1158b8e2f941afed79db95731b16c8a8db5774"}]},{"sha":"2a1158b8e2f941afed79db95731b16c8a8db5774","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDJhMTE1OGI4ZTJmOTQxYWZlZDc5ZGI5NTczMWIxNmM4YThkYjU3NzQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Brent Traut","email":"btraut@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T16:18:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T16:18:13Z"},"message":"feat(app-server): include turns page on thread resume (#23534)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe client currently calls `thread/resume` to establish live updates and\nimmediately follows it with `thread/turns/list` to hydrate recent turns.\nThis lets `thread/resume` return that page directly, eliminating a round\ntrip and the ordering/deduplication gap between the two calls.\n\nExperimental clients opt in with `initialTurnsPage: { limit,\nsortDirection, itemsView }`. The response returns `initialTurnsPage` as\na `TurnsPage`, including cursors for paging further back in history.\nKeeping the controls in a nested opt-in object provides the useful\n`thread/turns/list` knobs without spreading page-specific parameters\nacross `thread/resume`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just write-app-server-schema --experimental`\n- `just write-app-server-schema`\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server\nthread_resume_initial_turns_page_matches_requested_turns_list_page\n--tests`\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server\nthread_resume_rejoins_running_thread_even_with_override_mismatch\n--tests`\n- `just fix -p codex-app-server-protocol -p codex-app-server`","tree":{"sha":"c5c97cbffea0c8cb4a5428474337fde7ab8c89ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c5c97cbffea0c8cb4a5428474337fde7ab8c89ce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/2a1158b8e2f941afed79db95731b16c8a8db5774","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGGrFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAt9EQAKdVnnrK4LJpIfrA2jBOVn/g\nZW7vvbewUc9fuB5CsRo9aFGM5XbYm6NtE3nbJsUgCRjFXeZkZnxHict6F+QOk2jc\nvEgZTOyw4FRhM1Jokpgp99Sdx9ac52Nx+ZUZeH3sBG9Or8xGn272jDziWwK0qZ0G\nuopB1fdvhywYuFkoRXH8bg4XOjbifUh5eKgMVk1VJtX1hsUNYAvr1gorSbXyCqoa\nFqRIXpwHsVqp/5jDBIug/SyP0PIir0LC/J71Fut2NWv3TFUTS7ic3t0jhbBz/1J9\nhBpPITz1GHn/55h35nfIwnRjQvHZ/SCGQYndyx4iI2d+dyOAKQ6j/f3GwEM0Ik0O\nIVsVwgh8V9TEnXnzf5BA2jXcFYTq5lhLaMITN08MAuG3qZmX58j794uQG5vNowg8\nVgO/fyeKDPl/HF8J7AuXNQ8pRJiBbQjjf3c57S7kuHmE/R5VpL4EIZ3g/pe5N4rC\nbrTDhr+LA5JKh5jAXVvOgHSp39GbR79RVzvWik3F8M4yTu3yp3fMtikRkGFDFEl2\nYpAsH2tUnYpHLlYlLjZlyEFbAQpxIUjSfrCqdNL7vxI/8zH7fg3nO18nT2pg34e3\nrhiLEDjOf5wKt7UpxRehMnhqnpAhG3DagYdqJlvrXzrBgZjn3rQ5emKrzIiuiciN\nFCoMSQ1EhLGkE2QunnyK\n=TiKV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c5c97cbffea0c8cb4a5428474337fde7ab8c89ce\nparent 2066874415e1c3dcd1ec28cbf26506dd74e35d2e\nauthor Brent Traut <btraut@openai.com> 1779985093 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779985093 -0700\n\nfeat(app-server): include turns page on thread resume (#23534)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe client currently calls `thread/resume` to establish live updates and\nimmediately follows it with `thread/turns/list` to hydrate recent turns.\nThis lets `thread/resume` return that page directly, eliminating a round\ntrip and the ordering/deduplication gap between the two calls.\n\nExperimental clients opt in with `initialTurnsPage: { limit,\nsortDirection, itemsView }`. The response returns `initialTurnsPage` as\na `TurnsPage`, including cursors for paging further back in history.\nKeeping the controls in a nested opt-in object provides the useful\n`thread/turns/list` knobs without spreading page-specific parameters\nacross `thread/resume`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just write-app-server-schema --experimental`\n- `just write-app-server-schema`\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server\nthread_resume_initial_turns_page_matches_requested_turns_list_page\n--tests`\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server\nthread_resume_rejoins_running_thread_even_with_override_mismatch\n--tests`\n- `just fix -p codex-app-server-protocol -p codex-app-server`","verified_at":"2026-05-28T16:18:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2a1158b8e2f941afed79db95731b16c8a8db5774","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2a1158b8e2f941afed79db95731b16c8a8db5774","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2a1158b8e2f941afed79db95731b16c8a8db5774/comments","author":{"login":"btraut-openai","id":284131405,"node_id":"U_kgDOEO-ATQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/284131405?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/btraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/btraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2066874415e1c3dcd1ec28cbf26506dd74e35d2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2066874415e1c3dcd1ec28cbf26506dd74e35d2e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2066874415e1c3dcd1ec28cbf26506dd74e35d2e"}]},{"sha":"2066874415e1c3dcd1ec28cbf26506dd74e35d2e","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDIwNjY4NzQ0MTVlMWMzZGNkMWVjMjhjYmYyNjUwNmRkNzRlMzVkMmU","commit":{"author":{"name":"sayan-oai","email":"sayan@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T16:13:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T16:13:43Z"},"message":"extension-api: add TurnItemEmitter to tool calls (#24813)\n\n## Why\nExtension-contributed tools need to emit visible turn items through\nCodex's normal event and persistence pipeline.\n\n## What\n- Add `TurnItemEmitter` to extension `ToolCall`s and route the core\nimplementation through `Session::emit_turn_item_*`.\n- Hold weak session and turn references so retained tool calls cannot\nkeep host state alive.\n- Provide a no-op emitter for extension test callers.\n\n## Test Plan\n- `just test -p codex-core -E\n'test(passes_turn_fields_and_scoped_turn_item_emitter_to_extension_call)'`\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: jif-oai <jif@openai.com>","tree":{"sha":"ae2aeeae917bab7c84b8907d511ea5204ce30c0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/ae2aeeae917bab7c84b8907d511ea5204ce30c0e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/2066874415e1c3dcd1ec28cbf26506dd74e35d2e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGGm4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfDYQAA4T/Tz25tOgIKUc5m9zJ4Xp\nT7Ap9MmbhTjSWTOrqlvRh/zcjNeyT4OlgOzjWCcHD+KNjkZHcDZqElVc+cxIl5oC\nNZZARnGtAnoJ0C8CD5Ycbjg62lhfmuEjSLM6fnbGnS0z7jVycp/HXqkihYi+9Lgt\nx1Lv8TgdDkrunF3Pf7e6yeaEbRIJzROaxFGZJS4HrYT0yNPyTWXiRtKUMmYU6KrI\nqNmhoPa59aHvB6Zh0VUDxCIj8ULInysWJjCARai9DKUtOA9DU3as7V5Q+mp28/wU\nH4A63Xv7ZbmMluYzbz/czmBCJsKBimgp/I7PX1wSh13d1fSlPjWcjt/b72HWu1gx\nrJNvenyB2GKICiVpnNG8WmSRKLH0Hi0/iX13xiO6VyIcy5zNWCV+tOqbG7KvkZX9\nyTU+vwrjX1JhBHwbntVZzVfcrrVCUBBKt3f1XhsoWhkmwxdG3+9LIppMkEXuMPGo\nnnYSEWk7EfC39UNiVYtENb3VFy3qDORIBxmO+slq/nf12L55ty0oqzmURUoLGHV3\nc6xagZF8uRR9x65ykR756eQ+IYdwKpirUMXZLgpE+2FJ2kkFVT6sN2Of5nj2VGn0\nKtCa+aOS6wfHKoV/HyJUTiugPc2LN1wPEznPPV3vbIByF4WiP/kkyGcEc68Fbl/B\nEOTcHA10nI0VFppwHlKo\n=61z8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ae2aeeae917bab7c84b8907d511ea5204ce30c0e\nparent a061befb469e9cb620767c1230aa1429008178b3\nauthor sayan-oai <sayan@openai.com> 1779984823 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779984823 -0700\n\nextension-api: add TurnItemEmitter to tool calls (#24813)\n\n## Why\nExtension-contributed tools need to emit visible turn items through\nCodex's normal event and persistence pipeline.\n\n## What\n- Add `TurnItemEmitter` to extension `ToolCall`s and route the core\nimplementation through `Session::emit_turn_item_*`.\n- Hold weak session and turn references so retained tool calls cannot\nkeep host state alive.\n- Provide a no-op emitter for extension test callers.\n\n## Test Plan\n- `just test -p codex-core -E\n'test(passes_turn_fields_and_scoped_turn_item_emitter_to_extension_call)'`\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: jif-oai <jif@openai.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-28T16:13:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2066874415e1c3dcd1ec28cbf26506dd74e35d2e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2066874415e1c3dcd1ec28cbf26506dd74e35d2e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2066874415e1c3dcd1ec28cbf26506dd74e35d2e/comments","author":{"login":"sayan-oai","id":244841968,"node_id":"U_kgDODpf98A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244841968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/sayan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a061befb469e9cb620767c1230aa1429008178b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a061befb469e9cb620767c1230aa1429008178b3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a061befb469e9cb620767c1230aa1429008178b3"}]},{"sha":"a061befb469e9cb620767c1230aa1429008178b3","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGEwNjFiZWZiNDY5ZTljYjYyMDc2N2MxMjMwYWExNDI5MDA4MTc4YjM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T15:49:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T15:49:01Z"},"message":"Remove libubsan CI workaround (#24782)\n\nIt seems that this was added to allow rustc to load proc macros that had\nbeen compiled with UBSan enabled, which zig does for debug and\n`ReleaseSafe` builds. When zig drives the link of the final binary it\nknows to include the ubsan runtime, but our zig-built artifacts are\nbeing linked into a binary whose linking rustc drives. This removes the\nlibubsan workaround we have and replaces it with\n`-fno-sanitize=undefined` passed to zig.\n\nThe new argument is passed at the end of zig's args so should take\nprecedence over any earlier arguments from the script's caller.","tree":{"sha":"d6dc45f436fd2ddcddcc6dc47f2db62f78770fb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d6dc45f436fd2ddcddcc6dc47f2db62f78770fb5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a061befb469e9cb620767c1230aa1429008178b3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGGPtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXV0QADaZ97CkwSgaJez8gZmHRH3L\nyWv44VBcI57cxoIHMHahLXjZPEgo/wjvQzhoCFyRbXAEBAASkDOd4AoULxrqm5QE\njU4mHsQ3m/yxibzMtkIYEk8G0bRu0wjIWvxThsrEBkVELWUJqyr4VymI2/+U8a26\nms41qPS1BsUkg1cBjbwTVsjuiSTPExZJXC1ELy1kAvd3MJWX4/YGFur/L5/q23oz\nKOQfngfyJ5+rDvIJIzMKYuPFqNncsJKYH6FjIKp0jSrVwfnZKdqT705AnS40wFx8\n2+pZQGmXikJ47a0v2x8uDoRvvd+cmakUKaES6OGrmNDGcpO3USwMQpiqBIJF0acA\nrl/5r97r33w8BEjvSsIsEfULECXrD5IsmxhQHMsJrVZpczCMurFyOZZ6lQ/JM2Ke\n1IxfpZ55ouv4mZBO1hANS2nopOE83epfGVJVpMqD9cIVNrNnjnddeN0UmgwB7Ihx\nNjpA4peABPaUaqu0qmJv4eeYLCr/s86iG9Lctsq2dzIY9sEQUJg7R1+f114QdSr+\nyg+alyQqT83NJ6buLzG0mKxctzBqIOtYhTUuTUDz+4ijRzFP5/mev+M62g5Lzunm\nakPe0coLfPoXyEeZhFUs+5DVBBcRKFL5dp/Ukw0/VYJqGupmRWOKM9fL1/QVUI50\n4HqnQsNIx0TTiLFr6RDo\n=DxqU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d6dc45f436fd2ddcddcc6dc47f2db62f78770fb5\nparent e426d48f6de446ba4e262ec1933e1e1d7dcddd03\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1779983341 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779983341 +0000\n\nRemove libubsan CI workaround (#24782)\n\nIt seems that this was added to allow rustc to load proc macros that had\nbeen compiled with UBSan enabled, which zig does for debug and\n`ReleaseSafe` builds. When zig drives the link of the final binary it\nknows to include the ubsan runtime, but our zig-built artifacts are\nbeing linked into a binary whose linking rustc drives. This removes the\nlibubsan workaround we have and replaces it with\n`-fno-sanitize=undefined` passed to zig.\n\nThe new argument is passed at the end of zig's args so should take\nprecedence over any earlier arguments from the script's caller.","verified_at":"2026-05-28T15:49:01Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a061befb469e9cb620767c1230aa1429008178b3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a061befb469e9cb620767c1230aa1429008178b3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a061befb469e9cb620767c1230aa1429008178b3/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e426d48f6de446ba4e262ec1933e1e1d7dcddd03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e426d48f6de446ba4e262ec1933e1e1d7dcddd03","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e426d48f6de446ba4e262ec1933e1e1d7dcddd03"}]},{"sha":"e426d48f6de446ba4e262ec1933e1e1d7dcddd03","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGU0MjZkNDhmNmRlNDQ2YmE0ZTI2MmVjMTkzM2UxZTFkN2RjZGRkMDM","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif-oai","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T15:47:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T15:47:17Z"},"message":"Gate goal tools by thread eligibility (#24925)\n\n## Why\n\nGoal tools create and update goal state for a persistent thread. The\nextension was only checking whether goals were enabled before\nadvertising those tools, which meant they could be surfaced in contexts\nthat should not receive thread goal controls: ephemeral threads without\npersistent thread state and review subagents.\n\nThose sessions can still run the goal extension lifecycle, but the\nthread tools should only be visible when the current thread can safely\nuse them.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Adds a `GoalRuntimeConfig` that separates goal enablement from whether\ngoal tools are available for the current thread.\n- Computes tool eligibility on thread start from\n`persistent_thread_state_available` and `SessionSource`, hiding tools\nfor review subagents.\n- Uses `GoalRuntimeHandle::tools_visible()` when contributing thread\ntools so enabled runtime state does not automatically imply tool\nexposure.\n- Adds backend coverage for hiding goal tools on ephemeral threads and\nreview subagents.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Added `goal_tools_hidden_for_ephemeral_threads`.\n- Added `goal_tools_hidden_for_review_subagents`.","tree":{"sha":"27c43d296a0d3673fbdc8640ac5e44e4bda8fb20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/27c43d296a0d3673fbdc8640ac5e44e4bda8fb20"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e426d48f6de446ba4e262ec1933e1e1d7dcddd03","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGGOFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOcQQACIBkJ6gR8goH2YYQHF8ZhDK\nJcNIf0eJc1hYSIVXOAK92lV3qb9VNmnAL+H+k+vWpCanI9gdHqWFfUFRPvkcj07l\nA7Bmq++lXFGk5ZHyQM9T/76SbkzzE74Yj2YZwDBcN0z+XNPF7+/2mrwYNq39qs5/\nzp1hZgkSf6KWAKabhKFHPmf8uSsdOhovAzKdIR+K/iT0pIMzABFrZlqZp5Ds6n8n\n3yjcWEcuyZuVwGDbDUZnAGR7bG7d4yPasCnA+LouYO9VNNznmDgm2loUTY70Oz70\n+5a30W7k+H+WiaUtmQOG8c7h1A/hUCXSfpAvT5h95YWFaVdXb2nQl0p6CTDY3ebg\nv9sIAqny6YTQPUcoCQdSbP9mkvIHC3RBuYTNLKhOOdEp/TCaZH3t1uS43IHiInDN\nMY+shkxklwv8kZ2cD2xlVrhlaV8ZfE9PP5IGuTdOGZ8EtCcLFUNT0eq5Xug1wHcZ\ntoeqsjDo0eiVGszNnqu/CsZNfJW3G2p5K1/SXyUugXnfU6QgfulF/g+2kEWULG/F\nzume/K+4I1F9Yjk8HFfCVF+lS9UTjBI9/sito8nwzzUxOjNZFltmMimyGdFUIsKK\nL/KzWyGIHFZv5xkZ+XEItJwKsa+JIvBpv/5KTpyAQflPevNgJfEFpYR7uBbG9NoU\n4OcGaugszaG8ZcJzpcxW\n=LLKN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 27c43d296a0d3673fbdc8640ac5e44e4bda8fb20\nparent bd2a7329233b5bfc1e211a0d18419ca5c697c1e1\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1779983237 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779983237 +0200\n\nGate goal tools by thread eligibility (#24925)\n\n## Why\n\nGoal tools create and update goal state for a persistent thread. The\nextension was only checking whether goals were enabled before\nadvertising those tools, which meant they could be surfaced in contexts\nthat should not receive thread goal controls: ephemeral threads without\npersistent thread state and review subagents.\n\nThose sessions can still run the goal extension lifecycle, but the\nthread tools should only be visible when the current thread can safely\nuse them.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Adds a `GoalRuntimeConfig` that separates goal enablement from whether\ngoal tools are available for the current thread.\n- Computes tool eligibility on thread start from\n`persistent_thread_state_available` and `SessionSource`, hiding tools\nfor review subagents.\n- Uses `GoalRuntimeHandle::tools_visible()` when contributing thread\ntools so enabled runtime state does not automatically imply tool\nexposure.\n- Adds backend coverage for hiding goal tools on ephemeral threads and\nreview subagents.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Added `goal_tools_hidden_for_ephemeral_threads`.\n- Added `goal_tools_hidden_for_review_subagents`.","verified_at":"2026-05-28T15:47:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e426d48f6de446ba4e262ec1933e1e1d7dcddd03","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e426d48f6de446ba4e262ec1933e1e1d7dcddd03","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e426d48f6de446ba4e262ec1933e1e1d7dcddd03/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bd2a7329233b5bfc1e211a0d18419ca5c697c1e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bd2a7329233b5bfc1e211a0d18419ca5c697c1e1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bd2a7329233b5bfc1e211a0d18419ca5c697c1e1"}]},{"sha":"bd2a7329233b5bfc1e211a0d18419ca5c697c1e1","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGJkMmE3MzI5MjMzYjViZmMxZTIxMWEwZDE4NDE5Y2E1YzY5N2MxZTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T15:46:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T15:46:30Z"},"message":"Add app-server startup benchmark crate (#24651)\n\n## Summary\n- Add a new `app-server-start-bench` crate to measure app-server startup\nperformance\n- Wire the benchmark into the workspace and Bazel build so it can be run\nconsistently\n- Update lockfiles and repo automation to account for the new package","tree":{"sha":"16a1fab7294863e1bdab914c9f17d7061cbe1a7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/16a1fab7294863e1bdab914c9f17d7061cbe1a7b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/bd2a7329233b5bfc1e211a0d18419ca5c697c1e1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGGNWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqKUQAIZN0EcRjbw9vmpPTigKpGxh\nlkQL2L2VXU1lHHqy+4v8KVbed1Vj2WWzU9Kja1aVjhNrvbZoQsocOnuD/y1EpPGj\nUm98DC0BOSW+23PQsMcAjn6AHDKxl5gFYNsnXMaRiuN7304doj+/qsbeC5+vpbJv\n9q/T3nYxS+aFQ6ZKK71I9aEj3oh18kncRPkGhVNKQm4yVip8cKsbBGllk0WWa6mc\nKeDZnmfen2L0zqBjC4Nl/R66CtkRv1WRpqCPzZ+8fgB5XmGi8b9PJN0xQ1Nmrru2\nG0p31oXYxjWemZ58E9PQgAhpgS01mJ0xmwhgXBOHoV7zYHfIg6CwF7fe5TVI34ZC\n/P/7neDflBhC90KaEqfccQiFulzq8zgafsZBGd0NiV7z39BLj/kH2Bxche1PzITp\nr8n+u5MjHy8rJprIVI/5GePGz/6KfE3EOP1UeQz14gQNVSTYNGkA+yNBHenSNj6o\nqIKQNHtG34gK4aXBX/oHM0J8b+Iolg6LEMHVAi1wFpwb4IrDv44RU0fCSl2jvdAz\ns4vru6wYYIdVbEy9Lzl7AlNB0BPL8KeYRrP1k5healT9y5MkLlVenqILIjrtXJuH\n2psr5IHppGLnwon9lbi3vAjGoGxY6H9NoSORvPlHrA7bWKJjGu5UrejQss3dYFMe\n1CoIp6J8ohrKn/bmIWgR\n=zfMy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 16a1fab7294863e1bdab914c9f17d7061cbe1a7b\nparent a4ed6c5aa01bf9807b9159bb6caf11ecc11f0f1a\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1779983190 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779983190 -0700\n\nAdd app-server startup benchmark crate (#24651)\n\n## Summary\n- Add a new `app-server-start-bench` crate to measure app-server startup\nperformance\n- Wire the benchmark into the workspace and Bazel build so it can be run\nconsistently\n- Update lockfiles and repo automation to account for the new package","verified_at":"2026-05-28T15:46:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bd2a7329233b5bfc1e211a0d18419ca5c697c1e1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bd2a7329233b5bfc1e211a0d18419ca5c697c1e1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bd2a7329233b5bfc1e211a0d18419ca5c697c1e1/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a4ed6c5aa01bf9807b9159bb6caf11ecc11f0f1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a4ed6c5aa01bf9807b9159bb6caf11ecc11f0f1a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a4ed6c5aa01bf9807b9159bb6caf11ecc11f0f1a"}]},{"sha":"a4ed6c5aa01bf9807b9159bb6caf11ecc11f0f1a","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGE0ZWQ2YzVhYTAxYmY5ODA3YjkxNTliYjZjYWYxMWVjYzExZjBmMWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Vaibhav Srivastav","email":"vb@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T15:11:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T15:11:11Z"},"message":"[codex] Update OpenAI Docs skill (#24914)\n\n## Summary\n- update the bundled `openai-docs` system skill to match the latest\n`openai-docs-plus` content from `skills-internal`\n- add the cached Codex manual fetch helper and expand the skill routing\nfor Codex self-knowledge\n- keep the stable local skill identity and labels as `openai-docs`\n\n## Why\nThe built-in OpenAI Docs skill needed to reflect the current upstream\nguidance from `skills-internal` while preserving the local system-skill\nname used by Codex.\n\n## Impact\nCodex now ships the newer OpenAI Docs skill behavior for Codex\nself-knowledge and manual-first documentation lookups.\n\n## Validation\n- `just test -p codex-skills`\n- exact directory diff against transformed `skills-internal`\n`origin/main` was clean","tree":{"sha":"8068e21e17850784d180945a6321aea30188dc21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/8068e21e17850784d180945a6321aea30188dc21"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a4ed6c5aa01bf9807b9159bb6caf11ecc11f0f1a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGFsPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArYYQAGl3bSL81ys6/98sL3f9OF/Z\nO47CaRnTOb+nSK2boZWN7MHiqKaLoOtjgziPGqCR3bJFFfx5w7ruoYPwfhv+ElBE\n66ezmz4No8T3okaOURe08zW3aZJsChw592nGAfyyrqlMemwPqW0p+Drt7qqA8BhD\nD/wJjx+m/s0kl44mcHppDb1F2ssWMsXaYFe12gr/KNCkYE+k/6ubHbtw4GMccWJa\n7EXU/6X6z33AQeby0wFG5bepTbxB+hT2s4Ki0GA19yW6W8YECkfxhXybnAQrMVtU\nqk4R/Zn4hl7XiOrrs9VveWZfm9aOVwevXOqSEs1NpxZoBCk3lnETdyheS4jRchZe\nnaSZEQ0L93is2RdEAmoxBg4aN45WCOQ8VDQ3OyzngH7N8r+OLrIJm6UZ0O3yP+gQ\ntkMB90rrfIpOCj8cHOCQWG488veBqQO6Ff2PNvU2NFkDc5Evp6JcR0C1xHusPXPp\nLnZY3x/zYk/cRNUiEqLzXzA9uktyoeUCLMdxB2IksScLIfyEHLTmC5WaNzhVFmaX\nDKogzX5flE85CCrxVm3kO93lpU/WNuZn3K6lPrFPJAlWgdsSAHKGXZXbH5/QFhD8\ns4dQi45zUO0+fe6NaDiZFOHBxpVmqGT6I/Xg9Tc9VOQO+CrnI+B7tU7YVIkuGNbM\nV+GM86vxTYP9fk4rGNhd\n=oOot\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8068e21e17850784d180945a6321aea30188dc21\nparent 1c7832ffa37a3ab56f601497c00bfce120370bf9\nauthor Vaibhav Srivastav <vb@openai.com> 1779981071 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779981071 +0000\n\n[codex] Update OpenAI Docs skill (#24914)\n\n## Summary\n- update the bundled `openai-docs` system skill to match the latest\n`openai-docs-plus` content from `skills-internal`\n- add the cached Codex manual fetch helper and expand the skill routing\nfor Codex self-knowledge\n- keep the stable local skill identity and labels as `openai-docs`\n\n## Why\nThe built-in OpenAI Docs skill needed to reflect the current upstream\nguidance from `skills-internal` while preserving the local system-skill\nname used by Codex.\n\n## Impact\nCodex now ships the newer OpenAI Docs skill behavior for Codex\nself-knowledge and manual-first documentation lookups.\n\n## Validation\n- `just test -p codex-skills`\n- exact directory diff against transformed `skills-internal`\n`origin/main` was clean","verified_at":"2026-05-28T15:11:21Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a4ed6c5aa01bf9807b9159bb6caf11ecc11f0f1a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a4ed6c5aa01bf9807b9159bb6caf11ecc11f0f1a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a4ed6c5aa01bf9807b9159bb6caf11ecc11f0f1a/comments","author":{"login":"vb-openai","id":250380837,"node_id":"U_kgDODuyCJQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250380837?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vb-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/vb-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vb-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.g