oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e5afe5bf8cf4a9deaad9e0aa38890d44a27c933b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e5afe5bf8cf4a9deaad9e0aa38890d44a27c933b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e5afe5bf8cf4a9deaad9e0aa38890d44a27c933b"}]},{"sha":"e5afe5bf8cf4a9deaad9e0aa38890d44a27c933b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGU1YWZlNWJmOGNmNGE5ZGVhYWQ5ZTBhYTM4ODkwZDQ0YTI3YzkzM2I","commit":{"author":{"name":"cooper-oai","email":"cooper@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T12:40:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T12:40:17Z"},"message":"[codex-cli] Refresh near-expiry ChatGPT access tokens before requests (#23546)\n\n## Summary\n\n- refresh managed ChatGPT auth during auth resolution when its access\ntoken is inside ChatGPT web's five-minute near-expiry window\n- cover refresh-window decisions while preserving the existing\nexpired-token refresh path\n\n## Why\n\nCodex already resolves managed ChatGPT auth before outbound requests and\nrefreshes expired access tokens there. This change adjusts the existing\npredicate to refresh a still-valid access token once it is within the\nsame five-minute refresh window used by ChatGPT web, avoiding a request\nwith a token about to expire.\n\nA cross-process serialization follow-up was explored in #24663 and\nclosed for now; we do not currently suspect cross-process refresh races\nare a root cause of the refresh errors under investigation.\n\nExternal-token, API-key, and Agent Identity auth modes remain unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `bazel test //codex-rs/login:login-all-test`\n- `just fmt` runs Rust formatting successfully, then its Python SDK Ruff\nstep cannot install `openai-codex-cli-bin==0.131.0a4` on this Linux\nenvironment because no compatible wheel is published.","tree":{"sha":"c35c41238043010d7906efbef8472fb8eb2f8b18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c35c41238043010d7906efbef8472fb8eb2f8b18"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e5afe5bf8cf4a9deaad9e0aa38890d44a27c933b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGDexCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARj8QACvJoZdEZ2xHbYx799gByZts\nmVc+0G94G6tt29EpsZhAYyRmrH7VpeRH9IlHZFGKLrb9bvlbHk0pP+9EL/wr5a+2\n/JO+DK41dyISJsrkJdCh7fYtwqgoy1bNPL8l0+dZJpqwpBFNQ6opRMpwBgzqC3dv\nDxAdmgB586bjYW4ENU/+pd8uEC4GlXGZm2e4j1EQcjk8V/9RTWrNZLzUFIu9gIp7\nlBHyzSxP9+0yZGliG6SuV7llJ9atWur+bbsuENfTWjvHs0xqZRV4U9Tco2P+KupU\n3W5Tgne60x54zhIxPEK6OZK6VFJ/VqclyACgxlpTfMhPOq0Enwg5vSulzZ6+aTGl\nijRDIGyWn0846MrJDvrImUTrQiH1AR8Hj29MZHvktDhXjHtjVv49ln7tJgI/SRML\nb4DRnObYiDeIsesdKwdwZPDz+5VYqx1p2Ab0QR59QsLa3/SoY+kW9dsO5ik1Tr/d\nBuadMQFaLVqq0SNGkfvuMzdWSBZVyqfmunnQKdE+vhTRHLoYX8mt5niUD3c1Z/Kv\ndF1Z9nh/kUBrHHGLE9e9cokGQ5LkOM6fLW6YU5S4XFDoxqmWTCPBKVbXv1RPhpS3\nveCga21+Qe0/2O77Ul6NHOk6jQbKjAYVTHEsUPCw3AZDuiB/rOSTlSBwfb2aMt6F\nt7vLAkU6UwJpO3HLrVX4\n=H7t3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c35c41238043010d7906efbef8472fb8eb2f8b18\nparent 3abf96739b543a53d2a28870eaf2a05f61fa0c15\nauthor cooper-oai <cooper@openai.com> 1779972017 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779972017 -0700\n\n[codex-cli] Refresh near-expiry ChatGPT access tokens before requests (#23546)\n\n## Summary\n\n- refresh managed ChatGPT auth during auth resolution when its access\ntoken is inside ChatGPT web's five-minute near-expiry window\n- cover refresh-window decisions while preserving the existing\nexpired-token refresh path\n\n## Why\n\nCodex already resolves managed ChatGPT auth before outbound requests and\nrefreshes expired access tokens there. This change adjusts the existing\npredicate to refresh a still-valid access token once it is within the\nsame five-minute refresh window used by ChatGPT web, avoiding a request\nwith a token about to expire.\n\nA cross-process serialization follow-up was explored in #24663 and\nclosed for now; we do not currently suspect cross-process refresh races\nare a root cause of the refresh errors under investigation.\n\nExternal-token, API-key, and Agent Identity auth modes remain unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `bazel test //codex-rs/login:login-all-test`\n- `just fmt` runs Rust formatting successfully, then its Python SDK Ruff\nstep cannot install `openai-codex-cli-bin==0.131.0a4` on this Linux\nenvironment because no compatible wheel is published.","verified_at":"2026-05-28T12:40:18Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e5afe5bf8cf4a9deaad9e0aa38890d44a27c933b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e5afe5bf8cf4a9deaad9e0aa38890d44a27c933b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e5afe5bf8cf4a9deaad9e0aa38890d44a27c933b/comments","author":{"login":"cooper-oai","id":242064477,"node_id":"U_kgDODm2cXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/242064477?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/cooper-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3abf96739b543a53d2a28870eaf2a05f61fa0c15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3abf96739b543a53d2a28870eaf2a05f61fa0c15","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3abf96739b543a53d2a28870eaf2a05f61fa0c15"}]},{"sha":"3abf96739b543a53d2a28870eaf2a05f61fa0c15","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDNhYmY5NjczOWI1NDNhNTNkMmEyODg3MGVhZjJhMDVmNjFmYTBjMTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif-oai","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T12:07:25Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T12:07:25Z"},"message":"Add Guardian review metrics (#24897)\n\n## Why\n\nGuardian reviews already emit analytics events, but we do not expose\naggregate OpenTelemetry metrics for review volume, latency, token usage,\nor terminal outcomes. That makes it harder to monitor Guardian behavior\nduring rollouts and to compare review outcomes by source, action type,\nsession kind, model, and failure mode.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added Guardian review metric names for count, total duration, time to\nfirst token, and token usage in `codex-rs/otel`.\n- Added `core/src/guardian/metrics.rs` to convert\n`GuardianReviewAnalyticsResult` into sanitized metric tags covering\ndecision, terminal status, failure reason, approval request source,\nreviewed action, session kind, risk/outcome, model, reasoning effort,\nand context/truncation state.\n- Emitted the new metrics from `track_guardian_review` for each terminal\nGuardian review result.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Added\n`guardian_review_metrics_record_counts_durations_and_token_usage`, which\nverifies the emitted count, duration, TTFT, token usage histograms, and\ntag set through the in-memory metrics exporter.","tree":{"sha":"9125c979ddba4b4b576579778592c638a925bc29","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/9125c979ddba4b4b576579778592c638a925bc29"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/3abf96739b543a53d2a28870eaf2a05f61fa0c15","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGC/9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAauQQAFlp6yx1xpAL3fYTGnF6408Y\nTOdVN84yZNLQKkI5kZZkJqNDgehtvyynLDlpm9LcoADZcNkspM78N3pBMVufZorv\nPhU+nkUir3WDWy0O1FKcqYzRZbdFmn6aiHl1gcHLCY+L06kaHnjgBRuhc7RN+dmh\nwbW+CluFjqNJmu7BfHkM0T8GTL+Pf9CJebq8GSBxfZ3a7Yd0ANNK/+LBaT0bMTmB\nrgkoQCBPW9Yx3wrIZYHAjRO57AZs/rPXwGanYsU7UvJPoLXKkSynjaOUPwOGvxD5\nfg6AyUtSTG8yOKpzASKgFbqjn3+B2kIgkTkcb9uC7c91495lQFhP0fK2xUSG/txs\nKhen+qH9NJAI4DLHz/Pt+fcuBfAh/LhCduecMxT5rB4F9OlprdLET+MAINoJOZs6\n69ZoH6sqq80HAIJ/OHBgjDdDe8B1LVYBHwGZdWNONBEHsIG//XblY6pzWiFAy3Zk\nGJuAVjL6GFLv49PU3DiG3S5gKkXOhonLNPrf5N8PVoFZOqUrpEuFfYMsdhyR9CrR\naZnJEq6E6rWkIKMrE6YTS26Z8Dnhl1PG20LnBU9Nu9J8579lYjMzyIV/GAeDfTWB\n1VicmttE3deHdqlLQb6NfzhQeDHBmIWNAfuo2dguc1l2iWdH8E5wQaS5wcrQ7W/9\nAUtsG12PQJ/faEdLHVWE\n=qoZg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9125c979ddba4b4b576579778592c638a925bc29\nparent ba6678ca9a3475a59fc4b8124d037deb85c4a78d\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1779970045 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779970045 +0200\n\nAdd Guardian review metrics (#24897)\n\n## Why\n\nGuardian reviews already emit analytics events, but we do not expose\naggregate OpenTelemetry metrics for review volume, latency, token usage,\nor terminal outcomes. That makes it harder to monitor Guardian behavior\nduring rollouts and to compare review outcomes by source, action type,\nsession kind, model, and failure mode.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added Guardian review metric names for count, total duration, time to\nfirst token, and token usage in `codex-rs/otel`.\n- Added `core/src/guardian/metrics.rs` to convert\n`GuardianReviewAnalyticsResult` into sanitized metric tags covering\ndecision, terminal status, failure reason, approval request source,\nreviewed action, session kind, risk/outcome, model, reasoning effort,\nand context/truncation state.\n- Emitted the new metrics from `track_guardian_review` for each terminal\nGuardian review result.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Added\n`guardian_review_metrics_record_counts_durations_and_token_usage`, which\nverifies the emitted count, duration, TTFT, token usage histograms, and\ntag set through the in-memory metrics exporter.","verified_at":"2026-05-28T12:07:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3abf96739b543a53d2a28870eaf2a05f61fa0c15","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3abf96739b543a53d2a28870eaf2a05f61fa0c15","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3abf96739b543a53d2a28870eaf2a05f61fa0c15/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ba6678ca9a3475a59fc4b8124d037deb85c4a78d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ba6678ca9a3475a59fc4b8124d037deb85c4a78d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ba6678ca9a3475a59fc4b8124d037deb85c4a78d"}]},{"sha":"ba6678ca9a3475a59fc4b8124d037deb85c4a78d","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGJhNjY3OGNhOWEzNDc1YTU5ZmM0YjgxMjRkMDM3ZGViODVjNGE3OGQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif-oai","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T12:06:21Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T12:06:21Z"},"message":"Fix memories namespace for Responses API tools (#24898)\n\n## Why\n\nDedicated memories tools are exposed through a Responses API namespace\ntool. The namespace itself has to be a valid tool identifier, so\n`memories/` can fail validation before the model ever gets a chance to\ncall the memory tools.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Changed `MEMORY_TOOLS_NAMESPACE` from `memories/` to `memories`.\n- Added `memory_tool_namespace_matches_responses_api_identifier` so the\nnamespace stays non-empty and limited to Responses-safe identifier\ncharacters.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Added unit coverage for the namespace identifier shape in\n`codex-rs/ext/memories/src/tests.rs`.","tree":{"sha":"6f52c9c2719d1b35cb30d6bea97ed5313af8c5c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6f52c9c2719d1b35cb30d6bea97ed5313af8c5c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/ba6678ca9a3475a59fc4b8124d037deb85c4a78d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGC+9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmOoQAFXoG8ScTEgRf4lE643BYGN7\nYwUpUnaZDbTN5t/GUz9cnAK/BM9kh5f2/qY9UOk4TKP7Gqy+9ZIlcqAkvynUke3F\nSoW2N+EzOmuNGNrabe5VQZr4vYHOSGSnWqiu5KBEnGRrRKtIBz7G8E0VVhdJunTZ\nMTzRPt02uNxuuhrXUTOulisQoeqr3ghCCfYKMScEsbGd56p5D7XHB06bbU39NH2t\nSxC6xK9MWrVdbFPQcmoEqDLnYNPlebS2Xh3PAfQwfbn4x8Bf4yOlgNT8ZzMKn7XS\nPct5R0CxRMKDczja3pkkIBAjeVz88TGB+iGlIFGAv4yOMx7i8z3tKBS9DfIwxI8E\nAl6KlPW2Fv6mk0ulWbGVVSYHEqpWCk5Sazh6VUkKehA4j8XexHv0UDmt4X3r+tI9\nxv3o7eENcIPD9vDap8RWOM5rs6aGnZOJ3netAI0EofyaLW6FEbhHvqTHRuXAoWZ2\ngpPCaEnDZPUhC6rUWvn23ipcBnbEjDsx4cbHlgdU0SdF6JKKuQuOJfAtgKKWdVP8\nxbvxVVro+7oef5QP3cZCuAZcsv/GD6y/lZHm5m1LiW91TfnFQQVC7dmYIsdX11dP\ncgqkoxsp+nAKn/bgmueZn+trhpN/sBz+rTunjnPuxykbnD1rAbHFcI2MTbS7XCor\nj9SDIPt61UNLTj7X+6iu\n=3nIi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6f52c9c2719d1b35cb30d6bea97ed5313af8c5c7\nparent 120edad8edde7ce4af93ae7c3c570ba86d0ac4d3\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1779969981 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779969981 +0200\n\nFix memories namespace for Responses API tools (#24898)\n\n## Why\n\nDedicated memories tools are exposed through a Responses API namespace\ntool. The namespace itself has to be a valid tool identifier, so\n`memories/` can fail validation before the model ever gets a chance to\ncall the memory tools.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Changed `MEMORY_TOOLS_NAMESPACE` from `memories/` to `memories`.\n- Added `memory_tool_namespace_matches_responses_api_identifier` so the\nnamespace stays non-empty and limited to Responses-safe identifier\ncharacters.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Added unit coverage for the namespace identifier shape in\n`codex-rs/ext/memories/src/tests.rs`.","verified_at":"2026-05-28T12:06:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ba6678ca9a3475a59fc4b8124d037deb85c4a78d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ba6678ca9a3475a59fc4b8124d037deb85c4a78d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ba6678ca9a3475a59fc4b8124d037deb85c4a78d/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"120edad8edde7ce4af93ae7c3c570ba86d0ac4d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/120edad8edde7ce4af93ae7c3c570ba86d0ac4d3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/120edad8edde7ce4af93ae7c3c570ba86d0ac4d3"}]},{"sha":"120edad8edde7ce4af93ae7c3c570ba86d0ac4d3","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDEyMGVkYWQ4ZWRkZTdjZTRhZjkzYWU3YzNjNTcwYmE4NmQwYWM0ZDM","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif-oai","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T11:38:48Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T11:38:48Z"},"message":"[codex] Fix Guardian argument comment lint (#24902)\n\n## Summary\n- Add the required `/*parent_thread_id*/` argument comment at the\nGuardian review session test callsite flagged by CI.\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- Not run: clippy/tests, per request; CI will cover them.","tree":{"sha":"015e7ab22c78fec6cf9e17aabc8e0b36e1b251d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/015e7ab22c78fec6cf9e17aabc8e0b36e1b251d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/120edad8edde7ce4af93ae7c3c570ba86d0ac4d3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGClICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAztIQAGHmoXyNzQM+kHTTXmBq/nPH\nJDJO9PuDMrJ3oT6MEOyjFfbsGbJs+ZhbeFGLan2rPVErWdk1dsajcQ9XNV1z4vO9\nPepTZMOlAnGxum2LyjLO/FswFBKEVNe1ou0SZh/emFj+Wh94mEcvgGwHMbt0myK1\nA/AbEqaXWkEg51NW/ds61vgsi1izc6hqQqcaWRh+fG8zxnHEVWs3omOWCcGwfdo2\n+cdeYoIany9x7IGdGesQHxt+fN3INIOLgbiM3usf44cbk1GtkzI2eQxvG0FSgRhL\nDFwodBEAZxgzd4VvzY2ZCHg71BW9ExVlz0itN+egEUL/HkGyfpt/1gEg6XsJpdLp\nb+2HbOEn6BsMU0XqfsjEgj23T6qavGqrCqjAWuClDIIhMEAuSJl3ME5Z6vcr4rp4\nAOcg3QW6RHirWGEFjXtQVl6uz9WnpVCuKIfi7l/JPR3WKT6DTe5+FgJjtLkASlez\nfc6ZV0Gv2ccNG8nYQEAKqHyHXdjUeexDWTTo0+PKokLoSMYeNvfBMLk8uNT+Zzqf\nO9CFWAqT0ornDqgJRc2+sfIoLc8YiONLbZv5vlM/DUdHe08h66ihUw/js+dSAipy\ncw1njZ9zYj7rjuTWoKJtaS9e++72GEdy7UL9FrHhkmPnXNGCYP1SSYVkG8ITKBZ1\n1ttCZqDZ7wzcZZRfnuz3\n=b4Hf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 015e7ab22c78fec6cf9e17aabc8e0b36e1b251d2\nparent 3307240195ece4ef772b45e5323c683f4181f1e5\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1779968328 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779968328 +0200\n\n[codex] Fix Guardian argument comment lint (#24902)\n\n## Summary\n- Add the required `/*parent_thread_id*/` argument comment at the\nGuardian review session test callsite flagged by CI.\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- Not run: clippy/tests, per request; CI will cover them.","verified_at":"2026-05-28T11:38:49Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/120edad8edde7ce4af93ae7c3c570ba86d0ac4d3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/120edad8edde7ce4af93ae7c3c570ba86d0ac4d3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/120edad8edde7ce4af93ae7c3c570ba86d0ac4d3/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3307240195ece4ef772b45e5323c683f4181f1e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3307240195ece4ef772b45e5323c683f4181f1e5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3307240195ece4ef772b45e5323c683f4181f1e5"}]},{"sha":"3307240195ece4ef772b45e5323c683f4181f1e5","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDMzMDcyNDAxOTVlY2U0ZWY3NzJiNDVlNTMyM2M2ODNmNDE4MWYxZTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif-oai","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-05-28T10:55:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T10:55:08Z"},"message":"Use stable Guardian prompt cache keys (#24803)\n\n## Why\n\nGuardian review sessions are reusable across forks when their\n`GuardianReviewSessionReuseKey` is unchanged, but the underlying\nResponses request was still using the child thread ID as\n`prompt_cache_key`. That meant forked Guardian reviews that should share\ncache context produced different cache keys, reducing prompt cache reuse\nand weakening the reuse invariant.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Adds a `ModelClient` prompt cache key override and uses it for\n`ResponsesApiRequest.prompt_cache_key`.\n- Computes Guardian review cache keys as\n`guardian:<sha1(parent_thread_id:reuse_key)>`, scoped to the parent\nthread plus the reuse-sensitive Guardian config.\n- Wires session construction to apply that override only for Guardian\nsub-agent sessions.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Added coverage that Guardian cache keys are stable for the same\nparent/reuse key, change when either the parent thread or reuse key\nchanges, fit within the Responses API length limit, and are absent for\nnon-Guardian sessions.\n- Extended the parallel review test to assert forked Guardian reviews\nsend the same `prompt_cache_key`.","tree":{"sha":"c4ceea8830acb0733eddc00617eb8e98dacd2700","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c4ceea8830acb0733eddc00617eb8e98dacd2700"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/3307240195ece4ef772b45e5323c683f4181f1e5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGB8MCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAd9gQAGR+JpfBqY9MBCP7OHggpVir\nhvg0LcFH7LrMbCllrTtKp/ZsWRHevKxkdRMZvwZB5PZlcQjnKdBiYshVZty0fz8Z\nCoyqS9JpG/GYBztEcha/gLEuSZn5Lv3lLiX99qc5EjkL3EervSi+GO0MZFVXH5+t\nyYV7HOn4xofeQw7DJhc+KeOkbFOU+VAtkhvqQdJYJ4mSUaY7m+GfzRRguNDlWbsh\nWNWKzKy0txLihfZebSSDs5T8AhSvsP2EcGlq9oxExsUYbR2E3371TBFI9xxUa2mT\nU/lY6geklrtXGDFsUzpaMY+wWAAvlIZB46k5sEC4iu2c2DZ3mtmVP62Ku63nQh/H\n51YUbm90pAk39UOkQoFoWOQdPbSsQ6zzya5Tle81zDpjTDjYav8/+SCPO7Ug904a\nY04ZSykD8bU2covnSImaKvcsRgZhQMMJfnJRt+Q3vG4Y51ozL9h+SG8i1Clb7wnH\nQ6ox88DH0cUYDiCJWSdtLn3PJBEKpheFz7s9jrZd2zZaP0J3PnqNGw9+F/LtZ0Rg\nOJX90vVNzc+7hIqHpadPIZC/mJ/zOSjNT9VDbwKnQE3eynPhpbLI3ThdrFwvpDbf\n/usmVk4DcSM+oZcOh9/ZZ+N+cJC23uUazpOdEqzGDCeIv3TqPR/VEHloJ3fhDLmj\nbcfP5EWw4ln1WJx9O5B8\n=DRQf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c4ceea8830acb0733eddc00617eb8e98dacd2700\nparent 4b9eda6ff646938344bdfc718f294c6d0b2c1302\nauthor jif-oai <jif@openai.com> 1779965708 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779965708 +0200\n\nUse stable Guardian prompt cache keys (#24803)\n\n## Why\n\nGuardian review sessions are reusable across forks when their\n`GuardianReviewSessionReuseKey` is unchanged, but the underlying\nResponses request was still using the child thread ID as\n`prompt_cache_key`. That meant forked Guardian reviews that should share\ncache context produced different cache keys, reducing prompt cache reuse\nand weakening the reuse invariant.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Adds a `ModelClient` prompt cache key override and uses it for\n`ResponsesApiRequest.prompt_cache_key`.\n- Computes Guardian review cache keys as\n`guardian:<sha1(parent_thread_id:reuse_key)>`, scoped to the parent\nthread plus the reuse-sensitive Guardian config.\n- Wires session construction to apply that override only for Guardian\nsub-agent sessions.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Added coverage that Guardian cache keys are stable for the same\nparent/reuse key, change when either the parent thread or reuse key\nchanges, fit within the Responses API length limit, and are absent for\nnon-Guardian sessions.\n- Extended the parallel review test to assert forked Guardian reviews\nsend the same `prompt_cache_key`.","verified_at":"2026-05-28T10:55:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3307240195ece4ef772b45e5323c683f4181f1e5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3307240195ece4ef772b45e5323c683f4181f1e5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3307240195ece4ef772b45e5323c683f4181f1e5/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4b9eda6ff646938344bdfc718f294c6d0b2c1302","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4b9eda6ff646938344bdfc718f294c6d0b2c1302","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4b9eda6ff646938344bdfc718f294c6d0b2c1302"}]}]